{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire","id":964939,"title":"All out war : Technocracy against Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-07T07:10:21-07:00","id":964939,"title":"All out war : Technocracy against Vampire","content":"It is war of the extermination. Without mercy, without compassion, without remorse. A dual to the death. Think Total Annihilation.<br /> <br /> 1. Technocracy's object of mission is complete and utter eradication of the Leeches.<br /> <br /> 2. Vampire's object of mission is survival at all cost.<br /> <br /> 3. Maintaining masquerade and kine/sleepers collateral damage is no concern of the both sides.<br /> <br /> 4. Thanks to global shattering of masquerade, Paradox effects are dramatically lessened; now even the most ignorant and skeptical sleepers know and accept existence of the supernatural world. Consequently Void Engineers could operate on Earth with impunity - though they could not bring their (most of) Universal vessels on the earthy sky.<br /> <br /> 5. Both sides will utilize every tool at their disposal and that is not just limited to martial power - money, corporations, control of economy, political clout, social influence, mass media, the internet, sleeper governments, law enforcement agencies, military, and other myriad powers will be fully brought into war.<br /> <br /> 6. Both sides will use and exploit kine/sleepers and earthly assets to the utmost degree. Petty conscience and war crimes are no concern of the combatants; Technocracy will push conscripted sleeper soldiers into meet-grinder that is devastated cities without hesitation, and nuke said cities from orbit or raze it through other methods when absolutely necessary. On the other hand, Vampires will commence mass ghouling/embracing/blood bonding blood cattle with frantic speed.<br /> <br /> 7. Other greater powers, such as Traditions, Mad Ones, Garou and Pentex, will not be involved. Technocracy and Tradition call a truce, while Garou and Pentex are busy killing each other, as always.<br /> <br /> 8. Oracles and Antediluvian will not intervene worldly affairs.<br /> <br /> What do you think will be the outcome of the conflict? How the said conflict will affect mundane and supernatural worlds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:36:44-07:00","id":964951,"title":"","content":"Are we using the Technocracy at its full, MtAS strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:43:12-07:00","id":964953,"title":"","content":"Just because people know that Vampires exist will not mean that Paradox is lessened (proving the existence of aliens would not make Atlantis any more believable), as Vampire are either unaffected by the Consensus or are part of the Consensus. That being said, the primary threats that the Technocracy will face would be from Methuselahs, who have level 8 or 9 powers, and Elders, who have level 6 or 7 powers. When it comes to level versus level, they Technocracy is boned, as their countermagic would only work against Thaumaturgy and Necromancy, not other Disciplines (a treatment of this can be found in the Sorcerer and Sorcerer (Revised) books). An elder with Dominate 6 can turn Technocrats against their own friends while an elder with Obfuscate 7 could walk undetected into the most secure areas. A Methuselah with Potence 8 can literally punch orbital weapons in space and do enough damage to their sensors to make them worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:06:39-07:00","id":964959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964951#post964951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we using the Technocracy at its full, MtAS strength?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is Mage forum. Thus of course it is. At its MtA full glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:22:01-07:00","id":964967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964953#post964953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because people know that Vampires exist will not mean that Paradox is lessened (proving the existence of aliens would not make Atlantis any more believable), as Vampire are either unaffected by the Consensus or are part of the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of OP is that Paradox is lessened, and I'll run with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964953#post964953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, the primary threats that the Technocracy will face would be from Methuselahs, who have level 8 or 9 powers, and Elders, who have level 6 or 7 powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your Methusaleh and raise you Correspondence 4, Forces 4. With this combination, a Mage can literally teleport sunlight into your havens, combine with Matter 1 to see through walls completely. Dimensional Science ensures that no vampires but the few who have Disciplines that interact with the spirit world will be able to do anything to them, and they can literally swarm them in HITMarks and Constructs.<br /> <br /> Lawl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964953#post964953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to level versus level, they Technocracy is boned, as their countermagic would only work against Thaumaturgy and Necromancy, not other Disciplines (a treatment of this can be found in the Sorcerer and Sorcerer (Revised) books).</div> </div> </div> </div>Prove your claim please, I'm not going to spend hours searching through two books for a little, easily missed snippet. Besides, Primium works on everything, and a dude in Exoskeleton will be running around with 8 dice of Primium Countermagic.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like they'll actually NEED Countermagic, given that they can literally stack so many Kinetic Shieldings and Exoskeletons on their agents as they want. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964953#post964953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An elder with Dominate 6 can turn Technocrats against their own friends while an elder with Obfuscate 7 could walk undetected into the most secure areas. A Methuselah with Potence 8 can literally punch orbital weapons in space and do enough damage to their sensors to make them worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your Dominate and raise you Mind and Conditioning, an Elder's gonna do squat against an ATLAS set to murder, Obfuscate won't work on cameras and given that we have an entire Convention that has no problem with replacing their eyes with cameras and their minds with supercomputers, this'll be kind of useless.<br /> <br /> Also Dominate literally fails against mirrorshades, due to requiring eye contact. Guess what Convention is very fond of wearing mirrorshades all the time. <br /> <br /> There are two abilities you could be referring to when you mention Potence 8, one is Fist of Caine which requires Potence 6 and has a range measured in yards which is pathetic, and the other is Flick which has a range of &quot;line of sight&quot;, given that I am unable to see into space when I open my window and look up, it is safe to say that a vampire cannot do so either, furthermore it only does damage like a normal punch and the Technocracy can very well cloak their space stations in layers of Forces shielding, ablative barriers, and indeed hide them with Dimensional Science and laugh at you from another dimension while shooting you from space inside your haven with sunlight beams.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, vampires can operate during the night only and Technocrats can operate during both day and night, and no human tiredness isn't a problem, cybernetics fixed that problem ages ago. Get with the pogrom.<br /> <br /> Your move please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:25:32-07:00","id":964971,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy obliterates the cainite race, then. They already have the capacity to track them from space, and have since 2002. Combine that with a myriad of orbital weaponry platforms, a no-holds-barred policy that permits the use of nuclear weapons which cainites cannot withstand and the job is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:38:28-07:00","id":964981,"title":"","content":"I have my neonates hunt down and transform every Sleeper they find into vampires? Each vampire is capable of siring fifty new vampires per night, which would means that it would take roughly three days to transform the majority of the human species into vampires. Can the Technocracy stop that from happening if the Masquerade fails?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:46:00-07:00","id":964989,"title":"","content":"That depends. Can your neonates outrace statistical modeling and nuclear-armed orbital weapons platforms, anti-Vampire biological agents, artificial sunlight generators, and HIT Mark VI sweep-and-clear units? Making a new vampire every fifteen minutes is going to be extremely obvious - the amount of logistical support they'd require to keep that moving over the course of a single night is remarkable, and visible - so why aren't the Technocracy going to just put a cruise missile through the window and march in some HIT Marks to clean up any survivors? If you overrun the city, why aren't they going to just nuke it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:50:19-07:00","id":964992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964981#post964981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my neonates hunt down and transform every Sleeper they find into vampires? Each vampire is capable of siring fifty new vampires per night, which would means that it would take roughly three days to transform the majority of the human species into vampires. Can the Technocracy stop that from happening if the Masquerade fails?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for removing Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:05:56-07:00","id":964997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964971#post964971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy obliterates the cainite race, then. They already have the capacity to track them from space, and have since 2002. Combine that with a myriad of orbital weaponry platforms, a no-holds-barred policy that permits the use of nuclear weapons which cainites cannot withstand and the job is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the initial conditions (the acceptance of which is another topic entirely), this seems like the outcome. Not even the ultimate outcome. The hard and fast and completely inevitable outcome. Remember all those Extraordinary Citizens swelling the ranks of the Union come into play too. Plus ordinary citizens since now there's a good argument that everyone can use Devices. The Antediluvians might present something of a problem, but, with the &quot;gloves aren't just off, they don't even vaguely exist anymore&quot; preconception, even they wouldn't last too long. After all, the Union has had time (lots of time, thanks to Time compression effects) to fix the problems encountered during Operation Ragnarok. <br /> <br /> Besides, how hard would it be to have several Amalgams of Progenitors coming up with some vaccination against being embraced? Then having the Syndicate market it to EVERYONE in the world so it's as common as air?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:44:19-07:00","id":965010,"title":"","content":"This is a silly question, as the main conflict will come down to the very most powerful members of each side and when you get to those power levels, so much comes down to Storyteller discretion that there can be no objectively right answer.<br /> <br /> I suppose that since vampires are mostly stuck on earth, it might be the best for the Technocracy to just destroy the earth. They could hide out in the Umbra and bombard the earth with massive numbers of nuclear weapons until all life (and thus food sources) for vampires is destroyed if not the vampires themselves. Using their magic to become untouchable is the big advantage of mages, so they need to take advantage of that before any ancient vampires can Dominate mages and thus get access to those mage's powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:49:05-07:00","id":965014,"title":"","content":"It's literally the entire Solar system versus at most something like one million vampires.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has aerial supremacy, naval supremacy, ground supremacy, space supremacy and fucking dimensional supremacy.<br /> <br /> The question is not &quot;can the Technocracy win?&quot;, it's &quot;how many minutes does it take?&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:57:48-07:00","id":965020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=964967#post964967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Word of OP is that Paradox is lessened, and I'll run with that.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">I see your Methusaleh and raise you Correspondence 4, Forces 4. With this combination, a Mage can literally teleport sunlight into your havens, combine with Matter 1 to see through walls completely. Dimensional Science ensures that no vampires but the few who have Disciplines that interact with the spirit world will be able to do anything to them, and they can literally swarm them in HITMarks and Constructs.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Sunlight does 3 damages for turn to a Vampire.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Yeah, it will be pretty bad for a young Vampire,but for an Elder with Fortitude o protean is not.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Enkidu, for example, is gonna absorb those levels with...i don't know...18 dice?<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, what havens?</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Conceal<br /> The vampire may mask an inanimate object up to the size of a house (Obfuscate cannot be used to disguise inanimate objects without the use of this power). If the object is hidden, so are all of its contents. While Conceal is in effect, passersby walk around the concealed object as if it were still visible, but refuse to acknowledge that they are making any kind of detour.<br /> <br /> System: In order to activate this power, a character must be within about 30 feet (approximately 10 meters) of the object to be concealed and the item must<br /> hold some personal significance for him. The Conceal power functions as Unseen Presence for purposes of detection, as well as the duration and durability of the disguise. </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Lawl.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Prove your claim please, I'm not going to spend hours searching through two books for a little, easily missed snippet. Besides, Primium works on everything, and a dude in Exoskeleton will be running around with 8 dice of Primium Countermagic.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">8 dice of primium countermagick is nothing.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">What you don't understand is that Elders have insane dice pool: a &quot;small&quot; Elder&quot; like Hardestadt use 12 dice to dominate you, and he need just one success.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Chances favor him.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Besides, it's not like they'll actually NEED Countermagic, given that they can literally stack so many Kinetic Shieldings and Exoskeletons on their agents as they want.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">You mean the Exoskeleton that any Tremere can break with Technomancy 2?At difficult 5? Only 3 success needed?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022\u2022 Burnout<br /> It is usually easier to destroy than to create, and sensitive electronics are no exception to this rule. Burnout is used to cause a device\u2019s power supply (either internal or external) to surge, damaging or destroying the target. Burnout cannot be used to directly injure another individual, although the sudden destruction of a pacemaker or a car\u2019s fuel injection control chip can<br /> certainly create a health hazard.<br /> <br /> System: A character can use this power at a range of up to 10 times her Willpower in yards or meters, although a +1 difficulty is applied if she is not touching<br /> the target item. The number of successes determines the extent of the damage:<br /> <br /> Successes Result<br /> 1 success Momentary interruption of operation<br /> (one turn), but no permanent<br /> damage.<br /> 2 successes Significant loss of function; +1<br /> difficulty to use using the device for<br /> the rest of the scene.<br /> 3 successes The device breaks and is inoperable<br /> until repaired.<br /> 4 successes Even after repairs, the device\u2019s<br /> capabilities are diminished<br /> (permanent +1 difficulty to use).<br /> 5 successes The equipment is a total write-off;<br /> completely unsalvageable.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Or Thaumaturgy ritual level 2, Machine Blitz</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Machine Blitz<br /> Machines go haywire when this ritual is cast.<b> It takes effect instantly</b> and lasts as long as the vampire concentrates on it. This ritual may be used to kill car engines, erase flash drives, drain the battery of a cellphone, stop life-support machines, et cetera. <b>Essentially, Machine Blitz stops any machine more complex than a rope-and-pulley.</b> The thaumaturge must have a<br /> scrap of rusted metal in her possession for this ritual to work, though some vampires use a variant that requiresa knot steeped in human saliva to be untied.<br /> <br /> System: This ritual only stops machines; it does not grant any control over them. The effects of this ritual are invisible and appear to be coincidental. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">While this also could be nice</span><br /> <br /> Warding Circle versus Technology<br /> (Level Five Thaumaturgy Ritual)<br /> Although they have a great mastery of lore and Kindred physiology, most Inconnu are not modernists. This ritual was designed to protect themselves from recently- Embraced neonates and hunters using technological weapons. This ritual creates a circle of magic centered on the caster, into which technology (i.e. any machine more complex or advanced than a crossbow) cannot pass without shattering or becoming defunct. This circle can be made as large and as permanent as the caster desires, as long as she is willing to pay the necessary price.<br /> <br /> System: The ritual requires three points of mortal blood from individuals with at least an intelligence of 3. The caster determines the size of the warding circle when it is cast; the default radius is 10 feet/3 meters, and every 10-foot/3-meter increase raises the difficulty by one (one additional success is required for every increase past the number necessary to raise the difficulty to 9). The player spends one blood point for every 10 feet/3 meters of radius, and rolls. The ritual takes the normal casting time if it is to be short-term (lasting for the rest<br /> of the night) or one night if it is to be long-term (lasting a year and a day). Once the warding circle is established, it glows a faint coppery-orange, too faint to be seen in normal light, but notable in dim lighting conditions or natural darkness.<br /> A successful Intelligence + Occult roll (difficulty 8) identifies this as a warding circle. If technology crosses into the circle, the possessor of that technology must roll more successes on a Willpower roll (difficulty equal to the caster\u2019s Thaumaturgy rating + 3) than the caster rolled when establishing the ward. <b>Failure indicates that the ward causes all such technology on the individual to be irrevocably destroyed; data cannot be retrieved at a later date, and all parts of the item shatter.</b> If the technology leaves the circle and later enters it again, the possessormust repeat this roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">So good luck with that.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Even more the Kinetic Shieldings do not protect you from Dominate,Presence, and all mystical attack.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">So yea,you will attack the Toreador Elder, and after she'll use presence 3 you will become her thrall.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Besides when the Exoskeleton meet the elder wirth celerity the Exoskeleton is dead.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">You put an exoskeleton against any ancilla good enough in brawl and you'll see it fly.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">I see your Dominate and raise you Mind and Conditioning, an Elder's gonna do squat against an ATLAS set to murder, Obfuscate won't work on cameras and given that we have an entire Convention that has no problem with replacing their eyes with cameras and their minds with supercomputers, this'll be kind of useless.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Nope,nope.nope, i'm sorry cameras instead of eyes will do nothing,to use dominate you don't need real eye to eye contact, you just need that they both can see each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 p152</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many myths and stories exist about a vampire\u2019smystical ability to put people under herspell by looking deeply into her victim\u2019s eyes.The persistence of such stories through theages isn\u2019t surprising, since a number of Kindred Disciplines powers (most notably Dominate) require eye contact in order to work<b>.Other vampires, learning of this requirement,have attempted everything from wearing mirrored sunglasses to gouging out their own eyes in order to prevent an elder from exerting his will upon them.<br /> But Kindred are not so easily thwarted. The need for eye contact stems from the aggressor Kindred\u2019s need to see his victim\u2019s soul, and the eyes are the traditionally known asthe windows to the soul. While the vampire needs to capture his target\u2019s attention, the target\u2019s eyes need not be present for such a power to work</b> (although the arts of theTzimisce make this somewhat challenging at times) \u2014 they only need to find the soul ofhis victim laid bare. </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">So no, i'm sorry: Cameras, mirrorshade...they are gonna be useless, you are in for a mass manipulation trip!<br /> <br /> <br /> And nope nope nope even on the obfuscate part, because even if you have cameras you will not see the Assamite who's standing in front of you.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since Obfuscate clouds the mind of the viewer, vampires can\u2019t use it to hide their presence from electronic or mechanical devices. Video and photo cameras, for example, capture the vampire\u2019s image accurately. <b>Even so, the person using, say, her cell phone to record an Obfuscated vampire will still have her mind impacted by the power, and she won\u2019t see the Kindred\u2019s image until she views the video <u>at a later date</u> (if even then).</b> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">So nope, you are not gonna spot the assamite who's planting the C4 at your feet.<br /> But sure at home, later, when they will be reviewing the error's made in the mission through the camera's footage, the managers will find that the operative was quite stubborn non to shoot the vampire who was standing just in front of him...</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Besides you are not going to use mind on an elder, the difficulty is willpower +5 for influence him or willpower+7 to force him doing something.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">On the other hands you have elders who for dominate use a dicepool between 12 and 18 dices, so, good luck!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Also Dominate literally fails against mirrorshades, due to requiring eye contact. Guess what Convention is very fond of wearing mirrorshades all the time.</span> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as I said above it will be lovely to possess so many thralls in such fashion suit.<br /> They will be the envy of all the other thralls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> furthermore it only does damage like a normal punch and the Technocracy can very well cloak their space stations in layers of Forces shielding, ablative barriers, and indeed hide them with Dimensional Science and laugh at you from another dimension while shooting you from space inside your haven with sunlight beams. </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is all useless against Auspex.<br /> <br /> And no, Sunrise is not gonna shine in Vampire havens.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy ritual level 1, every neonate can learn it.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defense of the Sacred Haven<br /> This ritual prevents sunlight from entering an area within 20 feet (six meters) of this ritual\u2019s casting. A mystical darkness blankets the area, keeping the baleful light at bay. Sunlight reflects off windows or magically fails to pass through doors or other portals. To invoke this ritual\u2019s protection, the caster draws sigils in her own blood on all the affected windows and doors.<br /> The ritual lasts as long as the thaumaturge stays within the 20-foot (6-meter) radius.<br /> <br /> System: This ritual requires one hour to perform,<br /> during which the caster recites incantations and inscribes<br /> glyphs. One blood point is required for this<br /> ritual to work. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Your move please?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Dominate you all and make slaves out of you, kill you while you can't see us?<br /> <br /> Is still your move, since nothing you mentioned is gonna work: You can't summon the sun in their heavens, you can't resist their mental discipline,you can't see them and you can't create an anti-embrace vaccine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore I offer this challenge: Ventrue Methuselah sleeping in his grave in Italy use Dominate 8 against any technocrat in the world</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This refinement of Obedience (though the character need not have learned Obedience first) allows the use of Dominate on any subject that the vampire is familiar with, <b>at any time, over any distance. </b>If the elder knows where his target is, he may issue commands as if he were standing face- to-face with his intended victim.<br /> <br /> <br /> System: The player spends a Willpower point and rolls Perception + Empathy (difficulty equal to the subject\u2019s Wits + Stealth) to establish contact. If this roll succeeds, Dominate may be used as if the character had established eye contact with the target. A second Willpower point must be spent in order for a vampire to use this power on another vampire or other supernatural being. </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">So he can dominate you from any distance, and you do not even know where the bloody-monster is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">&quot;Paul? Paul? Are you acting strange today? Paul...why are disabling the base security system...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Besides there is a fallacy in the OP: The Antideluvian WILL intervene, it's a matter of fact, if you start killing many vampire the Ancient ones will rise.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:11:19-07:00","id":965028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965014#post965014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's literally the entire Solar system versus at most something like one million vampires.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has aerial supremacy, naval supremacy, ground supremacy, space supremacy and fucking dimensional supremacy.<br /> <br /> The question is not &quot;can the Technocracy win?&quot;, it's &quot;how many minutes does it take?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nonsense.<br /> There are 3000-4000 Technocrats in the world and just 800 Hit-Mark, against a possibly infinite number of vampires,they simply do not have the forces to keep the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The best thing for them would be hide in their space fortress, hoping the Ventrue and Lasombra Methuselah do not make them fall using Dominate 8 or the Inner Council wipe them out from the sky with Thaumaturgy 9.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the lasombra could just replicate the Chorazin's destruction: After they discover where you are with Auspex they use Abyss Mysticism ritual and the space stations are destroyed by the tsunami of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Ur-Shulgi will use some ancient and forgotten ritual to make them fall...<br /> <br /> <br /> There are a LOT of way to take down those birds.<br /> <br /> Another way? Montano enters the Abyss, and emerge in the Space Stations (if there is a shadow in there, then Montano can use it as a door), then Domination party.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And no, there is no anti-embrace vaccine, as Blood Treachery says no mage can roll more dices than God: Vampirism is a curse from God, and you are not gonna beat God.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:15:20-07:00","id":965032,"title":"","content":"Which of those counters the nuclear weapons, without relying on a suitable methuselah magically having met the technocrats manning the weapon platforms or the mages failing to employ rudimentary countermagic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:34:58-07:00","id":965050,"title":"","content":"Oh. One of these threads.<br /> <br /> Let me help you folks out real quick:<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage Game - The Technocracy Wins<br /> Vampire Game - The Vampires Win<br /> Neutral CWoD Game - There is no such thing, it's horrible for neutral crossovers, and the existing Crossover rules don't help and usually are biased towards one or the other gameline. If they are not, the fans of one particular gameline or another will make them biased.<br /> <br /> There you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:39:39-07:00","id":965053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire#post964939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. Thanks to global shattering of masquerade, Paradox effects are dramatically lessened; now even the most ignorant and skeptical sleepers know and accept existence of the supernatural world. Consequently Void Engineers could operate on Earth with impunity - though they could not bring their (most of) Universal vessels on the earthy sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make that a prerequisite than you might as well have the Mages win by fiat. <br /> <br /> All you're doing here is setting up a mean spirited power fantasy where you talk about how much you would totally shit all over another game line for the lulz. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:44:08-07:00","id":965059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965032#post965032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of those counters the nuclear weapons</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy? Chimestry 9 to make them stop mid air or revert? Dominating the army generals to destroy the missiles while they are on flight?<br /> <br /> Stopping a missile is not a difficult thing if you have the right means you know?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-ballistic_missile\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/OBV_GBI_1.jpg/960px-OBV_GBI_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-ballistic_missile\" target=\"_blank\"> Anti-ballistic missile - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-ballistic_missile\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-ballistic_missile </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If we have decided that this is an all-out war than I don't see why the Elder should not dominate the army top brass.<br /> Dominate, blood bond and presence on the top brass around the world, and your Nuclear missiles will never reach the ground.<br /> <br /> And you can't stop them because, ehi, you know... Dominate 8,Dominate 5, Presence 4 and so on...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> without relying on a suitable methuselah magically having met the technocrats manning the weapon platforms </div> </div> </div>It's not my fault if Meth are plot devices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or the mages failing to employ rudimentary countermagic? </div> </div> </div>Countermagick against what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:45:06-07:00","id":965061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965020#post965020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides there is a fallacy in the OP: The Antideluvian WILL intervene, it's a matter of fact, if you start killing many vampire the Ancient ones will rise.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want me to involve &quot;can toss around realms and crush the earth between his fingers with no Paradox&quot; Archmasters? Or &quot;I am the mind of the entire universe&quot; Archmasters perhaps? This is not a feasible plan. Forces 5 can destroy cities, involving beings that toss around realms like children's toys is not a good approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:45:52-07:00","id":965063,"title":"","content":"Countermagic against their disciplines. Countermagic is, as of M20, effective against supernatural disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:55:41-07:00","id":965070,"title":"","content":"There is of course also the slight problem in how vampires would get into a space station beyond the Spatial Horizon of course. With an effect something like this set up:<br /> <br /> &quot;Correspondence 3, Entropy 4&quot;<br /> &quot;Haemophagic Counter-Intrusion Grid&quot;<br /> &quot;Any vampire that enters the range of this grid takes 20 points of aggravated damage every turn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:55:44-07:00","id":965071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965061#post965061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you want me to involve &quot;can toss around realms and crush the earth between his fingers with no Paradox&quot; Archmasters? Or &quot;I am the mind of the entire universe&quot; Archmasters perhaps? This is not a feasible plan. Forces 5 can destroy cities, involving beings that toss around realms like children's toys is not a good approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you sweet!<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is immortal, Ennoia is the whole planet,Lasombra is Darkness,Tremere can dominate the whole human race,Brujah exist outside time,Absimiliard che hide entire nations,Malkav is a force field of madness that can hit anyone anywhere,Toreador knows eveything that will ever happen.<br /> <br /> And they can do all of this in one turn at the expense of one blood point.<br /> <br /> How much time do you need to perform a level 7 mind ritual and how many success do you need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:57:43-07:00","id":965074,"title":"","content":"Of course, the antediluvians and the oracles are staying out of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:59:34-07:00","id":965076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965063#post965063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Countermagic against their disciplines. Countermagic is, as of M20, effective against supernatural disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry, you don't have enough dices.<br /> <br /> How much arete does it have a normal mage? 3? 4? Come on, let's say six (unlikely, but ehy, let's help them).<br /> <br /> So you have 3/4/6 dice to counter (at difficulty 7) a Ventrue starting character that can easily have 10 dice to dominate you at you current willpower rating, and he just need one success.<br /> <br /> (and there are no mage that starts with arete 4 or 6 eh, I'm generous).<br /> <br /> Who has the better chances?<br /> <br /> And I took a ventrue that can be a neonate eh,not an Ancilla, not Elder, not a Methuselah,a character that can be created directly as a fledgling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:07:29-07:00","id":965083,"title":"","content":"Sure, let's say 6. But that six comes <i>after</i> the willpower contest, where any roll of six or higher subtracts dice from their attempt. Not to mention you can dominate all the army commanders you want - you're still in trouble when the orbital platforms start firing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:10:03-07:00","id":965088,"title":"","content":"Like others have said, the Technocracy would win, mostly due to the rules OP defined.<ul><li>Paradox is the main limiting factor for Mage in general - removing it basically makes Mages unstoppable.</li> <li>Removing Antediluvians is much more painful for vampires than removing Oracles is for mages. The power of the Technocracy isn't in Tychoides personally but in the organization he created. There is a hell of a lot of power in, say, [Tzimisce] that is not within all of his childer.</li> <li>Vampires are a fundamentally social (whereas mages are mental and werewolves are physical, in the original triad). They rely on subtlety and pressure, not on open war. Their innate powers, like blood bonds, are built around influence rather than, say, a werewolf's Crinos form being good for pureeing foes.</li> </ul>There are lots of cool Methuselah powers they could use but most vampires have levels of those powers that only allow minor contamination (Dominating one general, using Lure of Flames on a couple black helicopters). The high-level Disciplines that really threaten the Technocracy are only held by a couple elders, so you only get a couple shots at them. You can Embrace armies in a night, but they're just cannon fodder; nobody's getting Embraced and then throwing around Chimerstry 9.<br /> <br /> The best part of this war would actually be chasing down the holdouts in the city of Enoch in the Shadowlands. We're already going gonzo, why not refit a fleet of voidships for combat with post-life entities and go strafing?<br /> <br /> In a more balanced scenario - if the Technocracy slowly begins considering Cainites as a threat worthy of their attention, and vampires slowly start trying to gain influence/minions in the Technocracy, and this cold war boils over into a hot war - that is <b><i>much</i></b> more interesting and even if you keep the Antediluvians out, could still easily be a vampire victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:12:21-07:00","id":965090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965071#post965071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh you sweet!</div> </div> </div> </div>Your condescension is not appreciated. I am very well aware of what was written in Gehenna, I have after all been playing this game since Vampire 1e.<br /> <br /> I literally have every book, not that it is relevant to this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965071#post965071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce is immortal, Ennoia is the whole planet,Lasombra is Darkness,Tremere can dominate the whole human race,Brujah exist outside time,Absimiliard che hide entire nations,Malkav is a force field of madness that can hit anyone anywhere,Toreador knows eveything that will happen ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to a single scenario in Gehenna, yes.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't matter because there are no Antediluvians or Archmasters.<br /> <br /> Also Tremere requires a lengthy ritual, that he fucks up and fails in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965071#post965071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they can do all of this in one turn at the expense of one blood point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, they still aren't in this scenario, while the Mages who can destroy New York with a single Effect from space in another dimension behind layers of shielding and anti-vampire technology are in this scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965071#post965071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much time do you need to perform a level 7 mind ritual and how many success do you need?</div> </div> </div> </div>A few turns, and any amount of successes you feel like, according to an optional rule you can only have up to (Willpower * Arete), but since that's optional you can theoretically stack as high as you feel like.<br /> <br /> Mage is after all 