r /> -- Sergio the Pious, Sabbat Bishop. Dead by sunlight, committed suicide after reading this thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:53:10-07:00","id":965144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965138#post965138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why we can't? There is published material that makes rules for it, and even more there is lore that justifies it.<br /> Published material tell us you can create new rituals and path? Gives you even rules for it and gives you a lore background for make it work? They you can use it.<br /> And it's not even a secondary book,since it's the main book that explains how the conversion from mage to vampire works.<br /> <br /> Besides as I said there is plenty of lore about it, the New Thaumaturgic paths the Anarchs created that you can find in Rites of Blood, the history of Mary St.Johns in New York by nights, it's lore, and, even morte, it'supported by a rule system.<br /> <br /> And it has always been so with Thaumaturgy, there is a reason there are few rituals for high level of Hermetic Thauma,Abyss Mysticism,Koldun and so on,because basically at the higher level Blood magic starts working much like the true magic, this is way Velya has devised from zero a ritual to unbind the Tzimisce, that's why the Council of Nine was able to curse the assamites, that's why Baba could rise the Gauntlet, this is why Kemintiri has a unique ritual for her, this is way Menele was able to unleash the fury of the Vesuvius on Pompei, because from level six Blood Magic can be modeled to do what you need to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if we do so, we enter an unknown.<br /> <br /> This unknown is the ability to spontaneously generate new rituals and paths as you want to, this is stupid because it means I don't get to debate against Tremere, I get to debate against a Clan Tremere that spontaneously has a ritual to counter everything Mages can do, ever even though there is no reason they should have such a ritual, nor a reason that they would ever think of it.<br /> <br /> Why would they have a ritual that allows them to d what you describe anyways? I don't believe Tremere has ever encountered the Void Engineers before, so that they should have a ritual that coincidentally and perfectly solve their problems is fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> If you get to randomly create rituals that are specialized to do a specific thing that there is no reason that they would ever invent, this is not a debate anymore, it is a session of oral cybersex with the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:53:47-07:00","id":965147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965142#post965142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Win what? we have already lost. We do not fight a war to win, we fight for Redemption.<br /> Technocracy or not, Redemption sits in God's hands.<br /> Given to us, we are saved.<br /> Denied from us, we remain damned. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Now that's out of the way. I must return to my duties</i><br /> <br /> -- Sergio the Pious, Sabbat Bishop. Dead by sunlight, committed suicide after reading this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wise man, I should follow suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:58:24-07:00","id":965149,"title":"","content":"If the Technocracy is already resorting to wide scale use of nuclear weapons against civilian targets, they have already failed. Remember, the goal of the Technocracy is Mass Awakening, so they are not going to use nuclear weapons against civilian targets. As for 'new' rituals against nuclear weapons, nuclear weapons have been a threat to vampires for seventy years. You do not think that the Tremere have developed dozens (or hundreds) of rituals that can protect against nuclear weapons? Heck, I would not be surprised if they have developed and performed rituals that hinder uncontrolled fission reactions within fifty miles of every major city in the world with a Tremere chantry, which would make any nuclear weapon into a much less effective radiological weapon, just in case the mortals got too stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:03:43-07:00","id":965159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965149#post965149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Technocracy is already resorting to wide scale use of nuclear weapons against civilian targets, they have already failed. Remember, the goal of the Technocracy is Mass Awakening, so they are not going to use nuclear weapons against civilian targets. As for 'new' rituals against nuclear weapons, nuclear weapons have been a threat to vampires for seventy years. You do not think that the Tremere have developed dozens (or hundreds) of rituals that can protect against nuclear weapons? Heck, I would not be surprised if they have developed and performed rituals that hinder uncontrolled fission reactions within fifty miles of every major city in the world with a Tremere chantry, which would make any nuclear weapon into a much less effective radiological weapon, just in case the mortals got too stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A): <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire#post964939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Both sides will utilize every tool at their disposal and that is not just limited to martial power - money, corporations, control of economy, political clout, social influence, mass media, the internet, sleeper governments, law enforcement agencies, military, and other myriad powers will be fully brought into war.<br /> <br /> 6. Both sides will use and exploit kine/sleepers and earthly assets to the utmost degree. Petty conscience and war crimes are no concern of the combatants; Technocracy will push conscripted sleeper soldiers into meet-grinder that is devastated cities without hesitation, and nuke said cities from orbit or raze it through other methods when absolutely necessary. On the other hand, Vampires will commence mass ghouling/embracing/blood bonding blood cattle with frantic speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>B: If you guys get to invent your own special snowflake rituals to do exactly what you want them to. I'm leaving this thread.<br /> <br /> Let me guess? They also have a ritual to protect against a laser fired through Dimensional Science? And a ritual that allows them to identify Technocrats on sight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:08:42-07:00","id":965169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965149#post965149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Technocracy is already resorting to wide scale use of nuclear weapons against civilian targets, they have already failed. Remember, the goal of the Technocracy is Mass Awakening, so they are not going to use nuclear weapons against civilian targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a thread where the OP ignores the Masquerade in Vampire and Ascension in Mage. its supposed to be stupid. I say we move onto extramdientional beings labotomized and cybernetically enhanced piloted by psychologically scared 14 yearolds fighting the Cathedral of Flesh.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:09:10-07:00","id":965170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965169#post965169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its a thread where the OP ignores the Masquerade in Vampire and Ascension in Mage. its supposed to be stupid. I say we move onto extramdientional beings labotomized and cybernetically enhanced piloted by psychologically scared 14 yearolds fighting the Cathedral of Flesh.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure why the fuck not? I'll write some stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:10:44-07:00","id":965171,"title":"","content":"Do you remember the fear that came with being part of the Cold War? Even if you do not, vampires do not forget as easily as human beings. Nuclear weapons are a 'real' threat, even nowadays, while interdimensional lasers are not a 'real' threat.<br /> <br /> Could a ritual identify Technocrats? No, probably not. Could a ritual find and identify Awakened Avatars? That would be much easier. Remember, the elder Tremere were Mages, they understand Avatars. They might even have rituals that duplicate Gilgul. Could you imagine a ritual that would commit Gilgul against a targeted Awakened Avatar from a distance? Can you imagine what would happen to your space station when the Avatars of the Mages start to be destroyed one-by-one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:17:40-07:00","id":965175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965171#post965171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember the fear that came with being part of the Cold War? Even if you do not, vampires do not forget as easily as human beings. Nuclear weapons are a 'real' threat, even nowadays, while interdimensional lasers are not a 'real' threat.<br /> <br /> Could a ritual identify Technocrats? No, probably not. Could a ritual find and identify Awakened Avatars? That would be much easier. Remember, the elder Tremere were Mages, they understand Avatars. They might even have rituals that duplicate Gilgul. Could you imagine a ritual that would commit Gilgul against a targeted Awakened Avatar from a distance? Can you imagine what would happen to your space station when the Avatars of the Mages start to be destroyed one-by-one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? Gigul is explicitly something developed POST council of nine. It may even be completely unknown to the Technocracy. There's all sorts of developments that a unfiied theory of magic as developed via the council of 9 improved of the holes in many paradigms that previously existed. The Tremere lack a lot of the development that Mage society in general picked up since they split off with it. At best their founders were talking about Foundations and Pillars.. more likely many of them were talking about Paths.(Thaum looks ALOT more like sorcery than anything based on Pillars/sphere/nounverb)<br /> <br /> On the other hand they do have a ritual for destroying avatars, its called &quot;The Embrace&quot; but its not Tremere specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:19:27-07:00","id":965176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965171#post965171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember the fear that came with being part of the Cold War? Even if you do not, vampires do not forget as easily as human beings. Nuclear weapons are a 'real' threat, even nowadays, while interdimensional lasers are not a 'real' threat.<br /> <br /> Could a ritual identify Technocrats? No, probably not. Could a ritual find and identify Awakened Avatars? That would be much easier. Remember, the elder Tremere were Mages, they understand Avatars. They might even have rituals that duplicate Gilgul. Could you imagine a ritual that would commit Gilgul against a targeted Awakened Avatar from a distance? Can you imagine what would happen to your space station when the Avatars of the Mages start to be destroyed one-by-one?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is neato but ignores the Technocrats completely.<br /> <br /> These are the Technocracy at their absolute maximum power, they can literally drown the world in HITMarks if they feel like it, they have the entire solar system behind them, and innumerable off-world colonies that the Tremere cannot do shit about.<br /> <br /> Why do you constantly ignore the fact that the Technocrats can also murder them sympathetically, even if they have to eat the world with grey goo nanomachines.<br /> <br /> And I do indeed remember the Cold War, in fact as a person who lived through that shit, on the Russian side I remember that there was a mutual fear, not simply one side dominating everything.<br /> <br /> I see no issue in a world where neither the Technocracy or the Tremere dare attack each other for fear of retaliation and because they need the resources because that's the default setting in Revised.<br /> <br /> I have issue with this setting that wanks Tremere to be \u00fcbermensch gods of magic that are better mages than the conspiracy of mages that <b>invented</b> modernity and drove them from humanity with fire and flame as the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> The Tremere should fear the retribution of lasers and missiles and HITMarks and ATLAS units, just like the Technocracy should be afraid of the cold and clammy touch of the embrace, and the infinite sorrow as his Genius is flensed to shreds by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:20:10-07:00","id":965177,"title":"","content":"Also: It's implied that Tremere was a Sorcerer and not a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:25:27-07:00","id":965179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965144#post965144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because if we do so, we enter an unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it was the whole premise of the thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Technocracy's object of mission is complete and utter eradication of the Leeches.<br /> <br /> 2. Vampire's object of mission is survival at all cost.<br /> <br /> 5. Both sides will utilize every tool at their disposal and that is not just limited to martial power </div> </div> </div><br /> So yeah, if these are the premises than we must assume that the blood mages will use every tool they have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This unknown is the ability to spontaneously generate new rituals and paths as you want to, this is stupid because it means I don't get to debate against Tremere, I get to debate against a Clan Tremere that spontaneously has a ritual to counter everything Mages can do, ever even though there is no reason they should have such a ritual, nor a reason that they would ever think of it. </div> </div> </div>And still the rules make it so, there is a whole chapter in V20 rites of blood that helps you build new rituals, and if you read the description of their ritual you'll find that most of them have been created in time of war to resolve a specific need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wary Tremere created this ritual to protect themselves<br /> from the minions of vengeful rivals. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Developed during Clan Tremere\u2019s troubled inception,<br /> Burning Blade allows a caster to temporarily enchant<br /> a melee weapon to inflict unhealable wounds on<br /> supernatural creatures. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This ancient ritual is said to have been one of the<br /> first developed by the Tremere and a primary reason<br /> for the lack of cohesive opposition to their expansion. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although they have a great mastery of lore and Kindred<br /> physiology, most Inconnu are not modernists. This<br /> ritual was designed to protect themselves from recently-<br /> Embraced neonates and hunters using technological<br /> weapons. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would they have a ritual that allows them to d what you describe anyways? I don't believe Tremere has ever encountered the Void Engineers before, so that they should have a ritual that coincidentally and perfectly solve their problems is fucking stupid. </div> </div> </div><br /> The Tremere,but more in the general the elders, are full aware of the existence of technocracy.<br /> Grimgroth surely knows the order of reason, and be sure that he has keept an eye on the Mage world.<br /> <br /> Even Tremere knows of them, don't you remember his ending monologue in Blood Treachery?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I am old and tired, and perhaps it will come to pass<br /> one day soon that Fate cuts down the monster it has<br /> made. However, until such a day, I have my own<br /> responsibilities. So hear me, Gilmore - - press this matter<br /> at your own risk. For there are worse fates than death,<br /> <b>and better enemies to fight... are there not</b>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even Vitel and Villon knows it, remember that at the end of Thin Blood the Princes gathers to discuss Bangladesh, and they are fully aware of what really happened.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat will know about Technocracy through Zettler work for Pentex,and Pentex is infiltrating the SPD division of the Syndicate, so even here we have vampire who knows what's happening, so if we have decided that is gonna be an all-out war for survival you can be sure that Zettler will be happy to explain a lot of things to the other kindreds.<br /> <br /> Even more: it's simply the evolution of Thaumaturgy, it's the whole point of Rites of Blood, Thaumaturgy is evolving to new forms, modern forms, technological forms,Thaumaturgy is no more bound to an hermetic paradigm, it has evolved from that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, there is no need for them to already have the right ritual (while they probably have it, because since the destruction of the Anti-clans Tremere and the Inner Council are working on mighty rituals to kill the antideluvians and win Ghenna, so Nuclear Warfare is far beneath what they are already developing) they can simply create it out of need.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I don't see the point: there is plenty of common thaumaturges who are developing Techno-Thaumaturgy, and most of them are youngster, so why should it be a problem for the real masters of blood magic to adapt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:30:30-07:00","id":965183,"title":"","content":"Fuck this shit I'm out.<br /> <br /> Let us just say that I disagree heavily.<br /> <br /> Also: Blood Treachery is fucking shit, and requires that the Hermetics act like idiots instead of Mages. That encounter with Tremere should have ended with &quot;lol Correspondence 3, Forces 6, Spirit 5, you're dead, your soul is dead and every iteration of you is dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:36:17-07:00","id":965188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965183#post965183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck this shit I'm out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: Blood Treachery is fucking shit, and requires that the Hermetics act like idiots instead of Mages. That encounter with Tremere should have ended with &quot;lol Correspondence 3, Forces 6, Spirit 5, you're dead, your soul is dead and every iteration of you is dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol, Tremere spends one blood point and Dominate the entire room, or make it explode with Thauma 10.<br /> <br /> The moment Tremere entered the room the fight was over.<br /> <br /> Besides, again, how many turns to cast a Correspondence 3, Force 6,Spirit 5 effect that must destroy an Immortal soul?<br /> <br /> Mmmh...vulgare,without witness, base difficult 10.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they were going to pull it.<br /> <br /> Considering that for sure a 1300 years old Vampire has a bit more dexterity and wits that makes him start first?<br /> <br /> Besides sorry but who was going to cast it? I don't remember many archmages on earth after the reckoning.<br /> <br /> But again, what are we talking about? Dominate 10 and you are already in the room, the game is over.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:36:38-07:00","id":965189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965179#post965179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't see the point: there is plenty of common thaumaturges who are developing Techno-Thaumaturgy, and most of them are youngster, so why should it be a problem for the real masters of blood magic to adapt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the premise of the war of ages is that one of the few advantages that the younger generations have is adaptation? Its what scares the Elders that the young have this concept they've never heard of and use it to murder them. But this whole thread ignores basic premises of both games. Lets let Blood mages invent rituals on a fly rather than over years of time. Lets have them instant cast. Lets have the technocracy throw infinite resources at crazy scifi shit like like attacking God with a Deathstar!<br /> <br /> Or the now infinitely resourced Technocracy wakes up Autocththon who goes all Unicron on Earth and shits out all the vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:40:36-07:00","id":965190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965188#post965188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lol, Tremere spends one blood point and Dominate the entire room, or make it explode with Thauma 10.<br /> <br /> The moment Tremere entered the room the fight was over.<br /> <br /> Besides, again, how many turns to cast a Correspondence 3, Force 6,Spirit 5 effect that must destroy an Immortal soul?<br /> <br /> Considering that for sure a 1300 years old Vampire has a bit more dexterity and wits that makes him start first?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is in fact, not mature to respond to a person who has declared himself out of the debate, which is why I attempted to say &quot;I disagree heavily&quot;. But if you insist on doing this, I will bite though I honestly suspect that you are trolling.<br /> <br /> It takes as many turns as the Archmaster wants to given that he has an infinite amount of turns from Time 3. Tremere is only supreme in a vampire game, and in a Mage game he'll get stomped by an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy <b>has</b> killed an Antediluvian before, and it can do so again.<br /> <br /> So, now I implore you: I don't want to continue this debate because it makes me angry, and I don't like being angry, I disagree with you and would honestly like to leave it there. So can we fucking end this pain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:41:22-07:00","id":965192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965099#post965099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Versus debates are only funny when you aren't unlucky enough to take part in them. :C</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to enjoy my sanity, while it lasts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:52:54-07:00","id":965202,"title":"","content":"And if you'll excuse me, I'll go and do something actually productive such as writing some more of my totally not Ghost In The Shell Demon: The Descent chronicle.<br /> <br /> But the real ultimate deal here is that vampires in vampire are the secret masters of the world and Mages are nothing but mortals grasping blindly for power that isn't theirs, just like vampires in a Mage game are nothing but pathetic leeches shackled to the rules of the Consensus and unable to truly influence reality.<br /> <br /> I have engaged in this debate because it was entertaining in the beginning, but since it has become a bore now I'll draw and let you decide whether the Technocracy or the vampires would win, it's not like your ideas of the setting is going to change my setting where the Technocracy has handily destroyed the Sabbat and is busy with the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:00:53-07:00","id":965206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965190#post965190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is in fact, not mature to respond to a person who has declared himself out of the debate, which is why I attempted to say &quot;I disagree heavily&quot;. But if you insist on doing this, I will bite though I honestly suspect that you are trolling.<br /> <br /> <br /> It takes as many turns as the Archmaster wants to given that he has an infinite amount of turns from Time 3. Tremere is only supreme in a vampire game, and in a Mage game he'll get stomped by an Archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not understand, clearly.<br /> <br /> First of all you can't use extra turns with time 3 to cast an effect, sorry, that's not gonna happening, extra actions you get with Time 3 can only be used for physical actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> M20 page 528<br /> <br /> &quot;How Many Effects Can I Use at Once?<br /> A mage can cast o<b>nly one Effect per turn, even if she\u2019s using<br /> Time 3 magick to speed up her activities</b>. She may, however,<br /> keep any number of Effects running at a time, although it<br /> becomes more and more difficult for her to do so.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, the point you are missing is that in the moment Tremere teleported himself in the council room the game was over.<br /> To cast that effect you'd need several turns, and you can't use time 3 to help you, you are going to do an extended roll.<br /> <br /> And Tremere will kill you all in one turn,you simply do not have the time to cast it, because even if all those mages in the council room started fast-casting at Tremere trying to take him down they were doomed, because Tremere needs one action with Dominate 10, nothing more,<br /> <br /> Remember?<br /> <br /> &quot;The assembled magi stand, stunned. One FLAMBEAU<br /> rushes toward the ANCIENT. <b>The mask turns to<br /> face the FLAMBEAU, and the FLAMBEAU is frozen</b> in<br /> place. No one else dares to move.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;ANCIENT: <b>Come here.<br /> Irresistibly compelled, KURTZWEIL obeys and falls<br /> to his knees.</b><br /> GILMORE: What are you\u2014<br /> ANCIENT: You have something that belongs to us,<br /> don't you, Mr. Kurtzweil?<br /> KURTZWEIL: Please... don't...<br /> ANCIENT: Acquired a taste, have we?<br /> The ANCIENT gestures idly, and KURTZWEIL<br /> freezes in place. The red streaks in KURTZWEIL's mask<br /> turn bone-white all of a sudden, and the mage collapses,<br /> sobbing&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't simply resist a being that has dominate 10, not if you are in the same room with him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, he has 10 dice of inherent countermagick,the same ammount the Unnamed has,so good luck.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy <b>has</b> killed an Antediluvian before, and it can do so again. </div> </div> </div>No, I'm sorry, they kiiled an Antedeluvian who was just freshly awaken in frenzy, distracted by 3 Bodhisattva and an horde of wraiths.<br /> <br /> In a direct confrontation you cannot kill Ravnos with these means; you nuke him? Ok, Chimestry 10, fire becomes mices. You point the sun to him? The sky becomes solid and black.<br /> Technocracy killed a frenzied Ante, surrounded by Bodhi and wraiths,<br /> And even more, one of the Ante who had not ascended like his peers.*<br /> <br /> You can't kill Tzimisce, he is just immortal, you can't kill Ennoia, because she's planet Earth, you can't kill Lasombra because you can't Kill the Abyss.<br /> <br /> It's the whole point of Ghenna, to make them killable they had to rely on the whole whitering thing.<br /> <br /> Nothing short of an Oracle is gonna beat an Ante**.<br /> And even there, if we have to rely on the stats of the Unnamed, the outcome is not given.<br /> <br /> <br /> *And this only if we do not accept the whole &quot;Ravnos is Ravana and he tricked us all&quot;<br /> <br /> **Or a incredibly powerful Archmage who has a good plan, like Voormas with Touh Mouh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, now I implore you: I don't want to continue this debate because it makes me angry, and I don't like being angry, I disagree with you and would honestly like to leave it there. So can we fucking end this pain? </div> </div> </div>It's not my fault if you choose to ignore the rules and the lore.<br /> It's childish, it's like fleeing because someone made you notice that no, rules and lore permits other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> You started this by ignoring and dismissing the fact that at the higher level blood magic works like true magic,and you are complaining because there are rules and lore for this on canon published material.<br /> So stop complaining, it's childish.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm sorry, the elder thaumaturges can devise any ritual they need,and create any effect they desires, it's the whole point of House of Tremere,Rites of Blood and so on,giving rules that make Blood Magic an open discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> You simply entered because there was a chance to go &quot;YEEAAA THE MIGHTY METAL DRAGON POWER, TECHNOCRACY PLOWS ALL THE DEVIANTS&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then I made you notice that no,It's not that simple because plot devices and open-power are not something reserved to mages.<br /> And now you are diserting the thread because the toy was broken,poor thing, forgive me if I show little emphaty on this matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the whole &quot;Buuuu! Blood treachery sucks! Vampires can't win in a Mage book!&quot; is ridiculous, it's like those who whimper because in the Battle Royal of Plot Devices Ravnos got fried, yeah, shit happens, 3 virtual Arhat, an horde of wraith from Yomi Wan, Werewolves, Code Ragnarock, it got fried, and so what? It's lore consistent so I don't see the problem.<br /> <br /> (Well maybe I can see the problem, the whole thing created the mage hyubris &quot;Technocracy can kill everything&quot; and you seem quite an example of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:01:43-07:00","id":965210,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy takes a handful of sleepers to a secret training facility for a few months. Where enlightened kung-fu masters and sports coaches put them through the physical training gauntlet like has never been seen before. When they emerge, they can crush cars with their face. Slay even the mightiest of monsters with a single punch. And worship their technocratic masters as gods, ignoring any and all loyalties other than those masters.<br /> <br /> (Stack a Better Body effect with a Hands of Death effect with however many ludicrous levels of successes you feel like stacking, after conditioning the subjects to conditioning level 10. Then give them Primium gauntlets. So now they have a strength/dex of whatever. They do 10 Bajillion dice of damage with every punch. And they can tear through spells with their gauntlets. You can't brainwash them as by conditioning level 10, you will betray anyone and anything for the Technocracy. They can literally dictate who you love and you will obey without a second thought. There's no blatant TECH to be broken, just metal gauntlets and however many pounds of angry brainwashed 80's kung-fu movie cliches.)<br /> <br /> So in essence. Tremere shows up. Is punched once. And then he explodes.<br /> <br /> And this is why you don't allow the Charles Atlas training camp. Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:25:05-07:00","id":965227,"title":"","content":"To be perfectly honest I do think that positing a major conflict between Vampires and the Technocracy does have a lot of interesting potential, but not when the ground rules arbitrarily hand it to the Technocracy at the starting line. Masturbating over how hard the Technocracy would pwn everyone is neither productive or engaging. I'd be interested in having some real discussion how the thread's premise would play out, but the scenario as its been presented isn't worth pursuing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:28:48-07:00","id":965232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not understand, clearly.<br /> <br /> First of all you can't use extra turns with time 3 to cast an effect, sorry, that's not gonna happening, extra actions you get with Time 3 can only be used for physical actions.<br /> <br /> Second, the point you are missing is that in the moment Tremere teleported himself in the council room the game was over.<br /> To cast that effect you'd need several turns, and you can't use time 3 to help you, you are going to do an extended roll.<br /> <br /> And Tremere will kill you all in one turn.<br /> You simply do not have the time to cast it.<br /> Besides, he has 10 dice of countermagick, good luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fucking tired of your condescending attitude. It is honestly the primary reason I'm quitting this debate.<br /> <br /> &quot;But the real ultimate deal here is that vampires in vampire are the secret masters of the world and Mages are nothing but mortals grasping blindly for power that isn't theirs, just like vampires in a Mage game are nothing but pathetic leeches shackled to the rules of the Consensus and unable to truly influence reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have played WoD since it's infancy, I do quite understand this. But it seems that you do not understand that Tremere only has that awesome power in Vampire, in Mage he's just an upstart leech with delusions of grandeur.<br /> <br /> And now it is my turn: You are quite aware that if you have made it to the level of Archmaster there is a pretty good chance you'll be walking around with buff spells and active defenses all the time, so there's no reason not to believe they'll have all these up all the time, and have foreseen it with Time and acted accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm sorry, they kiiled an Antedeluvian who was just freshly awaken in frenzy, distracted by 3 Bodhisattva and an horde of wraiths.<br /> <br /> In a direct confrontation you cannot kill Ravnos with these means; you nuke him? Ok, Chimestry 10, fire becomes mices. You point the sun to him? The sky becomes solid and black.<br /> Technocracy killed a frenzied Ante, surrounded by Bodhi and wraiths,<br /> And even more, one of the Ante who has not ascended like his peers.<br /> <br /> You can't kill Tzimisce, he is just immortal, you can't kill Ennoia, because she's planet Earth, you can't kill Lasombra because you can't Kill the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm tired of vampire supremacy that isn't supported by the book, five-dot spheres destroy cities, Archmasters can and will destroy planets <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the whole point of Ghenna, to make them killable they had to rely on the whole whitering thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And luckily an Archmaster with Entropy 7 can control the destiny of an entire species!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing short of an Oracle is gonna beat an Ante.<br /> And even there, if we have to rely on the stats of the Unnamed, it's not so sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> The Unnamed would pick up an Antediluvian and <i>spank </i>them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not my fault if you choose to ignore the rules and the lore.<br /> It's childish, it's like fleeing because someone made you notice that no, rules and lore permits other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>A): Ad hominem is generally not an acceptable debating strategy, neither is &quot;no u&quot;<br /> B): I notice how you never mentioned that it takes years to invent a Thaumaturgical Path, and how you never mentioned that inventing a Path is filled with danger.<br /> C): Still no counter to invincible Technocratic battlestation of destruction that destroys the earth with grey goo nanites.<br /> D): If the Tremere are so ludicriously powerful (which they are not), why haven't they destroyed the Technocracy yet? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You by started ignoring the fact that at the higher level blood magic works like true magic,and you are complaining because there are rules and lore for this on canon published material.<br /> So stop complaining, it's childish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am in fact not complaining, I have already offered to drop the discussion twice.<br /> <br /> But at least I am not actively <i>lying</i>, given that creating a new Path takes years, and there are no rules for learning a Ritual except for &quot;talk with your storyteller, it takes some time based on the level.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965206#post965206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, I'm sorry, the elder thaumaturges can devise any ritual they need,and create any effect they desires, it's the whole point of House of Tremere,Rites of Blood and so on,giving rules that make Blood Magic an open discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a strange effect, if only there was an entire splat based around freeform and improvised magic, with an antagonist known for murdering people with freeform and inventive magic that can be improvised on the fly using a technological and sci-fi-ish look for their effec- Wait a minute! That's <i>every Mage alive ever.</i><br /> <br /> I also distinctly remember that it was mentioned as signigicant that a vampire elder caused a volcano to erupt and destroyed a city. This is funny because <i>ever master of any Sphere</i> can do that.<br /> <br /> So what I'd like to do is that you start actually arguing out of published guidelines instead of actively <i>lying</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:29:29-07:00","id":965233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965227#post965227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be perfectly honest I do think that positing a major conflict between Vampires and the Technocracy does have a lot of interesting potential, but not when the ground rules arbitrarily hand it to the Technocracy at the starting line. Masturbating over how hard the Technocracy would pwn everyone is neither productive or engaging. I'd be interested in having some real discussion how the thread's premise would play out, but the scenario as its been presented isn't worth pursuing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree completely, though wanking the vampires to absurd degree certainly isn't funny either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:29:59-07:00","id":965234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965227#post965227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be perfectly honest I do think that positing a major conflict between Vampires and the Technocracy does have a lot of interesting potential, but not when the ground rules arbitrarily hand it to the Technocracy at the starting line. Masturbating over how hard the Technocracy would pwn everyone is neither productive or engaging. I'd be interested in having some real discussion how the thread's premise would play out, but the scenario as its been presented isn't worth pursuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In essence why I've ignored the initial scenario. Because in that case it's just &quot;Voidcraft own everything.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:34:56-07:00","id":965236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965234#post965234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In essence why I've ignored the initial scenario. Because in that case it's just &quot;Voidcraft own everything.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, for some reason I'm still arguing from that perspective and you can see how <i>that</i> is going, so you must obviously be the wisest of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:37:30-07:00","id":965237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965233#post965233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree completely, though wanking the vampires to absurd degree certainly isn't funny either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly not. Any discussion involving the Antediluvians and even a lot of Methuseleh quickly starts getting into ST fiat territory as well as escalating into DBZ levels of silliness. <br /> <br /> Removing paradox from the situation is not approaching the contest honestly though. Mages are already incredibly powerful and versatile, to the point that Vampires are pretty much guaranteed to be fighting an uphill battle. This is fine, uphill battles are interesting. Getting rid of one of the few significant limiters on a Mage's power is just overkill though, giving them what might as well be god-like agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:41:09-07:00","id":965240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965237#post965237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly not. Any discussion involving the Antediluvians and even a lot of Methuseleh quickly starts getting into ST fiat territory as well as escalating into DBZ levels of silliness.<br /> <br /> Removing paradox from the situation is not approaching the contest honestly though. Mages are already incredibly powerful and versatile, to the point that Vampires are pretty much guaranteed to be fighting an uphill battle. This is fine, uphill battles are interesting. Getting rid of one of the few significant limiters on a Mage's power is just overkill though, giving them what might as well be god-like agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this very much. In my usual setting, when I use vampires they are generally stuck in a Cold War with the Technocracy, due to the immense economic damage it would do to wage war against them, and therefore the Syndicate closes down any attempts to attack vampires overtly. <br /> <br /> &quot;Using proxies though...&quot;<br /> <br /> Both sides think as they look at each other, which means that you get situations, where a bunch of Traditions magi hired by an Operative meet a bunch of Traditions magi hired by a Ventrue and they just go: &quot;sigh, not again.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:49:16-07:00","id":965246,"title":"","content":"In fact, I've been looking at the old war system from Ascension, and according to this, a unit of five Neonates with three dots of Celerity each is equivalent to 100 veteran soldiers, and a single Mage with a Sphere at Mastery is equivalent to 500.<br /> <br /> This is the most beautiful thing I've ever read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:49:59-07:00","id":965247,"title":"","content":"The second point then becomes the status of the Masquerade. I know people wanted a big public blowout, but in the interests of fairness to the Technocracy I would suggest leaving it intact. This may sound strange but the fact is that the Masquerade exists for the sole purpose of protecting vampires from the threat of potential extermination. If they're going to be exterminated with or without the Masquerade they're going to throw it out the window and start getting really unsavory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:55:11-07:00","id":965253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965247#post965247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second point then becomes the status of the Masquerade. I know people wanted a big public blowout, but in the interests of fairness to the Technocracy I would suggest leaving it intact. This may sound strange but the fact is that the Masquerade exists for the sole purpose of protecting vampires from the threat of potential extermination. If they're going to be exterminated with or without the Masquerade they're going to throw it out the window and start getting really unsavory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I insist we use the war system so a Neonate with Celerity 5 can outfight 500 trained soldiers with his katana and trenchcoat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:00:40-07:00","id":965278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965232#post965232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fucking tired of your condescending attitude. It is honestly the primary reason I'm quitting this debate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You write a lot for someone who's quitting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have played WoD since it's infancy, I do quite understand this. But it seems that you do not understand that Tremere only has that awesome power in Vampire, in Mage he's just an upstart leech with delusions of grandeur. </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh please it's a crossover thread, in Vampire the Technocracy can't stop Ghenna, so what? The premise of the thread is &quot;cross-over&quot;, and if this is a thread about cross-over then Tremere has those powers even in Mage world.<br /> <br /> Even more I'm sorry to tell you, but Blood Treachery is a MAGE book,and in that book Vampire discipline works like in Vampire, so sadly for you even in MAGE world Tremere has those powers because in MAGE canon published work the VAMPIRE HAVE those powers, for the same reason Baba Yaga has her Thaumaturgy 9 in Rage across russia, that is a Werewolf book, and for the same reason in Thime of Thin Blood the Void Engineers have Spirit-Nukes, because, sadly for you, with the end of the second edition and the revised the world has been unified, that's the reason pages and pages of the storyteller hand-book deals in cross-overs rules with Vampire and Werewolf, because,again sadly for you, White Wolf decided that the world was the same, so I'm sorry bu Blood Treachery made this clear: <b><u>even in mage world those powers exist.</u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And now it is my turn: You are quite aware that if you have made it to the level of Archmaster there is a pretty good chance you'll be walking around with buff spells and active defenses all the time, so there's no reason not to believe they'll have all these up all the time, and have foreseen it with Time and acted accordingly. </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure sure, I read ascension, 20 dice worth of effect prepared, sure.<br /> But again, how these are going to help you with a creature that can kill you in one turn?<br /> <br /> The only way is play smart like Voormas with Touh Mouh, or you are not gonna make it.<br /> Or being an Oracle who can cast as many effect he wishes in one turn.<br /> <br /> And that's the why only an Oracle can take a Ante in direct fight: because he can survive until the next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> But again...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so there's no reason not to believe they'll have all these up all the time, and have foreseen it with Time and acted accordingly </div> </div> </div>Didn't seem to me in Blood Treachery that the Council was expecting Tremere visit, don't they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before he can say more, CORDOVERA's eyes spout fountains of blood. He screams. Guards rush to help, but bolts of electricity shoot from his body, stunning them. CORDOVERA's face begins twitching, and his clothes begin changing. A massive telekinetic wave sends every mage sprawling. CORDOVERA's hands erupt into flame. And then, suddenly, it is no longer CORDOVERA, but a figure that wears the bloodied mask of a VAMPIRE ANCIENT. The masked figure, a spirit projected through undead powers into the very heart of the Traditions, radiates authority that will not be questioned. The mask bears a striking resemblance to that of the MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE in Act Two,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>The assembled magi stand, stunned.</b> </b>One FLAMBEAU rushes toward the ANCIENT. The mask turns to face the FLAMBEAU, and the FLAMBEAU is frozen in place. No one else dares to move. ANCIENT: No welcome for the prodigal son, then? More's the pity, I suppose.The ANCIENT surveys the Council Chamber. My, my, my... what a lovely retreat you've constructed for yourselves! Tell me, is this then where you have been hiding for all these years? I certainly haven't seen you out in the world, after all. I almost believed you were all destroyed.<br /> <br /> JOSIAH: He broke the wards?<br /> <br /> ANCIENT: Blood knows blood, young man. You<br /> were foolish enough to bring one of mine into your<br /> Sanctum. If I learned nothing else from our adversaries<br /> in the Carpathians, I learned that one never invites the<br /> vampyr into one's abode. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm tired of vampire supremacy that isn't supported by the book, five-dot spheres destroy cities, Archmasters can and will destroy planets </div> </div> </div>Pfffff...ahahahahha... lol.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/ed/ed1d530c3894f49cfcf43b01a30c08c74f4131a579862139f689edaa671d4bd2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To destroy a single city you need...I don't know...20-30 success if we stand by M20, vulgar as hell and you'd need also a lot of quintessence.<br /> <br /> To destroy a planet,.. please, don't make me laugh, we are talking of a feat a thousand success worth, with paradox biting your neck to the bone.<br /> <br /> the only similar case ever presented is Voormas ritual, which required by the way some thousands questing avatar, an unique godly artifact with a supreme resonance, and several of the most powerful nodes on Earth.<br /> <br /> If what you are suggesting was possible Porthos would have cracked Aucthonia years ago, or Senex would have purified the Karma wheel by himself,or the Nephandi would have destroyed Earth.<br /> <br /> Please, you are overshouting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is correct.<br /> <br /> The Unnamed would pick up an Antediluvian and <i>spank </i>them. </div> </div> </div><br /> I doubt it,he has the same problem every mage has: being slow and having a limited dicepool, he can't go unprepared.<br /> <br /> Because even the Unnamed for his effects use simply 10 arete dices and must get the necessary success to achieve it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Unnamed is gonna use force 7 to blow you up!<br /> <br /> Base difficult 11 (7+4), he reduce it by 3, base difficult 8.<br /> <br /> How many success do you need to blow up an Ante? So yeah, good luck getting 20 success at difficult 8 with an arete dicepool of 10 in one turn.<br /> <br /> If you can survive all those turns than yes, you can do it.<br /> If you cant' absorb the immane ammount of damage that is coming than no.<br /> <br /> Let's put this way: Ravnos, even after 3 days of fight with 3 virtual Arhat survived 4 spirit nukes, each one deals 10 levels (levels, not dice) of Agg from the impact, 10 agg from the firestorm, 10 bashing for the force wave and 16 agg from the radiation, all of this x4, (so 40 levels of agg, 40 dice of agg,40 dice of bashing, and 64 dice of agg), and after that 12 levels per turn of aggravated damage from the sun.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, unless the Unnamed, with his 10 dice arete pool, can deal a total of 144 dice of aggravated damages, plus 40 of bashing, in just one turn, even he is gonna have some problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which doesn't means he can't beat it, but not on easy terms.<br /> <br /> Besides, remember that the Unnamed was almost killed by Senex, with a knife.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> A): Ad hominem is generally not an acceptable debating strategy, neither is &quot;no u&quot;<br /> B): I notice how you never mentioned that it takes years to invent a Thaumaturgical Path, and how you never mentioned that inventing a Path is filled with danger.<br /> C): Still no counter to invincible Technocratic battlestation of destruction that destroys the earth with grey goo nanites.<br /> D): If the Tremere are so ludicriously powerful (which they are not), why haven't they destroyed the Technocracy yet? </div> </div> </div><br /> A) Sorry, Ad hominem just doesn't work this way, it would be Ad hominem if I was validating my point by saying that since you are childish my point is right, but I'm not saying the the righteousness of my argument is proved by your behaviour, I'm just saying you are acting childish, wich is a statement that esulate from the matter of the debate.<br /> <br /> B) I notice how you don't consider that the time needed to invent a path is based on the thaumaturge knowledge of the subject,a Thaumaturge like Ur-Shulgi, with Int 9,Occult 9,doesn't needs the research time a common vampire needs, by the means of his intelligence only a Methuselah might know technology better than any technocrats, just beacuse at intelligence 8 you are like an Enlighted agent who has Int 4 and Hypertech 4; Mary St.John, the founder of the Path of Technomancy, created the whole thing in one year, and she was a 20 years old vampire of the 13th generation, so if Mary St.John ,20 years old, 13th gen ,Int 4 computer programming 4 Occult 4 could devise an entire new path in one year what could do Ur-Shuli, 8000 years old, 4th gen, Int 9, Occult 9, Thauma 9 in a day?<br /> I'll tell you: in a day he can break the Tremere blood curse.<br /> <br /> <br /> C)As i said: the top Thaumaturges will simply create something, just like they did when they had to break the siege of Chorazin when they summoned the Abyss, like they did in the second Baali war when they make Thera errupt and destroyed the whole island of Knossus, like Menele did when he wanted to kill Helena in Pompei, they will simply create it out of need.<br /> It's not like the whole Thera-Vesuvius thing was planned, no, at some point some terribly powerfull thaumatuges need thing to blow up with style and they invented the right ritual on the moment, and, if they are all working together good luck,you have Velya,the Inner Council,Lohui, Ur-Shulgi, Al-Ashrad and a lot of other demi-god working togheter toward a common goal, how much time will take for them to devise something? One week? Ur-Shulgi broke the Tremere curse just as he rised from the grave, common.<br /> <br /> <br /> D)Who gives a damn about Technocracy? They are not an enemy at the moment,and more importantly they are playing to win a much older game,who cares about a bunch of techno-weirdos when your aim is winning the Jhyad? Sabbat is a priority, Saulot is a priority, all the other blaste blood-gods who are about to rise are a priority.<br /> Probably even the Horder of Hermes is an higher priority than Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But at least I am not actively <i>lying</i>, given that creating a new Path takes years, and there are no rules for learning a Ritual except for &quot;talk with your storyteller, it takes some time based on the level.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I'm not lying, I simply can read that it takes years based on the research you must do,I simply make cross reference with the entries of New York by Nights and Transylvania Chronicles,or with the Baali Clanbook,or Rites of Blood, t's not my fault if you clearly have fragmented notions of how blood magic works.<br /> <br /> And if you are Etrius you don't need to do any research, at Thauma 9 and Occult 9 there is nothing you don't know, you don't need to research anything, and the whole thing isn't simply required for Rituals, whose creation is much faster.<br /> It's a matter of fact that is affixed in lore, the most powerful Thaumaturges just can invent ritual on the fly, look what Baba Yaga did in Russia, or the Inner Council at the Convention of Tyre, or again the ritual Tremere created while in Etrius body while he was travelling to Mexico.<br /> <br /> Besides you are forgetting that V20 eliminated the time component of the blood magic creation, the only needed requirements to develop blood magic are the respect of the Principle of Will, the Principle of knowledge and the Principle of Identity, besides these today there are no other requirements.and to learn a new rituals or adapt it from another school of blood magic is a feat that requires from a couple of nights to a couple of weeks if you just focus on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What a strange effect, if only there was an entire splat based around freeform and improvised magic, with an antagonist known for murdering people with freeform and inventive magic that can be improvised on the fly using a technological and sci-fi-ish look for their effec- Wait a minute! That's <i>every Mage alive ever.</i> </div> </div> </div>Ehmmm...and so? What's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also distinctly remember that it was mentioned as signigicant that a vampire elder caused a volcano to erupt and destroyed a city. This is funny because <i>ever master of any Sphere</i> can do that. </div> </div> </div>Straw man,I wasn't saying a mage can't do it, I was saying a Vampire can do it too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So what I'd like to do is that you start actually arguing out of published guidelines instead of actively <i>lying</i>. </div> </div> </div>I'm already doing it, sadly your knowledge of it is not as good as mine so you can't understand it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The fact that you don't rember the part of Rites Construction in Rites of Blood, or the entry on Mary St.Johnesin New York by night or the plot-wise explanations of House of tremere is just like the whole time 3 thing, or the &quot;mirroshade for dominate&quot; or &quot;cameras for obfuscate&quot; thing.<br /> You just don't know rules and lore. as simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:22:22-07:00","id":965295,"title":"","content":"If you want to play a game where every 4th gen Tremere, al-Ashrad, etc. can instantaneously develop and use five dots in the Path of No You Can't Do That, that's fine - it doesn't harm me. It doesn't seem like a very fun game though, and you'd have to figure out why all Thaumaturges haven't used this godlike power to remake the world to their whims. It turns Vampire into a game of &quot;I wonder what those cool thaumaturges are going to do today&quot; and turns Mage into a game of &quot;wow I guess we should have all turned into blood mages like the Tremere, can't believe we suck so bad&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:35:32-07:00","id":965301,"title":"","content":"Undead Rabbit.<br /> <br /> Using the Lichdom Rote as a baseline, develop Cyberzombies. Ensure that prospective Cyberzombies have the Resilient Pattern merit.<br /> <br /> Apply aforementioned Charles Atlas training camp to aforementioned Cyberzombies.<br /> <br /> Then smack the Syndicate and tell them to give up some major quintessence to apply paradox wards out the ASS to the now UNKILLABLE 80's kung-fu movie cliches that can vaporize any foe in a single punch/kick. Cackle maniacally to taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Video for reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:39:21-07:00","id":965303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965278#post965278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you don't rember the part of Rites Construction in Rites of Blood, or the entry on Mary St.Johnesin New York by night or the plot-wise explanations of House of tremere is just like the whole time 3 thing, or the &quot;mirroshade for dominate&quot; or &quot;cameras for obfuscate&quot; thing.<br /> You just don't know rules and lore. as simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm, there is no &quot;whole Time 3 thing&quot;, a mage with Time 3 can give himself an absurd amount of extra actions:<br /> <br /> &quot;A mage wrapped in dilated or contracted time can easily cocoon himself in a protective layer that insulates himself from the outside world, effectively freezing himself in time, or accelerate to the point ofperforming numerous physical tasks in a few seconds.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can actually give yourself a completely arbitrary amount of actions.<br /> <br /> And when you claim that I don't know the rules and lore, I'll actually acquiesce to you there.<br /> <br /> I don't because it's ages ago since I could force myself to give a damn about Masquerade enough to remember all those things. I focus primarily on Wraith and Mage, and those are my two things, and even them I am losing my interest in slowly.<br /> <br /> But when you accuse me of not knowing the rules and lore, you also accuse literally every other person that has rooted for the Technocracy of not knowing the rules and lore, which is a pretty bold claim if I should say so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:40:14-07:00","id":965304,"title":"","content":"Looking this over the biggest issue I have is with the base premise itself, the Technocracy exists to dispel and remove mention of the supernatural. The Camarilla (and a good portion of the Independents, and some of the more adroit Sabbat) have a vested self-interest in maintaining the Masquerade. If the Masquerade has fallen, both sides have essentially already failed at their most basic mission. Additionally removing/greatly lessening Paradox eliminates the only check on magickal power, likely handing the victory to the Union since even without access to things like interdimensional vessels, they still have more than enough hypertech to eliminate all but the more potent elders with ease. Within the context of the parameters as given, I think the freeform nature of awakened magick (even limited by the Technocratic mindset) will eventually win out, the question is how much of humanity and the Earth is left after the fallout (both figurative and literally). Could vampires win? Possibly, with luck and guile they might work their way into dealing with the higher ups in the Technocracy before they can bring the full might of the Technocratic enlightened will to bear. That said the vampires are definitely the underdogs in this match in my opinion, if Paradox was still functioning in a manner as 'normal' I think the vampires stand a better chance (but are still the underdogs, magick's open ended nature is still a huge advantage).<br /> <br /> &lt;My two cents on how the failure of the Masquerade could play out in an interesting way&gt;<br /> With such a shattering of the screen which protects humans from knowledge of the supernatural, a more likely outcome is both sides fall prey to factionalization and infighting. The different conventions all blame each other for the failure. In the same way vampire society would likely come crashing down as well. The elders who remember the times of the Inquisition are likely to be in a panic, since humanity has come a long way from relying on pitchforks, fire, and faith to defeat vampires (especially those with knowledge of [Ravnos]'s fate). Younger vampires are likely to look at the event as the moment they've been waiting for (especially the Sabbat including some of their elders) where vampires can finally act like vampires without pretending to be human just for the sake of the Masquerade. Each side ends up paralyzed by infighting and finger pointing with those who aren't set about turning the world into what amounts to a dumpster fire. <br /> <br /> Eventually after exhausting the initial arguing over whose fault the situation is the elders among the Camarilla and the higher ups in the Technocracy are likely to come to an ironic agreement to remove the wild and out of control elements. Essentially I see the two entering into a devil's bargain; the vampires get the right to exist and the Technocracy will begin researching ways to provide for vampiric needs (think a True Blood like concoction) in return the vampires being working with the Technocracy to eliminate the vampiric elements who wont play nice with humanity (as well as offering the ability to create essentially immortal assets through ghouldom/embrace) as well as removing the threat of other reality deviants. With the knowledge of the vampiric elders (and the sympathetic links through vitae) the Sabbat and the other inhuman vampires are likely to be wiped out (a handful might escape, but will not have the strength to provide any real resistance, since if they reveal themselves they would be destroyed). That said some of the battles are going to be quite brutal, a fairly sizable chunk of humanity is likely to die in the war. In the end you have a new status quo.<ul><li>Vampires exist and the Technocracy has created (or is creating) scientific ways to explain the various powers and abilities they possess, essentially vampirism is added to the Consensus.</li> <li>New laws are crafted and quickly passed to answer questions regarding vampiric legal status for things such as political standing and rights, taxes, estates, ghouling, embrace, use of supernatural powers, etc.</li> <li>The Technocracy has created an artificial substitute for blood that is palatable for all vampires (even those with feeding restrictions) and is provided after registering with the New World Order (registering is likely to be providing a sample of vitae and or flesh for tracking and surveillance purposes).</li> <li>The pro-Masquerade elders now have nearly complete control over younger vampires (since the agreement that protect vampires is vouchsafed by the elders and the Technocratic control). Failure to follow the rules will be met with extreme punishment (in most cases likely destruction of the offending vampire).</li> <li>The Technocracy, bolstered by powers such as Dominate, Presence, Obfuscate, Chimerstry, etc, begin to zealously crush knowledge of other supernaturals and likely refocus their attention at dealing with the Traditions and other reality deviants. Bolstered by their vampiric allies, the Traditions could be in a great deal of trouble (which could lead to a Tradition and Garou alliance in the face of this new Techno-vampiric Union).</li> <li>The rogue elements of vampire society (Anarchs, Sabbat, and Independents who refuse to play within the new rules) are either destroyed or decimated to the point of being nonfactors (exceptions might occur, those knowledgeable in Necromancy or Spirit Manipulation might flee beyond the Shroud/Gauntlet for example). In the same way rogue elements within the Technocracy are likely to be found and dealt with after the application of the various powers of their new vampiric allies (blood bond and Dominate are great ways to insure re-education proceeds at the approved Technocratic pace).</li> <li>The Technocracy might even be able to remove the vampiric clan weaknesses (while they might not be able to roll more successes than God and cure vampirism they should be able to get more than Caine).</li> <li>Within the Technocracy I see vampires ending up in one of three possible situations<ul><li>The vampires become their own Convention within the Union</li> <li>The vampires join the Conventions which match their mindset and skill set. This could lead to things like Ventrue or Giovanni being higher ups in the Syndicate, Tzimisce using Vicissitude to assist Progenitor experiments, Tremere techno-mages assisting Iteration X in developing ghoul/vampire HIT Marks, etc.</li> <li>The vampires do not join the Union outright but rather maintain a separate governing body, bound by agreements and treaties with the Union and possibly mortal authorities depending on how new vampire laws look.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:40:45-07:00","id":965305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965301#post965301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Undead Rabbit.<br /> <br /> Using the Lichdom Rote as a baseline, develop Cyberzombies. Ensure that prospective Cyberzombies have the Resilient Pattern merit.<br /> <br /> Apply aforementioned Charles Atlas training camp to aforementioned Cyberzombies.<br /> <br /> Then smack the Syndicate and tell them to give up some major quintessence to apply paradox wards out the ASS to the now UNKILLABLE 80's kung-fu movie cliches that can vaporize any foe in a single punch/kick. Cackle maniacally to taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bS5P_LAqiVg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Video for reference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Give them Exomuscle and Exoskeletons too, because fuck you that's why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:55:32-07:00","id":965309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965303#post965303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehm, there is no &quot;whole Time 3 thing&quot;, a mage with Time 3 can give himself an absurd amount of extra actions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;A mage wrapped in dilated or contracted time can easily cocoon himself in a protective layer that insulates himself from the outside world, effectively freezing himself in time, or accelerate to the point ofperforming numerous physical tasks in a few seconds.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, he can't.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, it's clear you have no idea what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> m20 How do you do that page 107<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;To gain extra actions, or to slow other characters down, use Time 3. <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Every additional action demands two successes</span>. One or two extra actions may be passed off as coincidental bursts of speed; three or more extra actions per turn move the mage into vulgar magick territory.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Which he can use only for physical actions, because even using Time 3 you can do JUST arete one roll per turn<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage 20 Page 523<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022\u2022\u2022 Time Contraction or Dilation/<br /> <br /> \u201cBullet Time\u201d/ Rewind Time<br /> <br /> Speeding or slowing her relationship with time, the mage can now gain multiple actions, slow other characters or phenomena, or rewind small snatches of time. <b>In game terms, every two successes allow the character to take one additional action that does not involve casting magick (only one Arete roll<br /> may be made per turn);&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mage 20 page 528<br /> <br /> &quot;How Many Effects Can I Use at Once?<br /> <b>A mage<span style=\"font-size:24px\"> can cast only one Effect per turn, even if she\u2019s using Time 3 magick to speed up her activities</span>.</b> She may, however, keep any number of Effects running at a time, although it becomes more and more difficult for her to do so.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if in your turn you use Time 3 to get extra actions that's it, that's the effect you used, you can't use those actions to cast another effect, so you must choose: either you cast Time 3 to get extra-actions either you cast the...whatever ridiculous effect with Force 6 you were mentionig before.<br /> The only being who can cast more effect in one turn is the Unnamed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can actually give yourself a completely arbitrary amount of actions. </div> </div> </div>No, as you can see you can get onyl one extra action every two success, and after 3 it gets vulgar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And it was so in Revised also, it's not a new rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage Revies page 103<br /> <br /> Time 3, Distort Time<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Every two success scored causes the bubble to accelerate or decelerate time by one factor. Thus, two success would allow a mage to double her physical speed, taking two actions in a single turn&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 155<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<b>A mage can cast only one Effect per turn, even if she has used various powers to speed herself up</b> (reality is already \u201cpreoccupied\u201d when it\u2019s in a different time frame). &quot;<br /> <br /> You see? You just proved again that you simply do not know the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't because it's ages ago since I could force myself to give a damn about Masquerade enough to remember all those things. </div> </div> </div>Which, I hope you understand, it's a problem if your intention is discussing cross-over stuff in a thread about cross-over stuff.<br /> <br /> But even worse it's clear you do not even know Mage rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But when you accuse me of not knowing the rules and lore, you also accuse literally every other person that has rooted for the Technocracy of not knowing the rules and lore, which is a pretty bold claim if I should say so. </div> </div> </div>No, I'm accusing you specifically, because the others didn't said that with &quot;Time 3 can give himself an absurd amount of extra actions&quot;, or that &quot;Also Dominate literally fails against mirrorshades&quot;.<br /> It's you who have no idea what are you talking about, both on vampire side and on mage side (which is even worse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":""