16:05:11-07:00","id":965312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965309#post965309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if in your turn you use Time 3 to get extra actions that's it, that's the effect you used, you can't use those actions to cast another effect, so you must choose: either you cast Time 3 to get extra-actions either you cast the...whatever ridiculous effect with Force 6 you were mentionig before.<br /> The only being who can cast more effect in one turn is the Unnamed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaactually, there is a character in First Edition that can cast two effects per turn, since she's an amalgam of two Technocrats, and thus casts as two, she's the leader of the MECHA Construct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:12:26-07:00","id":965314,"title":"","content":"FIRST EDITION<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You are quoting mage FIRST EDITION<br /> <br /> <br /> Can't believe, I suspected as much but I can't believe it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's since second edition, aka 1995 that Mage works the way I say.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> But again where? I'm checking, and in the first edition worked just the same, two success for every extra-action, the only difference is that the roll could work for more turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:18:57-07:00","id":965317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965314#post965314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FIRST EDITION<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You are quoting mage FIRST EDITION<br /> <br /> <br /> Can't believe, I suspected as much but I can't believe it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's since second edition, aka 1995 that Mage works the way I say.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> But again where? I'm checking, and in the first edition worked just the same, two success for every extra-action, the only difference is that the roll could work for more turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was primarily quoting that thing for the joke of it, I can't stand First Edition and prefer Revised to any other edition any day. :P<br /> <br /> I believe she is in the Book of Chantries if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:20:30-07:00","id":965319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965310#post965310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For proper dick measuring,The 3 KJ were winning before the Technocracy nuked the situation. There's a strong implication that at least one of them survived. If they Technocracy had not interfered they were prophesized to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they were losing.<br /> In truth they were so desperate that they opened a portal to Yomi wan to summon an army of wraiths to fight Ravana.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tieh Ju and Chou Li watched the supernatural storm from a mile away. The mundane storm hardly bothered them.<br /> &quot;It is the Yomi World,&quot; Tieh Ju explained to the curious snake-man. &quot;Hell on Earth. If nothing contains it soon, it will cover the world. In opening doors to both the Yn and Yang Worlds, the Bodhisattvas may have acted imprudently&quot; </div> </div> </div>And I can't recall any prophecy about them winning, there was just a dream made by all the Dharma that foretold the fight in Devil-Tigers dharma book, and it didn't said that they were going to win.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This summer, shortly after the sighting of the red star, many Devil-Tigers dreamt nightly of the 10- headed Yama King Ravana. In their dreams, Ravana split the mountain that imprisoned him and sent evil dreams to chase his children. He ten battled a Crane, a Dragon and a Tiger until the sun rose and ended the dream. Scholars interpreted the dream as representing a great evil awakening in the world, perhaps not Ravana himself but rather a precursor to the Sixth Age schooled in the Yama King's arts of deceit and illusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides this I can't remember a prophecy about the battle, and here it doesn't say that the bodhi were destinated to defeat Ravana, but that th sun would have ended the dream.<br /> And it happened just as so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Voorhmas in Ascension is so powerful his very nature twists any and all uses of necromancy. They very concept of it, including the discipline. The whole of clan Cappadocious and Giovanni are they way they are because of him. His nature is such that it retroactively twists the universe to be such.<br /> <br /> <br /> He also killed a Yama King without an army. Just him. </div> </div> </div>No, he killed the Yama Queen after he tricked her in performing a tantric ritual to merge their essence.<br /> In the moment she lowered all her defenses for the merging he used his necromantic powers to relase all the souls she devoured.<br /> And it's a bit different than kill a Yama King in fight.<br /> <br /> Besides that, yes, Voormas was probably the most powerful mage in any traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:21:47-07:00","id":965320,"title":"","content":"Technically. In Revised Time 3 works that way, the only Time power that has a restriction on magic being used is sidestep time. Which states that your magic is being used up to power the effect. Though if you want to cast multiple effects a round, use Charms/Gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:24:19-07:00","id":965322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965320#post965320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically. In Revised Time 3 works that way, the only Time power that has a restriction on magic being used is sidestep time. Which states that your magic is being used up to power the effect. Though if you want to cast multiple effects a round, use Charms/Gadgets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Revised too you can use just cast one effect per turn (page 155) and every extra action needs two success (page 193).<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;A mage can cast only one Effect per turn, even if she has used various powers to speed herself up&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-07-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:29:09-07:00","id":965324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965319#post965319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually they were losing.<br /> In truth they were so desperate that they opened a portal to Yomi wan to summon an army of wraiths to fight Ravana.<br /> <br /> And I can't recall any prophecy about them winning, there was just a dream foretolding the fight in Devil-Tigers dharma book, and it didn't said that they were going to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot remember any such prophecy either, and reading through the section in Time of Thin Blood gives me nothing, except that they strain themselves really much and don't really accomplish a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:37:08-07:00","id":965327,"title":"","content":"In any case, the time thing doesn't matter. Because there's still no answer for the fact that the Technocracy could, in a no-holds barred war, mass produce fanatically loyal, literally unkillable, abominations that can <b>VAPORIZE YOU WITH A SINGLE PUNCH. </b>And are hilariously, immune to countermagic so you can't just unweave their stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title"