"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:43:48-07:00","id":965332,"title":"","content":"Eh, trying to avoid going all in on the cheese. But depending on how the Lichdom Rote survives Transition from Euthanic to Technocratic Paradigm... entirely possible.<br /> <br /> Though there's still the incidence cost in finding enough people with Resilient Patterns to make into super soldiers because otherwise they're just really tough, rather than literally unkillable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:45:19-07:00","id":965334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965332#post965332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, trying to avoid going all in on the cheese. But depending on how the Lichdom Rote survives Transition from Euthanic to Technocratic Paradigm... entirely possible.<br /> <br /> Though there's still the incidence cost in finding enough people with Resilient Patterns to make into super soldiers because otherwise they're just really tough, rather than literally unkillable.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> I was working on a sympathetic &quot;murder all vampires&quot; plague a bit earlier, then I got bored and realized it would be too much up to the storyteller whether it would work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:37:07-07:00","id":965362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965139#post965139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hate you, I hate all of you, I want to die.<br /> <br /> End my suffering propability-calculator-chan.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/xY0-FehL4lM?t=8\" target=\"_blank\">Just leave it to Dictator.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:49:50-07:00","id":965379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965028#post965028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense.<br /> There are 3000-4000 Technocrats in the world and just 800 Hit-Mark, against a possibly infinite number of vampires,they simply do not have the forces to keep the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The best thing for them would be hide in their space fortress, hoping the Ventrue and Lasombra Methuselah do not make them fall using Dominate 8 or the Inner Council wipe them out from the sky with Thaumaturgy 9.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the lasombra could just replicate the Chorazin's destruction: After they discover where you are with Auspex they use Abyss Mysticism ritual and the space stations are destroyed by the tsunami of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Ur-Shulgi will use some ancient and forgotten ritual to make them fall...<br /> <br /> <br /> There are a LOT of way to take down those birds.<br /> <br /> Another way? Montano enters the Abyss, and emerge in the Space Stations (if there is a shadow in there, then Montano can use it as a door), then Domination party.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And no, there is no anti-embrace vaccine, as Blood Treachery says no mage can roll more dices than God: Vampirism is a curse from God, and you are not gonna beat God.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? There are tens of thousands of Technocrats in this world. That 4,000 number was prior the Mage per population being revised(one per a million to one per 150,000), and IIRC, the Ascension explicitly stated that 4,000 number is only a portion of their personnel. And Enlightened Technocrats comprise scarcely (probably less than) 1% of the Technocracy's rank and file.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Antideluvian intervene, then surely the Oracles do. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-08-2016, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:53:41-07:00","id":965380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965053#post965053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you make that a prerequisite than you might as well have the Mages win by fiat.<br /> <br /> All you're doing here is setting up a mean spirited power fantasy where you talk about how much you would totally shit all over another game line for the lulz.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965227#post965227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be perfectly honest I do think that positing a major conflict between Vampires and the Technocracy does have a lot of interesting potential, but not when the ground rules arbitrarily hand it to the Technocracy at the starting line. Masturbating over how hard the Technocracy would pwn everyone is neither productive or engaging. I'd be interested in having some real discussion how the thread's premise would play out, but the scenario as its been presented isn't worth pursuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Judging from course of the discussion - over seven pages now -, it is rather obvious that referred condition does not guarantee automatics win switch or one-sided curb stomp for the Mages.<br /> <br /> Besides, you are over-reacting. You are simply incapable of accepting prospect of wholesale extermination of the Cainites and impotently Raging about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-07-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:01:07-07:00","id":965382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965319#post965319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually they were losing.<br /> In truth they were so desperate that they opened a portal to Yomi wan to summon an army of wraiths to fight Ravana.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I can't recall any prophecy about them winning, there was just a dream made by all the Dharma that foretold the fight in Devil-Tigers dharma book, and it didn't said that they were going to win.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This summer, shortly after the sighting of the red star, many Devil-Tigers dreamt nightly of the 10- headed Yama King Ravana. In their dreams, Ravana split the mountain that imprisoned him and sent evil dreams to chase his children. He ten battled a Crane, a Dragon and a Tiger until the sun rose and ended the dream. Scholars interpreted the dream as representing a great evil awakening in the world, perhaps not Ravana himself but rather a precursor to the Sixth Age schooled in the Yama King's arts of deceit and illusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides this I can't remember a prophecy about the battle, and here it doesn't say that the bodhi were destinated to defeat Ravana, but that th sun would have ended the dream.<br /> And it happened just as so.</div> </div> </div> </div>the prophesy is in the Nagah book. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> No, he killed the Yama Queen after he tricked her in performing a tantric ritual to merge their essence.<br /> In the moment she lowered all her defenses for the merging he used his necromantic powers to relase all the souls she devoured.<br /> And it's a bit different than kill a Yama King in fight.<br /> <br /> Besides that, yes, Voormas was probably the most powerful mage in any traditions. </div> </div> </div>its still something he did single handedly. Keeping in mind Saulot apparently worked REALLY hard to try and become a Yama King and.. didn't get there. Well according to the Transylvania chronicles.<br /> <br /> We could also talk about whether the Red Sign retcons Blood Treachery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:20:50-07:00","id":965391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965188#post965188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lol, Tremere spends one blood point and Dominate the entire room, or make it explode with Thauma 10.<br /> <br /> The moment Tremere entered the room the fight was over.<br /> <br /> Besides, again, how many turns to cast a Correspondence 3, Force 6,Spirit 5 effect that must destroy an Immortal soul?<br /> <br /> Mmmh...vulgare,without witness, base difficult 10.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they were going to pull it.<br /> <br /> Considering that for sure a 1300 years old Vampire has a bit more dexterity and wits that makes him start first?<br /> <br /> Besides sorry but who was going to cast it? I don't remember many archmages on earth after the reckoning.<br /> <br /> But again, what are we talking about? Dominate 10 and you are already in the room, the game is over.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You said Pentex infiltration in SPD, then Reckoning? <br /> <br /> How convenient conception of time, like Masters of Time Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:24:08-07:00","id":965394,"title":"","content":"Yeah this was clearly a mistake. Nice talkin' with y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:27:52-07:00","id":965397,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200b<b>Sticking my head in to remind people to keep it civil or the thread gets closed. I dislike these kinds of threads because we moderators invariably end up having to close them and this one is getting near to that point. Suspensions also commonly follow those closings, don't be that guy.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:08:10-07:00","id":965493,"title":"","content":"....................","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:34:49-07:00","id":965539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965379#post965379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you talking about? There are tens of thousands of Technocrats in this world. That 4,000 number was prior the Mage per population being revised(one per a million to one per 150,000), and IIRC, the Ascension explicitly stated that 4,000 number is only a portion of their personnel. And Enlightened Technocrats comprise scarcely (probably less than) 1% of the Technocracy's rank and file.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it was not a portion, it was the most of it, only Ragnarok command didn't answered the call of Aleph, beside that all the Technocracy answered the call for the final war.<br /> And no, the ratio enlightened agents to Un-enlightened agents is 1:5<br /> <br /> Page 78<br /> <br /> &quot;General Aleph commands 4000 Enlightened Technocrats, 8000 extraordinary Citizens and 20000 sleeper soldiers. <b>He has no other reserves .<br /> This is an all-or nothing fight to which he commits every Technocrat that he can muster</b>. Many of them are scientist, not warriors: dozens are freshly conditioned from the internment camps. Ragnarok Command's amalgams refuse to participate so they can dispatch aid to Sleepers and defend against threats from the Deep Universe.<br /> Twenty ARC-2 helicopters, four Aurora transatmospherich fighters, 1000 hardsuits and 500 HIT marks are at their disposal, along dozens of conventional veichles and satellite support.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, Guide to the Technocracy, page 95<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, the appearance of overwhelming power is useful to the Union,<b> but the fact is, there just aren't enough Enlightened agents and allied citizens to exert that sort of power over all of society.</b> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>With perhaps a few thousand Enlightened ops worldwide and four or five times that number in un-Enlightened assistance,</b></span> the Technocracy just doesn't have the manpower to be everywhere at once. Even the Enlightened Science used to monitor trouble spots has to be maintained by someone. Since those monitors are just as susceptible to human error as anyone else, quite a bit can fall outside the Technocracy's field of vision&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is consistent with the numbers given in Ascension by the way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, please source for the &quot;tens of thousands of Technocrats in this world.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965379#post965379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said Pentex infiltration in SPD, then Reckoning?<br /> <br /> How convenient conception of time, like Masters of Time Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the matter? We were talking specifically about Blood Treachery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also: <b>Blood Treachery is fucking shit</b>, and requires that the Hermetics act like idiots instead of Mages. <b>That encounter with Tremere should have ended with &quot;lol Correspondence 3, Forces 6, Spirit 5, you're dead, your soul is dead and every iteration of you is dead.&quot;</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The moment Tremere entered <b>the room</b> the fight was over.<br /> <br /> Besides sorry but who was going to cast it? I don't remember many archmages on earth after the reckoning. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> And in Blood Treachery, as in all the revised setting, is a matter of fact that archmasters are something that you don't quite find everywhere every day.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was a very specific consideration which dealt with a very specific occurrence: the meeting between Tremere and the Council, page 51-54.<br /> And since at the time of Blood Treachery there are few master and even fewer archmaster (Ishaq is probably the most powerful mage still active in the Order, and he would have not been able to cast that effect) my doubt was sound :in<b> that occurrence </b>who <b>in that room </b>had the power to cast an effect powerful enough to kill Tremere?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Besides I'm not even sure what's the problem with the whole SPD thing (even without taking in consideration the fact that for the reckoning I was talking about a totally different and specific subject).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-08-2016, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:52:41-07:00","id":965545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965382#post965382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the prophesy is in the Nagah book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't find anything in Nagah book which resembles a prophecy.<br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Found it.<br /> <br /> Well,it's unreliable at best.<br /> It's a prophecy that has never come to fulfilment, so not really a good prophecy.<br /> <br /> Even more it's overruled by the prophetic dream of the Devil-Tigers which was much more precise and forsesaw the intervention of Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So we have two prophecies, and one of them is utterly wrong, and not because of outside intervention, because the Devil-Tigers predicted that outside intervention.<br /> <br /> So again, unreliable at best, In-character misunderstanding at worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is only one way to make the prophecy true: interpret it with a wider and general meaning and assume that while the prophecy is true the might Nagah have misunderstood its meaning.<br /> <br /> The prophecy says that the Dragon was destined to beat Ravana.<br /> <br /> &quot;But the last, the Dancing Dragon, would have defeated him&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> This might still be so if the rumors about Black Earth Boy being trapped in Yomi turn out to be true.<br /> <br /> &quot;Black Earth Boy's ultimate fate remains a point of contetion among the Laughing Rainbow. Beyond the scandalous rumors of Thousand Crane Mother's melancholy, there is the question of whether her student and fellow saint has returned to the Hundred Clouds or fallen into the Mouth of Yomi&quot;<br /> <br /> So if really Black Earth Boy survived the cataclysm, maybe by falling in the Yomi portal the Bodhisattvas opened, then the prophecy would be true, because while he hasn't defeated Ravana he has survived him, winning the battle as only survivor of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> its still something he did single handedly. </div> </div> </div>Yeah sure, killing a demon queen while you are mating with her and she's distracted and she's giving you her essence is the same that killing her in fight, right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keeping in mind Saulot apparently worked REALLY hard to try and become a Yama King and.. didn't get there. Well according to the Transylvania chronicles. </div> </div> </div>No he didn't.<br /> In the Ivory Tablets he doesn't says that he wants to become Yama King, he says he wants to become Demon Emperor.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;If I am accursed, then let me be great in my depravity. I shall gain all I can for myself. I shall help to move the Great Wheel toward collapse and I shall smite the dreary realm with an iron fist and whips of fire. No longer shall I care what my father or my brethren want. I shall be hieddn in my plans and circumspect in my dealings with all. But they must not suspect my hand's stirring. Let them squabble among themselves and vie for position. Let them believe they struggle to reach ascendancy.<b> In the end , as the wheel turns and drakness covers all, I shall sit atop the throne of destiny, stronger than they, stronger than Cain, stronger than she who gave us our powers - perhaps even stronger than the god who originally cursed the First.</b><br /> Then I shall rule and if it be that the wheel must turn again, I shall again transform myself and ride it back to the top again. I shall have my vengeance for Caine's thoughtless curse that he laid upon me. For one thing I now kow that others consider not: Should the Wheel of the Ages reach the top once more, even in its apparent perfection, I shall linger like a blot upon pure sand. The whell shall one night turn again&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No mention of Yama King,<br /> The pondering is consistent whit him wanting to became the Demon Emperor, not a Yama King, since he mention the turning of the wheel (and so the advent of the Sixth Age) and the wish to become greater than God, which is what we are told the Demon Emperor will be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just compare this<br /> <br /> KoTE, page 8<br /> &quot;During the Sixth Age, the wheels of matter and spirit will cease any semblance of alignment. <b>The August Personage of jade, already estranged from the Ten Thousand Things of creation, will leave its throne. In the August Personage's place will rise a Demon Emperor, to reign supreme over the Sixth Age as the August Personage ruled over the First</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Saulot<br /> &quot; In the end , a<b>s the wheel turns and drakness covers all, I shall sit atop the throne of destiny, stronger than they, stronger than Cain, stronger than she who gave us our powers - perhaps even stronger than the god who originally cursed the First</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And again<br /> <br /> KoTE<br /> &quot;But just as <b>the Sixth Age is prophesied to come, it is prophesied to pass. The struggle will cease, and there will be a great stillness, and those few creatures left alive will emerge from hidden places. Then will arrive a Seventh Age, a little better than the Sixth</b>; <b>and an Eighth, a little better still; and so the Cycle will once more turn until it reaches the 12th Age, which is also the First Age,</b> and the Ten Thousand Things of matter and spirit will become one once more. Or so the sutras say. Few, in this Age, have sufficient hope to believe.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Saulot<br /> <br /> &quot;Then <b>I shall rule and if it be that the wheel must turn again, I shall again transform myself and ride it back to the top again. </b>I shall have my vengeance for Caine's thoughtless curse that he laid upon me.<b> For one thing I now kow that others consider not: Should the Wheel of the Ages reach the top once more, even in its apparent perfection, I shall linger like a blot upon pure sand. The whell shall one night turn again</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> They are really saying just the same things, indeed it's almost a paraphrase.<br /> <br /> He is talking about becoming Demon Emperor, not Yama King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-08-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:15:01-07:00","id":965552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965539#post965539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it was not a portion, it was the most of it, only Ragnarok command didn't answered the call of Aleph, beside that all the Technocracy answered the call for the final war.<br /> And no, the ratio enlightened agents to Un-enlightened agents is 1:5<br /> <br /> Page 78<br /> <br /> &quot;General Aleph commands 4000 Enlightened Technocrats, 8000 extraordinary Citizens and 20000 sleeper soldiers. <b>He has no other reserves .<br /> This is an all-or nothing fight to which he commits every Technocrat that he can muster</b>. Many of them are scientist, not warriors: dozens are freshly conditioned from the internment camps. Ragnarok Command's amalgams refuse to participate so they can dispatch aid to Sleepers and defend against threats from the Deep Universe.<br /> Twenty ARC-2 helicopters, four Aurora transatmospherich fighters, 1000 hardsuits and 500 HIT marks are at their disposal, along dozens of conventional veichles and satellite support.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, Guide to the Technocracy, page 95<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, the appearance of overwhelming power is useful to the Union,<b> but the fact is, there just aren't enough Enlightened agents and allied citizens to exert that sort of power over all of society.</b> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>With perhaps a few thousand Enlightened ops worldwide and four or five times that number in un-Enlightened assistance,</b></span> the Technocracy just doesn't have the manpower to be everywhere at once. Even the Enlightened Science used to monitor trouble spots has to be maintained by someone. Since those monitors are just as susceptible to human error as anyone else, quite a bit can fall outside the Technocracy's field of vision&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is consistent with the numbers given in Ascension by the way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, please source for the &quot;tens of thousands of Technocrats in this world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because both sources are now largely obsoleted. The same book states Tradition could muster MAXIMUM 3,000 Mages, including Hollow Ones and various Crafts. And that simply makes no sense whatsoever, if not in the case of writers assumed one million per one Awakened ratio as default setup.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, revised CBs explicitly state that there are twenty Sympathizers per one Extraordinary Citizen, and twenty Extraordinary Citizen per one Enlightened Technocrats.<br /> <br /> In addition, Progenitor CB gives us blissfully concrete, credible ratio : &quot;Naturally, the core of the Progenitors are Enlightened scientists, though we only make up three percent of the Convention (counting those who draw a Progenitor paycheck and work for us without knowing it). A further eleven percent falls into the Exceptional category, as able lab assistants and other roles working next to Inspired Science.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also clearly mentions that &quot;three percent&quot; is including quite a lot of non-aligned independent Enlightened Scientists. And remember the fact that Progenitors are the most reclusive, withdrawn Convention and have fewest field agents, and quite likely use the smallest number of un-Enlightened personnel among the Technocratic Conventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-08-2016, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T02:03:28-07:00","id":965560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965552#post965552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because both sources are now largely obsoleted. The same book states Tradition could muster MAXIMUM 3,000 Mages, including Hollow Ones and various Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>3000 thousands mages and 5000 sorcerers.<br /> But it doesn't says that this is all they had.<br /> <br /> While it is stated that Aleph mustered all the forces avaiable the 3000 mages is what the player can gather in a week work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that simply makes no sense whatsoever, if not in the case of writers assumed one million per one Awakened ratio as default setup. </div> </div> </div>No sorry, even if we assume the 1:150000 your numbers are unlikely.<br /> <br /> Between in 2004 there where something less than 6.5 billions people in the world.<br /> <br /> 6.4 billions/150k=42k mages in the world.<br /> <br /> 42 mages that you must divide between Orphans, Traditions,Crafts, Technocracy,Marauders and Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Even if we use modern numbers we get a 49k mages in the world, that must be divided between all factions.<br /> <br /> Had the writers assumed the 1 mage for 1000k sleepers ratio then there should be 6400 mages in the world, and just by adding Traditions + Technocracy we get 7000, and we are still not counting Mara,Nepha,Orphans and so on, so they didn't used the 1:1000k ratio.<br /> <br /> And the Technocracy is vastly outnumbered by the Traditions, and we know that to defeat the Mara Technocracy and Traditions must unite, so we can assume that Mara have more or less the same strenght of Traditions and Technocray put togheter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, revised CBs explicitly state that there are twenty Sympathizers per one Extraordinary Citizen, and twenty Extraordinary Citizen per one Enlightened Technocrats. </div> </div> </div>By revised CB what book are you meaning?<br /> <br /> Convention book?<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Syndicate and NWO revised now and except the fact that now there are much more extraordinary citizens and sympathizers than before I can't find anything.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is sure is that recruitment trend of the extraordinary citizens has increased 12 times more since a decade before.<br /> But I can't find anything about this tens of thousands of Enlightened Citizens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> <br /> I found this from Malcolm Sheppard, which is pretty clear and exaustive on the topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Malcolm Sheppard</b>, on 02 Nov 2006 - 20:43, said:<br /> <br /> Waaaay too many Nephandi in that breakdown. To be Nephandus you have to enter the cauls, not just be bad. Plus, they have the smallest number of canonical NPCs. I'd put their numbers at less than 5%. There are also probably slightly fewer Orphans, since the Traditions really are pretty good at assimilating mystics. The Crafts have been beaten down by the Technocracy, to boot, but we'll be opstimistic with both. Plus, there are quite a lot of Technocrats.<br /> <br /> So I'd say:<br /> <br /> Traditions- 40%<br /> Technocracy- 40%<br /> Marauders- 6%<br /> Nephandi- 4%<br /> Crafts- 10%<br /> Orphans- 10%<br /> <br /> <br /> Canonically, the largest are:<br /> 1) OoH (they recruit more than any other Trad and the House structure lets them incorporate many different styles)<br /> 2) Akashic Brotherhood (they recruit less than many Trads but have the largest population base to draw from).<br /> <br /> After that, the Dreamspeakers and Celestial Chorus are supposed to be pretty large and diverse. The Verbena trail slightly behind these two. The Ecstatics are probably about the size of the Verbena.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether are probably about equal size and next largest after the trads above.<br /> <br /> The Euthanatos are supposed to be smaller than the other Traditions.<br /> <br /> To make some hard choices and put it all in a list, with breakdowns the ranking from largest to smallest would be:<br /> <br /> 1) Order of Hermes 15%<br /> 2) Akashic Brotherhood 14%<br /> 3) Celestial Chorus 13%<br /> 4) Dreamspeakers 12%<br /> 5) Verbena 11%*<br /> 6) Cult of Ecstacy 11%*<br /> 7) Virtual Adepts 9%*<br /> 8) Sons of Ether 9%*<br /> 9) Euthanatos 6%<br /> <br /> *The higher ranks Trad may have a fractionally higher number of members.<br /> <br /> Bill Bridges revised the numbers during his run, which were originally 1 mage per million or 1 per 500,000, to 1 per 200,000 ro 250,000. Let's make it an even 30,000 Awakened mages in the world.<br /> <br /> That means the Traditions have 12,000 members.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1) Order of Hermes: 1800<br /> 2) Akashic Brotherhood: 1680<br /> 3) Celestial Chorus: 1560<br /> 4) Dreamspeakers: 1440<br /> 5) Verbena: 1320<br /> 6) Cult of Ecstacy: 1320<br /> 7) Virtual Adepts: 1080<br /> 8) Sons of Ether: 1080<br /> 9) Euthanatos: 720<br /> <br /> Breakdown by rank makes most Tradition mages Disciples, with a significant narrowing at Adept rank thanks to attrition and fewer apprentices because they tend to die more easily and because magic is generally in decline. So:<br /> <br /> Apprentice 15% -- 1800 Traditionalists<br /> Initiate: 20% -- 2400 Traditionalists<br /> Disciple: 50% -- 6000 Traditionalists<br /> Adept: 13% -- 1560 Traditionalists<br /> Master: 1.9% -- 228 Traditionalists?<br /> Archmaster: .1% 12 Traditionalists?<br /> <br /> Ranks will tend to break statistical predictions as the increase. For instance, thr Masters and archmasters are probably doled out more evenly that Tradition numbers would suggest. By contrast, the Technocracy probably has a fairly strict pyramidial distribution, with the fewest on top and as many as half being &quot;Apprentices.&quot;</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">So the real ratio is between 1:200k and 1:250k<br /> <br /> 40% Technocracy,40% Traditions, 10% Orphans, 10% Crafts and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if we use modern population stats we have 29,6K or 37k mages around the world.<br /> <br /> And Technocracy might have between 11,8k or 15k</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Lol, total factors adds to 110%.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-08-2016, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T03:11:54-07:00","id":965575,"title":"","content":"Who has more information?<br /> <br /> This isn't about who is more powerful. it's about who can ID targets better and faster than the other side. When you have two glass cannons, it's not about who shoots first it's about who shoots better.<br /> <br /> Both sides can can play the espionage game pretty well. But I believe the Mages have some of the best investigation tools at their disposal. It takes very little investment for a new mage to be able to ping other supers. and be a PI. But it is an investment for vamps to do so.<br /> <br /> That being said vamps have a lot more out of the box combat tools. For Mages its an investment to be combat focused.<br /> <br /> Once the vamps find a target, they can swarm pretty quickly and over run him. but mages can more consistently find targets and plan the encounter, which they'll win because they'll plan. It's the Batman V Superman argument. In chaos situations Supes wins. In order Bats wins. Thrown in Fate/Time Risk assessments and chaos becomes orderly chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:17:01-07:00","id":965631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965560#post965560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3000 thousands mages and 5000 sorcerers.<br /> But it doesn't says that this is all they had.<br /> <br /> While it is stated that Aleph mustered all the forces avaiable the 3000 mages is what the player can gather in a week work.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Three thousands, at the MOST, in the best case scenario. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965560#post965560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No sorry, even if we assume the 1:150000 your numbers are unlikely.<br /> <br /> Between in 2004 there where something less than 6.5 billions people in the world.<br /> <br /> 6.4 billions/150k=42k mages in the world.<br /> <br /> 42 mages that you must divide between Orphans, Traditions,Crafts, Technocracy,Marauders and Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Even if we use modern numbers we get a 49k mages in the world, that must be divided between all factions.<br /> <br /> Had the writers assumed the 1 mage for 1000k sleepers ratio then there should be 6400 mages in the world, and just by adding Traditions + Technocracy we get 7000, and we are still not counting Mara,Nepha,Orphans and so on, so they didn't used the 1:1000k ratio.<br /> <br /> And the Technocracy is vastly outnumbered by the Traditions, and we know that to defeat the Mara Technocracy and Traditions must unite, so we can assume that Mara have more or less the same strenght of Traditions and Technocray put togheter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Which source declares that the Technocracy is vastly outnumbered by the Tradition, and Marauders have more or less the same strength of Traditions and Technocracy put together?<br /> <br /> By the way, I have always supposed that the Technocracy gets lion's share of the Awakened and Sorcerer populations, because when considering recruitment pool disparity between the Union and other factions, it is only reasonable end result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965560#post965560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By revised CB what book are you meaning?<br /> <br /> Convention book?<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Syndicate and NWO revised now and except the fact that now there are much more extraordinary citizens and sympathizers than before I can't find anything.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is sure is that recruitment trend of the extraordinary citizens has increased 12 times more since a decade before.<br /> But I can't find anything about this tens of thousands of Enlightened Citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I referred Progenitors Convention book, not Syndicate or NWO. End of story.<br /> <br /> And if you carefully perused the NWO book, you should have noticed the statement that Extraordinary Citizen/S</span></span></span>ympathizers ratio is 1:20. And you have to know that Enlightened Citizen/Extraordinary Citizen ratio is more or less same and there exist lots and lots of Technocracy-sponsored, but officially non-aligned Extraordinary Citizen. In addition, Syndicate CB explicitly states Union has, and runs, literally <i>tens of thousands</i> Constructs across the globe. Technocratic Union is truly vast organization, and it only fits their operation budget, scale of operations and scope of power/influence projection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965560#post965560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT<br /> <br /> I found this from Malcolm Sheppard, which is pretty clear and exaustive on the topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">So the real ratio is between 1:200k and 1:250k<br /> <br /> 40% Technocracy,40% Traditions, 10% Orphans, 10% Crafts and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if we use modern population stats we have 29,6K or 37k mages around the world.<br /> <br /> And Technocracy might have between 11,8k or 15k</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> <br /> Lol, total factors adds to 110%.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fully aware of that chart.<br /> <br /> However, FTLV explicitly attests like this : &quot;One of the first challenges a Storyteller faces when creating a Mage setting is deciding just how many mages exist among the masses of Sleepers. White Wolf uses a rough rule of thumb of one mage per 150,000 people, though this should be readily broken in order to promote story.&quot; and I applied it into my estimation.<br /> <br /> And at any rate, you have got it wrong all along. There are tens of thousands of Enlightened Technocrats operating on the Earth, and each Convention possesses thousands of Enlightened Scientists. Face the truth and admit your error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-08-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:24:30-07:00","id":965762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965631#post965631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am fully aware of that chart.<br /> <br /> However, FTLV explicitly attests like this : &quot;One of the first challenges a Storyteller faces when creating a Mage setting is deciding just how many mages exist among the masses of Sleepers. White Wolf uses a rough rule of thumb of one mage per 150,000 people, though this should be readily broken in order to promote story.&quot; and <b>I applied it into my estimation</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you made up numbers while someone else is using numbers supplied by one of the lead writers of the game (which is considered the default numbers to use in a canon argument). You can stop the argument now, you two aren't having the same conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is exactly the kind of shit that gets threads like these closed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:32:03-07:00","id":965991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=965762#post965762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you made up numbers while someone else is using numbers supplied by one of the lead writers of the game (which is considered the default numbers to use in a canon argument). You can stop the argument now, you two aren't having the same conversation.<br /> <br /> This is exactly the kind of shit that gets threads like these closed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain why I have &quot;made up numbers&quot;? I directly cited from the Fallen Tower Las Vegas. I genuinely cannot comprehend meaning of your words, or what are you intending to say. If you have read this thread, you have to know that I have not contrived concrete, defined numbers; I just spoke tens of thousands, and like I said, that is roughly same figure regardless 1:200k or 1:150k.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-08-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:55:39-07:00","id":966002,"title":"","content":"Estimated = made up a rough number, while Undead Rabbit was going by the solid numbers given by one of the lead writers. You two aren't having the same conversation because you aren't starting from a common point of reference. This in turn is leading into a circular argument which gets tiresome to read. I'm not trying to be insulting, but I am being blunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:46:58-07:00","id":966042,"title":"","content":"The world ends.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what more needs be said.<br /> <br /> I do think there'd at least be an attempt at a worldwide solar blanketing using power satellites, given its 'relative success' with the Zapathasura debacle. That ought to have interesting implications for what the post-apocalyptic setting remaining looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:35:37-07:00","id":966245,"title":"","content":"Some of the problems I'd foresee coming up that I haven't really seen mentioned also heavily depend on which splat would be favored. Outside of directly Fire and Sunlight related effects, are most other magiks going to be very effective against Cainites? From a Mage perspective, &quot;Lightningbolts&quot; might deal Aggravated Damage, but from the Vampire perspective they probably deal very minimal Lethal damage. Just as an example. Even dropping a building on them supercharged with Magik is probably going to have a very different effect on a Cainite depending on if you favor Mage or Vampire for how to handle it.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue, that if Mages are immune to Paradox, lets also just go ahead and assume that all Cainites are immune to Sunlight. That's pretty close to fair. Just saying.<br /> It's also one of those very odd things, where it really depends on which game you favor, as in the VtM perspective, most Vampires DO actually cause Paradox backlash for Mages, but there are a few notable exceptions, like Malkavians due to their insane and chaotic nature, and the Tremere who have an understanding of true Magik. Anyway, from this point onwards, we are all going to assume that either Mages do have to deal with Paradox as normal or Vampires are just outright immune to Sunlight, and we will leave the question as to if Vampires can cause Paradox for Mages up in the air for if you favor Mage or Vampire.<br /> <br /> There seems to be a few odd assumptions made that I'm not sure are accurate. For example that Vampires can't access space, other realms, or much outside of the planet earth or the physical world. That's not very true. It's less important to VtM to go into much detail about the Astral Plane, the Umbra(s), etc. . . just because to most VtM games, it's not that important. Vampire doesn't revolve around that much. However, Auspex, Necromancy, Protean all allow for access to the other realms, which are generally speaking, all connected, and are not terribly uncommon powers. Thaumaturgy as well.<br /> <br /> We also seem to assume that Mages somehow get free access to things like Nukes, but Vampires do not, which doesn't seem to fly. For example, Marcus Vitel basically infiltrated Washing DC for the exact purpose of getting access and control of the US's Nukes. The Mages might have a nasty surprise coming their way when they try to pull that card, only to find out that much of their arsenal isn't actually at their disposal after al, but is instead going to be used against them, or if we assume that both Mages and Vampires have influence and &quot;control&quot; of the key world leaders, that many of those weapons are suddenly, unforeseeably, taken off the table completely for BOTH sides.<br /> <br /> On the idea of creating Rituals/Paths for AntiMage things, I'd argue that both sides are partially correct, and at best it really does come down to splat favoritism. It is possible to create a new Path and Rituals for basically anything. However, doing so is NEVER an on the spot thing. Even in the new Anarchs Unleashed book, it talks about how Punk Magic, (sort of an improvised variety aimed at specifically trying to do on the spot effects) is very difficult, limited, and a time consuming process up front. The fact that the Tremere did so in a lot of their backstory is just one of those things that doesn't make any sense and we just have to handwave logic under the rung because the devs wanted to have the Tremere in the game no matter what.. However, all that being said, we can probably also reasonably assume that the Tremere specifically went out of their way to develop some, at least basic, AnitMage Thaumaturgy as their first real battle was against other Mages as they tried to establish themselves, and as cunning right bastards, it makes no sense whatsoever that they would have left themselves o vulnerable against probably the single on threat they actually knew about in detail.<br /> <br /> Ravnos' death was literally a plot device. He (she) had just woken up, and fighting during the daytime, SHOULD have been extremely limited in Dice Pools, but still manages to nearly survive going head to head with a Werewolf Pack, Wraiths, KotE elders, and Mages, at the same time or one after another. At best, we have an example of some rules being ignored in favor of telling a story and making a point, but the issue(s) is that the different points it makes say some very different things. Ravnos did have Fortitude as a Clan Discipline, and (if we assume) that means it was maxed out to 10 dots (or more???), it makes it, at least on the surface feasible that it took all of that to BARELY put him down. Except that well, he shouldn't have had access to his full power for multiple reasons, (fighting during the day handicaps Vampires to the Path Rating, which was unlikely at 10 and probably closer to 1-3, he was already weak from not feeding and just waking up, and confused and disorientated). End result, the Story overrules EVERYTHING else, but since Antis and Oracles are not in this, it really doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Then we come to the issue of if Counter Magic even works on most Disciplines, and secondarily if Mage's other intrinsic ability to alter reality off screen affects Vampires at all. This can also lead to the overarching issue if Mage's, ANY MAGE, can override &quot;God&quot;. In Vampire unquestionably no. In Mage, arguably the entire point. Just for the sake of argument here, by &quot;God&quot; I'm including both the J-C and Noddist version as well as the basic fundamental principles of the universe that Mages have not universally altered such as gravity. Once again, it's entirerly based upon which game line the ST favors over the other.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a strong implication, or even taken as fact, that Mages know all, and are fully prepared, while Cainites are not. I'm not sure that that is very accurate. While in general, Cainites are probably going to be less specifically designed to fight a war against Mages than the reverse, that would probably only matter very significantly if one group was attacking the other from surprise. Since the basic assumption seems to be that both sides are pretty aware of the theoretical war, that Vampires would also start pulling out all the stop, which leads to a bit of a problem for Mages, even if we assume that both groups have exerted a great deal of influence across the mortal/mundane world, politics, technology, etc. . . and that is that Vampires probably have a hell of a lot more personal experience with fighting/surviving Mages and other creatures than Mages do Vampires. As immortals, they just have a lot more experience they can call upon, even if it's less directly applicable, it should have a lot of crossover potential. There is also the fact that things like the Inquisition didn't just target Vampires, and at least according to VtM was actually much, much more of a threat towards Mages and Sorcerers (and innocents) that it was against Vampires. There is also the fact that even the Technocracy really has minimal &quot;true&quot; information about Vampires (and any other Supernatural being), more studying the vampire from the Mage's Antagonist perspective (a watered down and inaccurate version) rather than actual Cainites. This is also true for Vampires, though, but I'd think that it's much less of a hindrance for VtM than it is for MtA.<br /> <br /> And finally, one last assumption I'm not sure is very good, is that it's not Mages vs the Tremere, but rather that there are also a lot of other Clans out there too who might have all sorts of nifty powers and tactics that might screw with Mages. An earthmelded Gangrel shouldn't be detectable by Mages at all (or at least not by most methods they would think to use), and many Mages might have an issue doing anything to a cloud of fog. Fortitude is also a pretty common Discipline, but is also one that is 1.) always on and 2.) pretty all inclusive. Technology, even boosted by Magick probably doesn't do a thing against Obfuscate, which doesn't turn you invisible, and isn't an illusion, but rather directly affects the minds of everyone, even after the fact to simply not accept that the user was even there. Mage's probably have little defense against a small group of Nosferatu that just walk in undetected, call on a small swarm of crows, and then unleash their Beast on a Mage who should then loose all access to magick and rational thought, and probably go freaking crazy and attack anything near it that moves.<br /> <br /> So, with all that in mind, I'm more inclined to say more likely it would go to Mages, but I wouldn't count Cainites out so quickly unless you continue to just favor Mage's rules, themes, and truths over Vampire's and everyone else's (seeing a trend here on that account), and then it's really not even a question. If, on the other hand, it is more of a unbiased thought exercise, Vampires might surprise you with the long game, that thing they excel at. There is also the little fact that you literally have to exterminate every single Vampire in existence for Mages to truly win, because even one Vampire can repopulate the earth, and if we also assume that Caine and the 3rd Gen stay out, that does mean right off the bat Mages automatically fail at achieving overall victory and just a stalemate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:02:50-07:00","id":967478,"title":"","content":"Technocracy could create the best anti-vampire gadgets, like ultraviolet bombs, poisons or biological weapons. To null supernatural powers by enemy monsters is coincidental magic. <br /> <br /> My suggestion to get ideas is the book and teleserie &quot;the strain&quot;, the movies &quot;ultraviolet&quot;, &quot;daybreakers&quot; and &quot;the breed&quot; (2001 film, with Adrian Paul and Bai Ling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:16:08-07:00","id":967491,"title":"","content":"Vampires are immune to ultraviolet weapons, you need the sun, the true sun to hurt them.<br /> And they are immune to poisons and biological weapons, they can be infected only through tainted blood, but even there they just need to &quot;burn&quot; the infected blood points to heal.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, nullyfing supernatural powers is not coincidental, it's vulgar because Vampires are part of the consensus, so by nullyfing their powers you are going against the consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:21:06-07:00","id":967495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967491#post967491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are immune to ultraviolet weapons, you need the sun, the true sun to hurt them.<br /> And they are immune to poisons and biological weapons,<br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, nulling supernatural powers is not coincidental, it's vulgar because Vampires are part of the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you don't. Because the Ultraviolet weapons are made with True Magic which tells the Static rules that vampires run off of to go die in a ditch. It's a prime 2 effect to make a gun do aggravated damage to ANYTHING. Vampires included.<br /> <br /> It's coincidental unless there's a sleeper with an unusual amount of vampire lore around. Much like Rocket boots are coincidental until you fly past a physics professor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:41:08-07:00","id":967569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967495#post967495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No you don't. Because the Ultraviolet weapons are made with True Magic which tells the Static rules that vampires run off of to go die in a ditch. It's a prime 2 effect to make a gun do aggravated damage to ANYTHING. Vampires included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means that it doesn't hurt vampires because its &quot;sun like&quot; but just beacuse you infused prime in it,a thing you could do even with a pencil.<br /> <br /> So you'd have this ultraviolet weapon that can do the same thing a common 38 infused with prime 2 can do, woa!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's coincidental unless there's a sleeper with an unusual amount of vampire lore around. Much like Rocket boots are coincidental until you fly past a physics professor. </div> </div> </div>Nope, Vampires and their powers are part of the static consensus, there is nothing Technocracy can do about it, so if you are disrupting their powers you are disrupting the static consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:58:22-07:00","id":967579,"title":"","content":"Format Space. Vampires no longer conform with that static consensus. Any other questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:00:35-07:00","id":967582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967579#post967579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Format Space. Vampires no longer conform with that static consensus. Any other questions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Source so I can read the rules of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because if it works like the other time Aleph already explained you why this won't work<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/951625-why-the-vampires-werebeasts-wraiths-spirits-fae-changelings-demons-mummies-etc-are-existing?p=955341#post955341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have made a fatal mistake in your calculations Enginseer...Earth, with all and it's vampires, IT'S PART OF CONVENTIONAL SPACE, as per P.55 of VE Revised. Your Format Reality ain't going to do anything, since all it does it's transforming an area into Conventional Space, which the Earth already is (as per P. 86 of VE Revised).<br /> <br /> You have a fundamental misconception. You take the letter of rotes at face value, seeing the trees, but not the forest.<br /> <br /> Sure, the wording of the procedure says that &quot;creatures that don't follow technocratic paradigm sicken and die&quot;. But that already happens in Earth, it's just that some creatures are immune to this effect.<br /> They are always immune, they don't get sick and die in a Technocratic Reality Zone (which all cities are). They don't get sick and die in outer space (undistinguishable from Formatted Space, as creating that sort of enviroment it's exactly what Format Space does). They don't get sick and die in Realms.<br /> Format Space merely reproduces an effect that Earth has, and does so in a way that suits Technocratic Belief.<br /> <br /> Think about these paragraphs, carefully, and you will see that I'm right:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Earth it's already Formatted, in the sense that VE use the term...The spell reproduces the effect that the masses probes already have on the universe, it transforms a part of the Umbra into Conventional Space. And it conveniently transforms it into a Technocratic Reality Zone that accepts their Procedures (which it's something that has never affected vampires). A Pericarp get's erected (like a Gauntlet, like in Realms), and magical creatures that don't conform to the paradigm sicken and die...just as happened in the real world, as effect of Reality Zones...assuming that it will affect creatures that are normally immune to this effect, whitout being stated directly that this happens...just because some (purposely) unproven theories about why supernaturals can use magic without Paradox...You're assuming a lot. Werewolves don't get sick and die by exposure to a hostile Horizon Realm or Technocratic lab. This thing has never happened and never will happen, Mages may have theories about why this is that way, but it's in the end, purely a metaphysical reasoning on your part, and one that it's supposed to be decided by the ST...<br /> <br /> What you're suggesting it's not only impossible, but preposterous in the face of what the spell actualy does.<br /> That's a much better reason to never have attempted it, don't you think?<br /> <br /> You may want to reconsider your metaphysics...<br /> <br /> And DimSci and Spirit were litteraly the same Sphere until Revised...Thus, one could counter the other. It's a bit weird to think that one can't counter the other anymore, if it isn't explicitly stated anywhere. Technocratic Spheres are a variation on the normal ones, thus, they're related at a fundamental level, they affect the same fundamental aspects of reality. I can see one countering the other, and I bet that Phil would say the same if asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:20:53-07:00","id":967590,"title":"","content":"Ahhh yeah...Void Engineers Revised, just as I tought.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Format Space (Correspondence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Dimensional Science \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> Void Engineers prefer to regulate<b> extraterrestrial space </b>the easy way: by creating safe models of its phenomena for ordinary citizens to absorb, internalize and impose on the target region. Human minds collapse a region\u2019s dangerous possibilities into manageable Conventional Space. But sometimes, the Convention doesn\u2019t have time to wait for the Masses to send crude probes, and PDC scientists step in with brute force and mathematics. Void Engineers deploy quantum-entangled virtual particle emitters linked to an AI array that models the target area as it should be: obedient to the Anthropic Principle and the Technocratic laws of physics. Due to the prodigious scientific knowledge required, Format Space is normally undertaken by two PDC experts directing a team of assistants. Their players must define at least four reference points where virtual particle generators have been deployed\u2014this is enough to affect a tetrahedral volume. The players must score enough successes to make Correspondence contact with each of them (see p. 83 for revised Correspondence ranges.) The team\u2019s players must then score Duration successes, as per p. 209 of Mage: the Ascension Revised. After that, successes generated by their efforts may impose the following effects: \u2022 Each success raises the Gauntlet by 1 for Reality Deviants, and decreases it by 1 for Technocrats, to a maximum rating of 10 and minimum rating of 0, respectively. In a region outside of Earth, this Gauntlet is called a pericarp, and erects itself even if it didn\u2019t exist before. Pericarps do not manifest the Dimensional Anomaly. \u2022 Five successes render all Reality Deviant Procedures vulgar, even if they would normally be coincidental, while all Technocratic Procedures become coincidental. The only exceptions to this consist of certain Procedures that are vulgar throughout the Tellurian\u2014 including \u201cFormat Space.\u201d If this feature is chosen, material, living organisms that cannot be accepted by Technocratic science becomes what Traditionalists call \u201cthaumivores.\u201d Without one point of Primal Energy per day, they will sicken and die, or fade across dimensional boundaries to become para-material EDEs. \u2022 Five successes force the mundane physics of the region to conform to the Consensus. Hyperspatial \u201cether\u201d turns into hard vacuum, for example. Due to this Procedure\u2019s extreme difficulty, Extraordinary Devices capable of performing some or all of its functions are highly sought after. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And so, no, sorry, it's not gonna work, Aleph explanation should show you why.<br /> You can't format something that is already formatted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:03:36-07:00","id":967611,"title":"","content":"Alephs Explanation is stupid, no offense intended to Aleph. Because the Earth ISN'T formatted or else every traditional casting would be vulgar. Which they aren't. The Gauntlet would be 10 at all times. Which it isn't. And the fact that void engineers use their procedures IN SPACE does not mean they cannot be used on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:18:02-07:00","id":967619,"title":"","content":"Nope, Aleph explanation is quite complete and, I dare say, it's even obvious.<br /> <br /> Coincidental magick, Night-folks and so on are ALREADY in the Consensus, it is widely explained through several books, you can't render consensual something that it is already consensual.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you'd show a poor understanding of the metaphysic of Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;by creating safe models of its phenomena for ordinary citizens to absorb, internalize and impose on the target region. <b>Human minds collapse a region\u2019s dangerous possibilities into manageable Conventional Space</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The Horizons<br /> Horizons arise due to the limits of sentient reality computation. The Biospheric Horizon at the upper edges of Earth\u2019s atmosphere represents the extent of non- intelligent life\u2019s influence. The <b>Spatial Horizon marks the edge of the Masses\u2019 computational reach, and the end of Conventional Space</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Conventional Space<br /> <b>The mundane world is the best-known example of Conventional Space, where the laws of nature function largely as the Masses expect. A strong dimensional Gauntlet separates<br /> incompatible instances of reality. Conventional spacecraft contend with vacuum and radiation.</b> In this dimension, Yuri Gagarin looked down from his capsule, and Neil Armstrong took his small step on the Moon.&quot;<br /> <br /> And since the Vampire do not live beyond the Gauntlet they already LIVE in conventional space and so they already ARE part of it, because they are not &quot;incompatible instances of reality&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So no, this rote makes Unconventional space conventional, but earth is already conventional, the only unconventional part of it it's the umbra.<br /> <br /> Even more it's obvious that this rote has been devised for Space exploration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even more, proving your lack of understanding of the setting , you did not take this in account.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b> If this feature is chosen, material, living organisms that cannot be accepted by Technocratic science becomes what Traditionalists call \u201cthaumivores.\u201d Without one point of Primal Energy per day, they will sicken and die, or fade across dimensional boundaries to become para-material EDEs</b>. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires are ALREADY thaumivores, it's the whole matter about vampire and mages, vampires eat blood and so they eat quintessence, and yes, they even consume one blood point (primal energy) per day.<br /> This because they ALREADY live in a Conventional Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:27:21-07:00","id":967622,"title":"","content":"Explain then why a location upon which Format Space has used, allows for Plasma cannons, a highly vulgar device in any other circumstance, to be used freely as a coincidental thing? Explain why no matter how coincidental it would normally be, Traditionalist magic is now ALWAYS VULGAR.<br /> <br /> And Vampires are actually the REVERSE of Thaumivores. They PRODUCE quintessence far in excess of what they need to consume.<br /> <br /> You're acting like it's an on off switch. It's not. There are grades involved. This is somewhat clear in the effects of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:42:04-07:00","id":967627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967622#post967622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain then why a location upon which Format Space has used, allows for Plasma cannons, a highly vulgar device in any other circumstance, to be used freely as a coincidental thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No sorry, you clearly do not undersand what are you talking about and what are you reading.<br /> <br /> Plasma cannons do not became coincidental, what becames coincidental are Technocratic rotes that in the Umbra would be VULGAR.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> M20 corebook<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Coincidental Magick<br /> As a general rule, all forms of mystic magick are coincidental<br /> in the Umbra as a whole. Certain Realms, however, may be<br /> more or less attuned to certain paradigms, accepting one type<br /> of magick as coincidental (say, High Ritual Magick) while<br /> rejecting others (like weird science or martial arts) as vulgar.<br /> In the High Umbra, technomagick tends to be as<br /> coincidental as mystic magick is. Science and technology, after<br /> all, are products of rarefied thought.<b> In the Middle Umbra\u2019s<br /> Spirit Wilds, on the other hand, technomagick is often vulgar,<br /> and fails completely in the Aetherian Reaches. </b>Again, certain<br /> Realms flip that around, recognizing technomagick (or at least<br /> certain forms of it, anyway) as coincidental while rejecting<br /> mystic practices as vulgar.<br /> <b>As for the Low Umbra, techomagick tends to be vulgar<br /> there, while primal, ritual, and sacred magick is coincidental.</b><br /> Perhaps the disastrous effects of the spirit nuke added a<br /> spectacular Paradox Effect on top of the usual conflagration\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's the point, the rote is a way to TAME UMBRA, and UMBRA ALONE, why do you think they talk about the Gauntlet? For the sake of it? No, because it's an UMBRA based rote.<br /> <br /> So no if you use Format space on New York your plasma gun is not gonna be coincidental.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What is gonna happening is that if you use it on the middle umbra of new york the magic that you, with a techonological paradigm, are going to use there will be coincidental,while the mystic magic is gonna be vulgar. And no, your plasma cannon is still vulgar because it's the classic thing that it's vulgar &quot;throughout the Tellurian&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise explain: why Technocracy do not use this on Earth to win the Ascension war?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Jeez, do you even understand what are you reading?<br /> <br /> &quot;Five successes force the mundane physics of the<br /> region to conform to the Consensus. Hyperspatial<br /> \u201cether\u201d turns into hard vacuum, for example.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where in hell does not mundane physics work on our Planet? Let me help you: IN THE UMBRA<br /> <br /> <br /> Because, if you have forgotten it, the whole Void Engineers thing is about UMBRA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again<br /> &quot;But<br /> sometimes, the Convention doesn\u2019t have time to wait for<br /> the Masses to send crude probes, and PDC scientists step in<br /> with brute force and mathematics.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why should you ever send a CRUDE PROBES on Earth?<br /> Why should the PDC, which if you don't remember are the PAN DIMENSIONAL CORPS &quot;stepping in&quot; on Earth?<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's see what PDC does<br /> <br /> &quot;The Void Engineers have delved further into the Universe than any other human beings. On the forefront of that effort is the Pan-Dimensional Corps. <b>Its operations take it well past the Spatial Horizon and out into the Deep Universe, establishing beachheads of varying sizes in locales around our galactic volume. Closer to home, the PDC assists the other Conventions, particularly the EFD, in surveillance and security operations in the Near Universe.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh! PDC is involved in UMBRA, how strange.<br /> <br /> This because Void Engineers have another corps for earth: the Earth Frontier Division<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, let's recap.<br /> <br /> <br /> This rotes<br /> <br /> -Makes unconventional space (umbra) conventional (not-umbra)<br /> -It raises the gauntlet (which separates umbra from mundane)<br /> -It is used when you can't wait for Probes (which are sent in Umbra) and Pan Dimensional Corps (which deal with Umbra)<br /> -It force Un-conventional physics (which can be found only in Umbra) to work as in conventional physics.<br /> -It makes Technocratic procedures coincidental (and where Technocratic procedures are not? In umbra) and makes mystical rotes vulgare (and where mystical magic is coincidental? In Umbra)<br /> -It transformate EDE (which lives in Umbra) into Thaumivores (which are umbral creatures who lives on this side of the Gauntlet, and if they do not eat they are expelled to the other side of it (aka, the Umbra)<br /> -It's a rote of a convention who DOES NOT deal in conventional space because they are famous for dealing with UMBRA, just like Toreador are famous for being snobs<br /> <br /> But ehi! It must not be a Umbra thing!<br /> <br /> It looks like a duck, it quackles like a duck, it walks like duck, but ehi, it must be clearly an elephant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Vampires are actually the REVERSE of Thaumivores. They PRODUCE quintessence far in excess of what they need to consume. </div> </div> </div>No, no vampire PRODUCE quintessence.<br /> They DRINK it, and so they store it,since, as I'm sure you know, mortal blood is full of quintessence.<br /> <br /> So no, you will not make them Thaumivores, since they already are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:18:00-07:00","id":967647,"title":"","content":"Just tossing this question out there: How much collateral damage is the Technocracy willing to tolerate in this fight? Are they prepared to pursue the extermination of vampires so fanatically that they salt the planet in the process? If they consider that to be acceptable losses that's fine, but I can't see how that squares with their humanitarian propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:21:39-07:00","id":967649,"title":"","content":"Don't give a damn what M20 says. Ever. Don't own it. Don't intend to own it.<br /> <br /> In revised, which is the edition Format Space is from, ALL magic and enlightened science is coincidental in the umbra. It's even specifically mentioned in the plasma cannon entry.<br /> <br /> I'm personally convinced you're being deliberately obtuse about this because it's broken as fuck. But no.<br /> <br /> <br /> Each success raises the Gauntlet by 1 for Reality Deviants,<br /> and decreases it by 1 for Technocrats, to a maximum<br /> rating of 10 and minimum rating of 0, respectively.<br /> In a region outside of Earth, this Gauntlet is called a<br /> pericarp, and erects itself even if it didn\u2019t exist before.<br /> Pericarps do not manifest the Dimensional Anomaly.<br /> <br /> A person reading this would go &quot;Oh so it can increase the Gauntlet. Or even create one in the Umbra where one didn't exist before.&quot; That it needs to SPECIFY it's effects in a region outside of earth implies that it can be used ON earth.<br /> <br /> Five successes render all Reality Deviant Procedures<br /> vulgar, even if they would normally be coincidental,<br /> while all Technocratic Procedures become coincidental.<br /> The only exceptions to this consist of certain<br /> Procedures that are vulgar throughout the Tellurian\u2014<br /> including \u201cFormat Space.\u201d If this feature is chosen,<br /> material, living organisms that cannot be accepted by<br /> Technocratic science becomes what Traditionalists call<br /> \u201cthaumivores.\u201d Without one point of Primal Energy per<br /> day, they will sicken and die, or fade across dimensional<br /> boundaries to become para-material EDEs.<br /> <br /> This does not take reference to the Consensus. This is simple brute fact and in many ways matches the description of Sanctums and Laboratories. ALL Traditionalist Rotes and effects are now Vulgar. Regardless of what the Consensus says about it. ALL Technocratic Procedures are now Coincidental. Regardless of what the Consensus says about it. The only exceptions are, as stated, procedures that are ALWAYS Vulgar. Such as Format Space. A strict reading of this would even say that now Vampires incur paradox for their powers. How that would work? Dunno.<br /> <br /> And finally the least important effect....<br /> <br /> Five successes force the mundane physics of the<br /> region to conform to the Consensus. Hyperspatial<br /> \u201cether\u201d turns into hard vacuum, for example.<br /> <br /> Says nothing about WHAT region or precludes you from using the other effects on regions where this is already true. In fact it's inclusion as a separate thing with an assigned cost, readily implies the other two can be used in a scenario in which this one is not necessary.<br /> <br /> Is the power insanely broken if misused? HELL YES. It's also rather difficult to misuse.<br /> <br /> Also Vitae is not blood. Vampires drink entirely mundane blood, and convert it into Vitae. Vitae is Tass. Blood is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:32:45-07:00","id":967678,"title":"","content":"And how about this Procedure?<br /> <br /> Enforce Reality<br /> (Prime 5 Dimensional Science 2)<br /> We control what the masses regard as reality. Deviants like to pierce, rend and disturb this consensus whenever they can. We can not allow this to happen, most of them are punished by the unerring force of the consensus and suffer from Paradox, some Reality Deviants are of such magnitude that they need some more attention.<br /> Imagine complete stasis, nothing supernatural can exist anymore. This powerful Procedure creates a pocket of completely static reality. Werecreatures can no longer change shape, Vampires die (they were dead after all weren't they?), Faeries ultimately succumb to banality, Umbrood dissolve etc. The main target for extreme measures such as this one are marauders though. Their excessive display of magick makes them the most dangerous thing possible for the Technocracy. Enforcing reality by all means is the only way to counter this threat.<br /> [This Procedure spells Paradox in mile-high capitals for everything except technomagick. All supernatural creatures die or lose their abilities while remaining in the area of effect. The area is determined in radius with the Correspondence range chart. Even Marauders may be forced out of their Quiets and their mythic beasts are thrown back behind the Gauntlet. Speaking of which, each success also strengthens the gauntlet by one point. Worst of all, this Procedure is also coincidental. It only strengthens what the sleepers were made to believe anyway, there is nothing supernatural.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:34:37-07:00","id":967680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967649#post967649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't give a damn what M20 says. Ever. Don't own it. Don't intend to own it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In revised, which is the edition Format Space is from, ALL magic and enlightened science is coincidental in the umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, so much ignorance.<br /> <br /> No it is not.<br /> Just read the Book of the worlds<br /> <br /> <br /> Book of the worlds p187<br /> <br /> Elemental Domains<br /> <br /> &quot;All technomagickal effects are considered Vulgar&quot;<br /> <br /> about Umbrood Realms<br /> <br /> &quot;All forms of mystick magick are coincidental; the spirits are old fashioned and consider technomagick a vulgare aberration.&quot;<br /> <br /> About middle umbra<br /> <br /> &quot;Technomagick is vulgare in all Middle Umbral Realms except Dystopia; there the reverse is true&quot;<br /> <br /> Balador<br /> <br /> &quot;All forms of technomagick are strictly vulgare&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All the rest of your speech is discarded as consequence.<br /> <br /> Seriously, take the books and study, you still have a long way ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:35:20-07:00","id":967681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=966245#post966245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the problems I'd foresee coming up that I haven't really seen mentioned also heavily depend on which splat would be favored. Outside of directly Fire and Sunlight related effects, are most other magiks going to be very effective against Cainites? From a Mage perspective, &quot;Lightningbolts&quot; might deal Aggravated Damage, but from the Vampire perspective they probably deal very minimal Lethal damage. Just as an example. Even dropping a building on them supercharged with Magik is probably going to have a very different effect on a Cainite depending on if you favor Mage or Vampire for how to handle it.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue, that if Mages are immune to Paradox, lets also just go ahead and assume that all Cainites are immune to Sunlight. That's pretty close to fair. Just saying.<br /> It's also one of those very odd things, where it really depends on which game you favor, as in the VtM perspective, most Vampires DO actually cause Paradox backlash for Mages, but there are a few notable exceptions, like Malkavians due to their insane and chaotic nature, and the Tremere who have an understanding of true Magik. Anyway, from this point onwards, we are all going to assume that either Mages do have to deal with Paradox as normal or Vampires are just outright immune to Sunlight, and we will leave the question as to if Vampires can cause Paradox for Mages up in the air for if you favor Mage or Vampire.<br /> <br /> There seems to be a few odd assumptions made that I'm not sure are accurate. For example that Vampires can't access space, other realms, or much outside of the planet earth or the physical world. That's not very true. It's less important to VtM to go into much detail about the Astral Plane, the Umbra(s), etc. . . just because to most VtM games, it's not that important. Vampire doesn't revolve around that much. However, Auspex, Necromancy, Protean all allow for access to the other realms, which are generally speaking, all connected, and are not terribly uncommon powers. Thaumaturgy as well.<br /> <br /> We also seem to assume that Mages somehow get free access to things like Nukes, but Vampires do not, which doesn't seem to fly. For example, Marcus Vitel basically infiltrated Washing DC for the exact purpose of getting access and control of the US's Nukes. The Mages might have a nasty surprise coming their way when they try to pull that card, only to find out that much of their arsenal isn't actually at their disposal after al, but is instead going to be used against them, or if we assume that both Mages and Vampires have influence and &quot;control&quot; of the key world leaders, that many of those weapons are suddenly, unforeseeably, taken off the table completely for BOTH sides.<br /> <br /> On the idea of creating Rituals/Paths for AntiMage things, I'd argue that both sides are partially correct, and at best it really does come down to splat favoritism. It is possible to create a new Path and Rituals for basically anything. However, doing so is NEVER an on the spot thing. Even in the new Anarchs Unleashed book, it talks about how Punk Magic, (sort of an improvised variety aimed at specifically trying to do on the spot effects) is very difficult, limited, and a time consuming process up front. The fact that the Tremere did so in a lot of their backstory is just one of those things that doesn't make any sense and we just have to handwave logic under the rung because the devs wanted to have the Tremere in the game no matter what.. However, all that being said, we can probably also reasonably assume that the Tremere specifically went out of their way to develop some, at least basic, AnitMage Thaumaturgy as their first real battle was against other Mages as they tried to establish themselves, and as cunning right bastards, it makes no sense whatsoever that they would have left themselves o vulnerable against probably the single on threat they actually knew about in detail.<br /> <br /> Ravnos' death was literally a plot device. He (she) had just woken up, and fighting during the daytime, SHOULD have been extremely limited in Dice Pools, but still manages to nearly survive going head to head with a Werewolf Pack, Wraiths, KotE elders, and Mages, at the same time or one after another. At best, we have an example of some rules being ignored in favor of telling a story and making a point, but the issue(s) is that the different points it makes say some very different things. Ravnos did have Fortitude as a Clan Discipline, and (if we assume) that means it was maxed out to 10 dots (or more???), it makes it, at least on the surface feasible that it took all of that to BARELY put him down. Except that well, he shouldn't have had access to his full power for multiple reasons, (fighting during the day handicaps Vampires to the Path Rating, which was unlikely at 10 and probably closer to 1-3, he was already weak from not feeding and just waking up, and confused and disorientated). End result, the Story overrules EVERYTHING else, but since Antis and Oracles are not in this, it really doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Then we come to the issue of if Counter Magic even works on most Disciplines, and secondarily if Mage's other intrinsic ability to alter reality off screen affects Vampires at all. This can also lead to the overarching issue if Mage's, ANY MAGE, can override &quot;God&quot;. In Vampire unquestionably no. In Mage, arguably the entire point. Just for the sake of argument here, by &quot;God&quot; I'm including both the J-C and Noddist version as well as the basic fundamental principles of the universe that Mages have not universally altered such as gravity. Once again, it's entirerly based upon which game line the ST favors over the other.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a strong implication, or even taken as fact, that Mages know all, and are fully prepared, while Cainites are not. I'm not sure that that is very accurate. While in general, Cainites are probably going to be less specifically designed to fight a war against Mages than the reverse, that would probably only matter very significantly if one group was attacking the other from surprise. Since the basic assumption seems to be that both sides are pretty aware of the theoretical war, that Vampires would also start pulling out all the stop, which leads to a bit of a problem for Mages, even if we assume that both groups have exerted a great deal of influence across the mortal/mundane world, politics, technology, etc. . . and that is that Vampires probably have a hell of a lot more personal experience with fighting/surviving Mages and other creatures than Mages do Vampires. As immortals, they just have a lot more experience they can call upon, even if it's less directly applicable, it should have a lot of crossover potential. There is also the fact that things like the Inquisition didn't just target Vampires, and at least according to VtM was actually much, much more of a threat towards Mages and Sorcerers (and innocents) that it was against Vampires. There is also the fact that even the Technocracy really has minimal &quot;true&quot; information about Vampires (and any other Supernatural being), more studying the vampire from the Mage's Antagonist perspective (a watered down and inaccurate version) rather than actual Cainites. This is also true for Vampires, though, but I'd think that it's much less of a hindrance for VtM than it is for MtA.<br /> <br /> And finally, one last assumption I'm not sure is very good, is that it's not Mages vs the Tremere, but rather that there are also a lot of other Clans out there too who might have all sorts of nifty powers and tactics that might screw with Mages. An earthmelded Gangrel shouldn't be detectable by Mages at all (or at least not by most methods they would think to use), and many Mages might have an issue doing anything to a cloud of fog. Fortitude is also a pretty common Discipline, but is also one that is 1.) always on and 2.) pretty all inclusive. Technology, even boosted by Magick probably doesn't do a thing against Obfuscate, which doesn't turn you invisible, and isn't an illusion, but rather directly affects the minds of everyone, even after the fact to simply not accept that the user was even there. Mage's probably have little defense against a small group of Nosferatu that just walk in undetected, call on a small swarm of crows, and then unleash their Beast on a Mage who should then loose all access to magick and rational thought, and probably go freaking crazy and attack anything near it that moves.<br /> <br /> So, with all that in mind, I'm more inclined to say more likely it would go to Mages, but I wouldn't count Cainites out so quickly unless you continue to just favor Mage's rules, themes, and truths over Vampire's and everyone else's (seeing a trend here on that account), and then it's really not even a question. If, on the other hand, it is more of a unbiased thought exercise, Vampires might surprise you with the long game, that thing they excel at. There is also the little fact that you literally have to exterminate every single Vampire in existence for Mages to truly win, because even one Vampire can repopulate the earth, and if we also assume that Caine and the 3rd Gen stay out, that does mean right off the bat Mages automatically fail at achieving overall victory and just a stalemate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the solution : Orbital bombardment until death. Warhmmaer 40k-esque Exterminatus Procedure. Ragnarok Command ensure that much.<br /> <br /> OP said that is all out war, and neither side care about collateral damage. Also, Technocracy takes great pain to protect world leaders from such supernatural subversion. In addition, US government implements their own Project Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-11-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:46:33-07:00","id":967685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967678#post967678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how about this Procedure?<br /> <br /> Enforce Reality<br /> (Prime 5 Dimensional Science 2)<br /> We control what the masses regard as reality. Deviants like to pierce, rend and disturb this consensus whenever they can. We can not allow this to happen, most of them are punished by the unerring force of the consensus and suffer from Paradox, some Reality Deviants are of such magnitude that they need some more attention.<br /> Imagine complete stasis, nothing supernatural can exist anymore. This powerful Procedure creates a pocket of completely static reality. Werecreatures can no longer change shape, Vampires die (they were dead after all weren't they?), Faeries ultimately succumb to banality, Umbrood dissolve etc. The main target for extreme measures such as this one are marauders though. Their excessive display of magick makes them the most dangerous thing possible for the Technocracy. Enforcing reality by all means is the only way to counter this threat.<br /> [This Procedure spells Paradox in mile-high capitals for everything except technomagick. All supernatural creatures die or lose their abilities while remaining in the area of effect. The area is determined in radius with the Correspondence range chart. Even Marauders may be forced out of their Quiets and their mythic beasts are thrown back behind the Gauntlet. Speaking of which, each success also strengthens the gauntlet by one point. Worst of all, this Procedure is also coincidental. It only strengthens what the sleepers were made to believe anyway, there is nothing supernatural.]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It will not work, you'll have to deal with the inherent countermagick of each reality deviant in the area.<br /> <br /> So in a city like New york your gonna deal with the countermagick of some 85-175 vampire,let's say the base countermagick for each vampire is 3 (it is not, is much higher, just the 3 Tremere elders in new york have a total ammount of 30 dices , but let's assume this as an hypotesis), you will have to pull your effect through 255-525 dices of countermagick, plus the countermagick of every mystic mage in the area,mummies,Fae,Fera,Wraiths and True Faith peoples.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-11-2016, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:11:50-07:00","id":967701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967681#post967681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the solution : Orbital bombardment until death. Warhmmaer 40k-esque Exterminatus Procedure. Ragnarok Command ensure that much.<br /> <br /> OP said that is all out war, and neither side care about collateral damage. Also, Technocracy takes great pain to protect world leaders from such supernatural subversion. In addition, US government implements their own Project Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Technocratic victory comes to that I'm content to let them have it. Revealing themselves as the bullies, tyrants, and all around monsters they are is a pretty acceptable price from my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:49:46-07:00","id":967718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967680#post967680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, so much ignorance.<br /> <br /> No it is not.<br /> Just read the Book of the worlds<br /> <br /> <br /> Book of the worlds p187<br /> <br /> Elemental Domains<br /> <br /> &quot;All technomagickal effects are considered Vulgar&quot;<br /> <br /> about Umbrood Realms<br /> <br /> &quot;All forms of mystick magick are coincidental; the spirits are old fashioned and consider technomagick a vulgare aberration.&quot;<br /> <br /> About middle umbra<br /> <br /> &quot;Technomagick is vulgare in all Middle Umbral Realms except Dystopia; there the reverse is true&quot;<br /> <br /> Balador<br /> <br /> &quot;All forms of technomagick are strictly vulgare&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All the rest of your speech is discarded as consequence.<br /> <br /> Seriously, take the books and study, you still have a long way ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, like a crossover book, which are rather infamously stupid in oWoD, is going to be better than the ACTUAL GAME.<br /> <br /> So when you actually want to discuss the subject and not throw irrelevant books at me. Get back to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:55:16-07:00","id":967724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967685#post967685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It will not work, you'll have to deal with the inherent countermagick of each reality deviant in the area.<br /> <br /> So in a city like New york your gonna deal with the countermagick of some 85-175 vampire,let's say the base countermagick for each vampire is 3 (it is not, is much higher, just the 3 Tremere elders in new york have a total ammount of 30 dices , but let's assume this as an hypotesis), you will have to pull your effect through 255-525 dices of countermagick, plus the countermagick of every mystic mage in the area,mummies,Fae,Fera,Wraiths and True Faith peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probable numbers:<br /> Mummies: maybe 1?<br /> Mages: 8-50 depending on how you do your ratios (1:150,000 to 1:1,000,000)<br /> Wraiths: A silly amount. But would this affect them at all since they are already on the other side of a Gauntlet?<br /> now the big 2:<br /> Changelings: about 400+<br /> Fera: conservatively a few hundred at least. Probably a between 1 and 2 thousand or more when including Ratkin<br /> <br /> So since this has given me food for thought. I think the biggest impediment to grand magical workings like this being tossed around would actually be the Changelings. They tend to be the most populous (1 in 20,000 was tossed around in another thread) and 100% of them have countermagic in the form of banality they can wield (though they gain Banality from using it that way).<br /> It could be an interesting meta-story point. Mages wouldn't be able to get non-direct damage mass workings to work and would possibly just assume it impossible or that it requires too many successes, when it ends up just being the supposedly extinct Fae.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this has nothing to do with the thread topic, but it was funny to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, I think the Technocracy would have to kill life on the planet to ensure victory. And at the point, it really isn't winning. It's running away to the spirit world and vaporizing the Earth behind you. And I don't actually think they can pull that off without a lot of mundane help in the form of all out nuclear war.<br /> <br /> Also, how does that Prime 5, Dimensional Science 2 Procedure work? It doesn't seem to have the Spheres necessary to even affect the creatures it lists. (actual question, not sarcasm)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T22:17:57-07:00","id":967776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967718#post967718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, like a crossover book, which are rather infamously stupid in oWoD, is going to be better than the ACTUAL GAME.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? Crossover book? Book of the Worlds is a pure Mage gameline book, just like Infinite Tapestry.<br /> Also, multiple Mage books state that it's the Deep Umbra where *all* Magick is coincidental *everywhere* no matter where you go. Heck, it's the reason why the most powerful Marauders get flung there.<br /> In the normal Umbrae it highly depends on the realm(s) and zones you visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-12-2016, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:25:53-07:00","id":967803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967569#post967569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, Vampires and their powers are part of the static consensus, there is nothing Technocracy can do about it, so if you are disrupting their powers you are disrupting the static consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on, where is this from? I'm looking through the crossover bit in Mage Storyteller's Handbook Revised and there's... nothing whatsoever saying anything like this. If a vampire's powers are magical - which they are even in vampire paradigm - then countering them with an opposing power is just countermagick, Countermagick... isn't vulgar, ever, unless there's something specific contradicting that. Like being in the Flux Realm or other supermagical places, and... if a vampire's in the Flux Realm, they have a hell of a lot more problems than a couple Mages.<br /> <br /> Hell, a lot of Disciplines can just not succeed sometimes, and something that could entirely plausibly happen is Coincidental.<br /> <br /> Even for something like Celerity:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Storyteller's Handbook Revised p. 200</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Countermagic</b><br /> Disciplines such as Animalism, Dominate, Presence and Thaumaturgy may generally be countered directly by mages through use of their Spheres. In order to do so a mage must usually have at least one dot in the Mind Sphere. Other Disciplines, or their specific effects, may be countered at the Storyteller\u2019s option. For example, a mage might use Time 3 to counter Celerity. <b>The mage rolls her normal Arete roll, usually at coincidental magic difficulty numbers since it is preventing a supernatural effect, though some Storytellers may prefer to use a standard difficulty number of 8.</b> Each success cancels one of the vampire\u2019s successes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967776#post967776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? Crossover book? Book of the Worlds is a pure Mage gameline book, just like Infinite Tapestry.<br /> Also, multiple Mage books state that it's the Deep Umbra where *all* Magick is coincidental *everywhere* no matter where you go. Heck, it's the reason why the most powerful Marauders get flung there.<br /> In the normal Umbrae it highly depends on the realm(s) and zones you visit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, the Deep Umbra is where no magic is Paradoxical. IIRC there are things that are in fact Vulgar actually everywhere, Format Space in particular being the sort of thing that does that.<br /> <br /> You can use it there without Paradox, it'd just... still be Vulgar. Difficulties and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-12-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T04:46:53-07:00","id":967862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967718#post967718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, like a crossover book, which are rather infamously stupid in oWoD, is going to be better than the ACTUAL GAME.<br /> <br /> So when you actually want to discuss the subject and not throw irrelevant books at me. Get back to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No sorry, another proof of ignorance on Mage 101: Book of the worlds is a MAGE book, not a crossover book, it's the main book that deals about the Umbra in the Mage line (along with Infinite Tapestry, which have a slightly different topic, and the Book of Madness in a lesser extent)<br /> <br /> You really do not know what are you talking about, don't you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967803#post967803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, where is this from? I'm looking through the crossover bit in Mage Storyteller's Handbook Revised and there's... nothing whatsoever saying anything like this. If a vampire's powers are magical - which they are even in vampire paradigm - then countering them with an opposing power is just countermagick, Countermagick... isn't vulgar, ever, unless there's something specific contradicting that. Like being in the Flux Realm or other supermagical places, and... if a vampire's in the Flux Realm, they have a hell of a lot more problems than a couple Mages.<br /> <br /> Hell, a lot of Disciplines can just not succeed sometimes, and something that could entirely plausibly happen is Coincidental.<br /> <br /> Even for something like Celerity:<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No no no, stop, I'm not talking about countermagic; of course you can countermagic a discipline, no doubt.<br /> I'm talking about creating an effect or a device that prevents the Vampire from using his discipline.<br /> In the previous posts was theorized effects and devices that where capable of nullifyng vampire's disciplines, outside the countermagic case.<br /> <br /> So while you can countermagic a Ventrue Dominate you can't infect him with a virus that suppress his ability to use Dominate powers.<br /> Or again, if you shapeshift a werecreature back to his homid form you are doing a vulgar effect, not a coincidental one, because the shapeshifting abilities of fera are already in the consensus.<br /> <br /> It was about this, not about counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:35:33-07:00","id":967869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967647#post967647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just tossing this question out there: How much collateral damage is the Technocracy willing to tolerate in this fight? Are they prepared to pursue the extermination of vampires so fanatically that they salt the planet in the process? If they consider that to be acceptable losses that's fine, but I can't see how that squares with their humanitarian propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:dotum\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not mere propaganda. That is the reason why the Union is founded, and why it has existed for eight hundred years. That is the Union's fundamental purpose what they espouse, support and enforce by numberless means. Therefore proud statement of their resolve. Probably the Union, along with the Tradition, is the most humanitarian organization in the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">crapsack world that is cWoD. So yes, I agree Union will never enact such drastic measures unless absolutely necessary and try to exterminate the Leeches by other means.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, that is a premise given by the OP. Absurd or not, we must respect the given premises in the discussion. </span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967647#post967647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:dotum\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If a Technocratic victory comes to that I'm content to let them have it. Revealing themselves as the bullies, tyrants, and all around monsters they are is a pretty acceptable price from my perspective.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:dotum\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And Vampires are already </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the bullies, tyrants, and all around monsters they are, without any war of annihilation or other suchlike atrocities. In the playing, they are interesting. Tragic, heartbreaking, even(in fact, I mostly play the Vampire, because, well, it is easiest to play, while the Mage is arguably the hardest). I love them as fictional characters, and enjoy playing as C</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">amarilla, or Black Hand, or any other Sects. However, from realistic, objective in-game perspective,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Vamps are pure, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">unadulterated </span></span></span><b>abominations need to be extinct any time soon, and any means necessary</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. They are </span></span></span><b>vile parasites </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">actively feeding, eating, enslaving, using, exploiting, toying, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">traumatizing, terrorizing </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">humanity. They are all </span></span></span><b>evil, damnable monstrosities</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, all of them, without a single exception. Unlike many of the supernaturals, and Technocracy as zenith of it, these</span></span></span><b> abominable monsters</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> contribute absolutely NOTHING to humanity. And if they contribute anything slightest the humanity, it is entirely for self-aggrandizement, collecting property, blood farming, Ghoul propagating and &quot;</span></span></span><b>cattle(kine, mortals, or whatever) edibility control</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>&quot; </b>so that they can live and feed and breed well, just same way as smart parasites do for their hosts' &quot;benefit&quot;. On stark contrast, Technocracy's whole existence is to guide humankind to the Unchained Utopia, and has always held moral high ground against the Cainates, especially regarding the Masses and if they have to lose that lofty ground to fulfill their founding purpose of serving Good of Humanity, so be it. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I am a mortal living in cWoD, I would dearly wish to see complete and utter eradication of the Leeches for the sake of panhumanity. Even if that means my death, my family's death, and 80% of the humanity's death. Indeed, that is precisely what Hunters aspire. That is their proclaimed noble purpose. Once humankind is liberated from Tyranny of the Vile Dead and D</span></span></span></span></span></span>isease <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:dotum\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">of Hemophagic Parasites who regard humanity in contempt and consider them as cattles, servants and playthings, WE will rebuild quickly, efficiently, admirably, and majestically under benevolent dominion of the Technocratic Union. Regardless how steeple price we have to pay, eradication of Vampires will be priceless boon to the Humankind's survival and prosperity. I will gladly call it Scouring, Great Purge, Triumph of Panhumanity, Realization of Collective Will or whatever fancy names the Union would surely conjure up, if I manage to survive the Purifying Pyre. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The said act might render the Union as the monsters. But it means merely the Union fall into the same league with morally bankrupt station of its adversary, not <i>below </i>or <i>reverse</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. </span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-12-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:54:36-07:00","id":967899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967681#post967681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the solution : Orbital bombardment until death. Warhmmaer 40k-esque Exterminatus Procedure. Ragnarok Command ensure that much.<br /> <br /> OP said that is all out war, and neither side care about collateral damage. Also, Technocracy takes great pain to protect world leaders from such supernatural subversion. In addition, US government implements their own Project Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Technocracy might not have all those weapons they thought they did after all if, (and this is pretty dang likely in anything but a Mage focused scenario), if the vampires already beat them to the punch. Or that the Vampires have not already infiltrated the organization with &lt;lowercase&gt; sleepers. The main point I'm trying to get across is that these little one shot one kills people think the Mages have probably will not work nearly as well as they might seem, unless you just ignore a great deal of Cainite's strength and theme to push them through, (ie favoring Mage over Vampire). It's just as likely that Vampires nuke the Technocracy into extermination, and we know that there are a few Vampires out there that have made it their goal to have absolute control of all nukes in a given country. And while Mages might have access to others, they also very well might not after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967869#post967869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#000000][FONT=dotum][SIZE=12px]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And Vampires are already </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the bullies, tyrants, and all around monsters they are, without any war of annihilation or other suchlike atrocities. In the playing, they are interesting. Tragic, heartbreaking, even(in fact, I mostly play the Vampire, because, well, it is easiest to play, while the Mage is arguably the hardest). I love them as fictional characters, and enjoy playing as C</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">amarilla, or Black Hand, or any other Sects. However, from realistic, objective in-game perspective,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Vamps are pure, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">unadulterated </span></span></span><b>abominations need to be extinct any time soon, and any means necessary</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. They are </span></span></span><b>vile parasites </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">actively feeding, eating, enslaving, using, exploiting, toying, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">traumatizing, terrorizing </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">humanity. They are all </span></span></span><b>evil, dameable monstrosities</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, all of them, without a single exception. Unlike many of the supernaturals, and Technocracy as zenith of it, these</span></span></span><b> abominable monsters</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> contribute absolutely NOTHING to humanity. And if they contribute anything slightest the humanity, it is entirely for self-aggrandizement, collecting property, blood farming, Ghoul propagating and &quot;</span></span></span><b>cattle(kine, mortals, or whatever) edibility control</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>&quot; </b>so that they can live and feed and breed well. On stark contrast, Technocracy's whole existence is to guide humankind to the Unchained Utopia, and has always held moral high ground against the Cainates, especially regarding the Masses and if they have to lose that lofty ground to fulfill their founding purpose of serving Good of Humanity, so be it. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And Mages are better? In fact, I'd actually view Mages, as a whole as the worse evil, literally attempting to force everything else in existence to conform to their personal views of what is right and how things should be, and with the potential power to do so. Vampires have to feed to survive. It's usually vile, but at least it's based on a need. Mages on the other hand do it because they want, and I'd generally say that a hell of a lot more innocents get caught in the middle of Mage machinations than Vampire ones. Mages have absolutely no moral high ground whatsoever, they just have the arrogance to think, to the point where they &quot;know&quot; that their utopia (ie, their enslavement of everyone) is &quot;better&quot; and pretend that there is no cost. Na, Mages are the worst of the evils.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure that Countermagick would be too effective. Remember, this isn't a MtA game of Mages vs Vampires, (nor a VtM Game of Vampires vs Mages), so while somethings might work a certain way in a given setting, it doesn't automatically take precedence as fact in a neutral scenario. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T07:20:00-07:00","id":967913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967899#post967899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Technocracy might not have all those weapons they thought they did after all if, (and this is pretty dang likely in anything but a Mage focused scenario), if the vampires already beat them to the punch. Or that the Vampires have not already infiltrated the organization with &lt;lowercase&gt; sleepers. The main point I'm trying to get across is that these little one shot one kills people think the Mages have probably will not work nearly as well as they might seem, unless you just ignore a great deal of Cainite's strength and theme to push them through, (ie favoring Mage over Vampire). It's just as likely that Vampires nuke the Technocracy into extermination, and we know that there are a few Vampires out there that have made it their goal to have absolute control of all nukes in a given country. And while Mages might have access to others, they also very well might not after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And how the Cainate could possibly hope to take control of the Technocracy's orbital assets? End of story.<br /> <br /> And how Cainate already beat Union to the punch? And how the Vampires could &quot;just as likely&quot; nuke the Technocracy into extermination? They are utterly oblivious to location of each and every of the Union's Earthbound Constructs, they could NOT reach, or even aware of, Horizons, Near Universe, Deep Universe, Deep Sea, Deep Underground, Polar Regions, Alpine Regions, and other myriad locations Union could fully access and Vampires could ABSOLUTELY NOT. Furthermore, Project Twilight obliterates any supernaturals dare attempt to influence higher-ups of US and allied governments, and the like I said, Union monitoring and actively prevent such subversive activity. For example, NWO Watchers know one of vice president's chief adviser is actually a Vampire, and poise themselves to eliminate it immediately if it attempts to use Dominate or Presence unto vice president.<br /> <br /> Moreover, have you read the infamous Chaos Factor? In that scenario, the Union possesses near complete identity and residence lists of Sabbat Leeches stalking the Mexico City, and eradicate 43 of them in one single dolorous stroke, whilst successfully fighting against Tradition Mages, Nephandi and powerful Bane Spirits. Whereas Sabbat completely oblivious of <b>existence </b>of the Technocracy(it is THEM who <i>actually </i>rule the Mexico City, in contrary to the Sabbat's delusional belief) and assume that attack came from Camarilla, Garou or Hunters and vehemently, but ultimately futilely, </span></span></span>retaliate <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">against them while call rescue to the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> So no, I'm absolutely sure the Technocracy know whereabout of Cainates whilst Cainates are completely OBLIVIOUS of existence of Union in general. If you have read any Vampire story or source materials, you have to know the fact that 99.9% of Vampires do not possess even a scant of knowledge whatsoever about the Mages(except Tremere and other Vampiric sorcerers, of course), let alone know about Tradition or Technocracy, while both factions are aware of existence of Vampire and in many cases, fully aware of division of Sects, Clans and politics among them. And in case of the Technocracy, their location, identity, dwelling place and hunting ground. </span></span></span>Whereas most of Cainate are woefully blind of Union's existence, and a lot of them does not even know, or acknowledge, Magic's existence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Know this : NWO is actively FEEDING identity, activity and location of troublesome Sabbat and Anarch Leeches to the Camarilla via mortal proxies and servants and let it police the Cainate society and internal politicking, and only intervene when brute force operation is absolutely necessary. Again, end of story.<br /> <br /> As opposed to your presumption, there is <i><b>tremendous </b></i>information disparity between the Mage and the Vampire, and the reverse is <b>utterly false</b>.<br /> <br /> That sort of information disparity is no less than staggering.<br /> <br /> Oh, and let's assume, purely for augment's sake, the Vamps SOMEHOW managed to control world's worth of nuclear weapons and Union could not bring its Orbital assets, for whatever reasons. And still, that does not matter at all. Union holds aplenty of hypertech nuke stockpiles. That has been mentioned multiple times, and realized as the rule. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967899#post967899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mages are better? In fact, I'd actually view Mages, as a whole as the worse evil, literally attempting to force everything else in existence to conform to their personal views of what is right and how things should be, and with the potential power to do so. Vampires have to feed to survive. It's usually vile, but at least it's based on a need. Mages on the other hand do it because they want, and I'd generally say that a hell of a lot more innocents get caught in the middle of Mage machinations than Vampire ones. Mages have absolutely no moral high ground whatsoever, they just have the arrogance to think, to the point where they &quot;know&quot; that their utopia (ie, their enslavement of everyone) is &quot;better&quot; and pretend that there is no cost. Na, Mages are the worst of the evils.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure that Countermagick would be too effective. Remember, this isn't a MtA game of Mages vs Vampires, (nor a VtM Game of Vampires vs Mages), so while somethings might work a certain way in a given setting, it doesn't automatically take precedence as fact in a neutral scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus that is your opinion. I could respect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-12-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https