 The resources to do this have to come from somewhere. I'm pretty sure that every single person involved in building, maintaining, and manning these orbital weapons/bases is a Mage or even fully aware of everything, which means they are susceptible to what Vampires tend to do best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967913#post967913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, Project Twilight obliterates any supernaturals dare attempt to influence higher-ups of US and allied governments, and the like I said, Union monitoring and actively prevent such subversive activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which might fly in a Mage game, but is outright false and contradicted otherwise, and that means it's a NOGO here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967913#post967913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, have you read the infamous Chaos Factor? In that scenario, the Union possesses near complete identity and residence lists of Sabbat Leeches stalking the Mexico City, and eradicate 43 of them in one single dolorous stroke, whilst successfully fighting against Tradition Mages, Nephandi and powerful Bane Spirits. Whereas Sabbat completely oblivious of <b>existence </b>of the Technocracy(it is THEM who <i>actually </i>rule the Mexico City, in contrary to the Sabbat's delusional belief) and assume that attack came from Camarilla, Garou or Hunters and vehemently, but ultimately futilely,</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967913#post967913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">retaliate <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">against them while call rescue to the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> So no, I'm absolutely sure the Technocracy know whereabout of Cainates whilst Cainates are completely OBLIVIOUS of existence of Union in general. If you have read any Vampire story or source materials, you have to know the fact that 99.9% of Vampires do not possess even a scant of knowledge whatsoever about the Mages(except Tremere and other Vampiric sorcerers, of course), let alone know about Tradition or Technocracy, while both factions are aware of existence of Vampire and in many cases, fully aware of division of Sects, Clans and politics among them. And in case of the Technocracy, their location, identity, dwelling place and hunting ground. </span></span></span>Whereas most of Cainate are woefully blind of Union's existence, and a lot of them does not even know, or acknowledge, Magic's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saying, by your own admission, &quot;infamous&quot; says it all. :P<br /> It is interesting though, that the book does talk about how most Mage's abilities will fail to work on Vampires unless they actually understand how Vampire's abilities work, (as opposed to how they think they work or along their own Paradigm, cough, cough), and that requires time resources, and the explicit desire to do so on a given subject.<br /> <br /> Also a bit funny, because as I remember it, as it turns out, it wasn't the NWO that truly &quot;controlled&quot; Mexico City after all was said and done, but a single Vampire that played them as dupes just like the others.<br /> <br /> But all of that aside, that presentation of Mexico City was a bit unique, and it's not really that great a feat to monitor and take notes on a bunch of Sabbat (wow a whole 43 out of hundreds in the middle of a war), known for being pretty openly vampiric. Good Job Mages. It's not, however, a very common situation. Now, taking a look at the rest of the world at a whole, and the truth is that most Mages, and this includes especially the Technocracy, (and this is actually in Chaos Factor, too!!!!), no very, very little about each other, and a good portion of that is false. Mages, especially the Technocracy just believe that they know more of the truth than they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:24:29-07:00","id":967979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967869#post967869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not mere propaganda. That is the reason why the Union is founded, and why it has existed for eight hundred years. That is the Union's fundamental purpose what they espouse, support and enforce by numberless means. Therefore proud statement of their resolve. Probably the Union, along with the Tradition, is the most humanitarian organization in the crapsack world that is cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, propaganda. Very effective propaganda it would appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967869#post967869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Vampires are already the bullies, tyrants, and all around monsters they are, without any war of annihilation or other suchlike atrocities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Vampires are absolutely bullies, tyrants, and monsters. The difference is they're honest about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967718#post967718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, like a crossover book, which are rather infamously stupid in oWoD, is going to be better than the ACTUAL GAME.<br /> <br /> So when you actually want to discuss the subject and not throw irrelevant books at me. Get back to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it does qualify as a &quot;crossover book&quot; we're dealing with a crossover situation, so it is anything but &quot;irrelevant.&quot; If you're going to categorically invalidate and denigrate anything that doesn't agree with your preconceived notions I don't really get what the point is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:18:19-07:00","id":968008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967979#post967979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, propaganda. Very effective propaganda it would appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, genuine purpose. Explicitly stated and in-universally acknowledged <b>Reason of Very Existence</b>. You are just plainly blind of it, or simply do not want to recognize the Mage holds moral high ground. Do you remember Technocrats are Mages, right? And unlike Vampire, and every other sentient organisms, non-Nephandic Mages are utterly <b>INCAPABLE </b>of lying about their purpose, since their very being of is inseparably intertwined with their purpose. The more they become powerful, the more their worldview is solidified and reinforced accordingly. Their ideal. Their goal. Their Vision. Their Ascension. Don't forget the very premise of the Line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967979#post967979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Vampires are absolutely bullies, tyrants, and monsters. The difference is they're honest about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh no, Vampires </span></span></span>absolutely <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">do not acknowledge the fact, except perhaps Sabbat, who openly flaunts it. The difference is Vampire is not only bullies, tyrants and monsters, but also dishonest about it, and upholds no great cause whatsoever except self-aggrandizement and feeding. Say whatever you want to the Union or the Hunter. However you could never claim they do not implement, or dishonest, about their noble cause. Whilst most Vamps are utterly dishonest about their very <i>existential </i>purpose - namely feeding, breeding, grubbing money, and exploiting the Masses to live as self-styled nobles and princes.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-12-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:00:15-07:00","id":968018,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to stop using all of the different codes in your posts. It makes it difficult to read when trying to reply.<br /> <br /> I do not at all believe the Mages have any sort of higher moral ground than any other splat. They may, no scratch that, they outright do believe it, but at the end of the day, they are literally the worst monsters in existence by trying to change reality to conform to their particular (or group's) view of what it should be. The Technocracy is just the worst of the worst, and even if they do do some things that many people consider to be &quot;good&quot;, not everyone is going to agree on either that it is actually &quot;good&quot; or that the price is worth it.<br /> <br /> It's hard to tell if you actually buy into it or if you are just playing along a bit in character.<br /> <br /> The machines in the Matrix first created the Matrix as a perfect utopia, remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:02:26-07:00","id":968021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968008#post968008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, genuine purpose. Explicitly stated and in-universally acknowledged <b>Reason of Very Existence</b>. You are just plainly blind of it, or simply do not want to recognize the Mage holds moral high ground. Do you remember Technocrats are Mages, right? And unlike Vampire, and every other sentient organisms, non-Nephandic Mages are utterly <b>INCAPABLE </b>of lying about their purpose, since their very being of is inseparably intertwined with their purpose. The more they become powerful, the more their worldview is solidified and reinforced accordingly. Their ideal. Their goal. Their Vision. Their Ascension. Don't forget the very premise of the Line.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Jeez I can't believe what I'm reading.<br /> Are you serious? The moral high-ground from a century old fascist,un-democratic,pro-rich conspiracy?<br /> <br /> Please it is creepy, it really seems you believe what are you saying, like if you couldn't distinguish the game from reality.<br /> <br /> Mages lies every day, about everything, just like every human being.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes lied about Mark Gillian &quot;crimes&quot; to cover up Paramaguru Voormas, the Euthanatos lied about Voormas and the Consaguinity, Doissetep was nest of viper with Caeron Mustai at his center, the Tytalus lied about everything, stealing blood from the vampires and repeating the same mistakes of Tremere, when he was stilla human mage Tremere lied about house deidne infernalims just to heal is wounded honor,the Syndicate is a coven of liars of are pissing themselves with the idea that the others conventions could uncover just of corrupt and greedy they are, Caeron Mustai lied about everything, even about the story of House Jannissaries, just like Albayrak lied to the order of hermes claiming that the Jainnissaries were some great killers of technocrats, when they were the silent blade that struck multiple time the Traditions,the whole Horizon was plenty with people who cared nothing about Ascension and cared only to their political intrigues, the technocracy lied to Dante's mother so they could experiment on him.<br /> <br /> Look at the Technocracy how they lie about their purpose, the higher ups KNOW that they are mages, they KNOW that what they are doing is magic, but they will not tell it to the lower ranks, because they are obsessed by the whole control structure they created.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is the world of darkness, everybody lie,not a single organization is pure and good.<br /> <br /> It's the whole point of the Sphinx Manifesto, that the true spirit of Ascension has been lost in dogmas and politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:04:06-07:00","id":968022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968018#post968018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hard to tell if you actually buy into it or if you are just playing along a bit in character.<br /> <br /> The machines in the Matrix first created the Matrix as a perfect utopia, remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's creepy I say, I hope he is just playing the character, because otherwise is creepy, it really seems he has done quite the trip to Room 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:33:32-07:00","id":968046,"title":"","content":"&gt;implying Traditions morally superior to Technocrats<br /> Standard argument between 'freedom' and 'tyranny'<br /> <br /> &gt;imply Vampires morally superior to Technocrats<br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/60/84/31/6084314bf18212715fdcc3c5c43e40e8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Hey at least the Technocrat is Human","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 09-12-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:58:41-07:00","id":968091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967862#post967862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No no no, stop, I'm not talking about countermagic; of course you can countermagic a discipline, no doubt.<br /> I'm talking about creating an effect or a device that prevents the Vampire from using his discipline.<br /> In the previous posts was theorized effects and devices that where capable of nullifyng vampire's disciplines, outside the countermagic case.<br /> <br /> So while you can countermagic a Ventrue Dominate you can't infect him with a virus that suppress his ability to use Dominate powers.<br /> Or again, if you shapeshift a werecreature back to his homid form you are doing a vulgar effect, not a coincidental one, because the shapeshifting abilities of fera are already in the consensus.<br /> <br /> It was about this, not about counter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, how exactly is the 'virus to suppress Dominate' not a delayed countermagick effect?<br /> <br /> That's basically what Forge Primium is, a lasting dicepool of countermagick against 'shit that affects the thing protected by the Primium'. Said virus would basically be the same.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be an absolute effect but acting to keep their DIscipline from going off by counterdiceing their activation roll seems perfectly legit as a Coincidental effect. Again, vampires sometimes not succeeding on activating their Disciplines happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:19:11-07:00","id":968107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968091#post968091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, vampires sometimes not succeeding on activating their Disciplines happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with disciplines that needs no rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:42:17-07:00","id":968151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968107#post968107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with disciplines that needs no rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not then, obviously. Still, IIRC Celerity doesn't have an <i>explicit</i> roll, but is noted as being counterable, so its 'active' mode might have effective autosuccesses or something. Point is, it's not really some sort of blatant violation of the underpinnings of reality, it's just opposing magic with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:00:28-07:00","id":968160,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'll have to step in here, and in a surprising twist of events against the Union.<br /> <br /> I have no boat in this race anymore, but I am however a huge Union fan.<br /> <br /> But calling the Union, unambiguously good is doing it a disservice.<br /> <br /> The sins of the Union are the sins of the west, it is a patriarchal, explotative organization, and the entire point of many Union games are whether you can tolerate what the Union has become or whether you want to attempt to restore it to it's glory days as the Order of Reason, when nobility and Reason wasn't buried beneath layers of &quot;to break an omelet&quot; and &quot;for the good of the Union&quot; propaganda. Like, this is some of the first things that Guide to The Technocracy tells you, if you refuse that the Union is just as morally ambiguous as it's enemies, you refuse the central point of what Mage is about.<br /> <br /> The Union is not fascist however, it truly wants to elevate all of humanity to the ranks of the Enlightened, but the problem is that you have a core of Enlightened people who have reached Enlightenment 6 and can thus see that when you use a plasma cannon, all that you're really doing is that you're saying Forces 3/Primium 2 in a different way. And these people, realizing that they are the one-eyed men in a world of the blind, believe that there must be an Enlightened elite to shepherd the masses, guiding them through the terrors of the night, without realizing that they have become <i>exactly </i>like the ancient old tyrant-wizards that they rallied their fellow men to arms against during the Sorcerer's Crusade.<br /> <br /> Neither is the Technocracy un-democratic. It believes in democracy because the Union represents the sins of the patriarchial west, enforcing it's &quot;One True Way&quot; one everyone else, it's CIA infiltrating other countries and bringing them down so that USA can implement &quot;democracy&quot;, it's the USA backing terrorists to fight a greater enemy, and then being unwilling to fix the problem it created in any way other than it created it in the first place.<br /> <br /> It is not pro-rich, though the Syndicate might tell you differently depending on who you ask. The Void Engineers are Space Marines and Ghostbusters fighting a desperate battle for humanity's survival (and being space conquistadors), the Iterators are transhumanists who want to help humanity to remove it's flaws (whether you want it or not), the Progenitors are biologists and doctors, who want to free humanity from the yoke of death and disease (if you show up on a list of Reality Deviants, you count as disease btw) and the NWO support a strong state that can help it's subjects when they are in need, so they don't ever need to experience sadness or poverty or war (who cares if you have to sacrifice a little freedom to get it?).<br /> <br /> Of these, only the Syndicate is pro-rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:57:07-07:00","id":968209,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> Lots of good points.<br /> <br /> One of the main reason I find my self siding on the Tech side of the question is really simple. Their strengths, triumphs, and faults are Humanities' Strengths Triumphs and Faults. Collectively I can get behind the message of trying to make things better / making sure it all doesn't go to pot. Say what you want about the limitation of reality underneath the Techs. but technology has become the great equalizer. Deeply rooted in Rationalism. Its the magic anyone can use. You don't need to be a wizard to cast Message. You just pick up your cellphone and give them a call.<br /> <br /> And I believe the reason the Techs are on top is not because they got lucky or were ruthless. Its more simple than that. They gave humanity a Choice: Reason or Belief ? Reason says you can do something. Belief says hope for luck. The Tool became the implication of Will. Just as it always was. Mankind was always a Tool Orientated creature. <br /> <br /> And before someone else brings up room 101 again. Everymage with at least Mind3 has a room 101.<br /> <br /> Vamps has all the control of the Techs and even less humanity.<br /> <br /> Now if we're done talking out of our collective asses. Lets focus. The OP post didn't give us a situation to work with. its just gave us the 'rules' but not the setting. and before you save reality as a whole. no. that's too broad and unhelpful.<br /> <br /> Let's look at resources:<br /> Vamps need blood. end of sentence<br /> Tech need food and quint <br /> <br /> Both of these things can be found in an abundance in urban setting. Vamps eat humans and Techs piggy back off of economy. So I propose setting the stage of the conflict with in a city. <br /> <br /> Lets also give the Vamp home field advantage. not because it's theirs but because before the conflict had happen they would entangle themselves into the City's political structures and industries. The tech would be playing second fiddle, and gaining influence behind the vamps. <br /> <br /> In the opening days of the conflict. I can see Vamps striking out taking a number of Tech Agents. Certain vamps can notice when things are Off/Odd/ Not of them. So in a conflict situation, I can see them trying to nail down everyone that isn't them. Once that has happen. The remaining Tech start employing obfuscation tactics, to keep themselves safe. A regular game of cat and mouse. Each must investigate the other.<br /> <br /> And like my post previously, Who has more information?<br /> <br /> This isn't about who is more powerful. it's about who can ID targets better and faster than the other side. When you have two glass cannons, it's not about who shoots first it's about who shoots better.<br /> <br /> Both sides can can play the espionage game pretty well. But I believe the Mages have some of the best investigation tools at their disposal. It takes very little investment for a new mage to be able to ping other supers. and be a PI. But it is an investment for vamps to do so.<br /> <br /> That being said vamps have a lot more out of the box combat tools. For Mages its an investment to be combat focused.<br /> <br /> Once the vamps find a target, they can swarm pretty quickly and over run him. but mages can more consistently find targets and plan the encounter, which they'll win because they'll plan. It's the Batman V Superman argument. In chaos situations Supes wins. In order Bats wins. Thrown in Fate/Time Risk assessments and chaos becomes orderly chaos.<br /> <br /> Then you find a flipping of the momentum. and Vamps have to def.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:57:13-07:00","id":968210,"title":"","content":"So the Union is like the Culture from the Culture books, only without even a hint of self-awareness? Cool. I'll go and hang out with the Brujah, at least they are honest assholes.<br /> <br /> I also like how everyone is basically comparing raw combat power in one form or another, when the main raison d'etre of both splats is not being out in the open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 09-12-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:40:10-07:00","id":968241,"title":"","content":"This thread was always going to be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> But one more thing to fan the flames (not at all a serious suggestion)... <br /> <br /> Realising the End is Nigh, Shaitan awakens, expends all his permanent Willpower and ushers Grandma into the mortal world. Cue universal obliteration as Oblivion crosses the Shroud and the resultant paradox (lower case) annihilates all matter.<br /> <br /> BTW, Antediluvians are out, but Caine wasn't explicitly mentioned. Hurting him causes seven times the injury to the attacker as cursed by God (infinite successes or near enough...). Wiping out all vampires would require wiping him out too. That won't go down well when it hits you in the face seven times over.<br /> <br /> If vampires have to obliterate all humans to win, they lose. Likewise with the Technocracy. This feels like a lose-lose situation.<br /> <br /> Also, where does God stand in all this? Does he/she/it stand idly by?<br /> <br /> My money is on Pokemon. Any one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:40:24-07:00","id":968242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968210#post968210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Union is like the Culture from the Culture books, only without even a hint of self-awareness? Cool. I'll go and hang out with the Brujah, at least they are honest assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rather disingenuous towards the Technocracy. The Technocrats are also champions of humanity and reason in what some might call a world gone mad, as well as holding the role of assholes, but that's because everyone in WoD is an asshole.<br /> <br /> Also, the Revised Convention Books show plenty of self-awareness, in Iteration X there is a <i>glorious</i> line that goes something like this: &quot;Every Iterator goes through a training camp straight out of their worst nightmares, rigorously designed to tear them apart and force them to work to their highest capabilities. We call it tech support.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, NWO and the Syndicate are pretty honest about being assholes, they are also extremely smug while doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968210#post968210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like how everyone is basically comparing raw combat power in one form or another, when the main raison d'etre of both splats is not being out in the open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the post above you proposes an information war scenario, and we've had several cold war-esque ideas earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> But we could also have a hiding contest in case that's what you want?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:45:30-07:00","id":968246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968241#post968241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread was always going to be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> But one more thing to fan the flames (not at all a serious suggestion)...<br /> <br /> Realising the End is Nigh, Shaitan awakens, expends all his permanent Willpower and ushers Grandma into the mortal world. Cue universal obliteration as Oblivion crosses the Shroud and the resultant paradox (lower case) annihilates all matter.<br /> <br /> BTW, Antediluvians are out, but Caine wasn't explicitly mentioned. Hurting him causes seven times the injury to the attacker as cursed by God (infinite successes or near enough...). Wiping out all vampires would require wiping him out too. That won't go down well when it hits you in the face seven times over.<br /> <br /> If vampires have to obliterate all humans to win, they lose. Likewise with the Technocracy. This feels like a lose-lose situation.<br /> <br /> Also, where does God stand in all this? Does he/she/it stand idly by?<br /> <br /> My money is on Pokemon. Any one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? What does Shaitan (the 4th gen Baali) have to do with the (as far as I am concerned, non-canon) Grand Maw of Orpheus? Or are you talking about the 9 dot Daimoion power?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Caine, isnt Mage best summed up by &quot;rules lawyering God&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 09-12-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:50:55-07:00","id":968249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968242#post968242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally the post above you proposes an information war scenario, and we've had several cold war-esque ideas earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> But we could also have a hiding contest in case that's what you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and most information war scenarios were with starting positions so imbalanced as to outpace the one in the OP (our goverment consipiracy works, totes, and yours totes does not, because reasons).<br /> <br /> I mean, these threads are fun to read, but are about as informative a playground fight between two kindergarteners who both pull powers our of their arses at random.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:28:35-07:00","id":968375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=967969#post967969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly by not just pretending that anything and everything that can be done is an infallible autowin button, but only for Mages. :P<br /> <br /> As to how, there are plenty of options and potentialities (and all of them reasonable). There is going to be a paper trail. The resources to do this have to come from somewhere. I'm pretty sure that every single person involved in building, maintaining, and manning these orbital weapons/bases is a Mage or even fully aware of everything, which means they are susceptible to what Vampires tend to do best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, you have to actually ANSWER my questions, instead of endlessly eluding and teasing and make baseless speculations and spouting nonsenses. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T23:18:57-07:00","id":968388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968249#post968249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and most information war scenarios were with starting positions so imbalanced as to outpace the one in the OP (our goverment consipiracy works, totes, and yours totes does not, because reasons).<br /> <br /> I mean, these threads are fun to read, but are about as informative a playground fight between two kindergarteners who both pull powers our of their arses at random.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, obviously.<br /> <br /> We are a bunch of grown men and women, touting the supremacy of our favorite pretend conspiracies in our favorite magical elfgame pretend game.<br /> <br /> It will, by it's very nature be imbalanced and slightly stupid.<br /> <br /> By it's very nature, this thread accomplishes nothing, which has been stated repeatedly given that the only one who wins is the one the stortyteller feels like. I mean, if I felt like it, I could go &quot;this single Generation 15 vampire solos the Technocracy with a rusty spoon and a dildo&quot;, and then that vampire would win, because I as a storyteller felt like it.<br /> <br /> Your point is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:18:52-07:00","id":968408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968246#post968246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? What does Shaitan (the 4th gen Baali) have to do with the (as far as I am concerned, non-canon) Grand Maw of Orpheus? Or are you talking about the 9 dot Daimoion power?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Caine, isnt Mage best summed up by &amp;quot;rules lawyering God&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Daimoinon 9 lets you spend all your permanent Willpower to open the way for whichever dark power you want to enter the world. It's the cosmic annihilation plot device power.<br /> <br /> As for God, mages still don't get to beat him, rules lawyers or not. That would be even more silly than the premise of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T02:07:38-07:00","id":968421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968408#post968408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for God, mages still don't get to beat him, rules lawyers or not. That would be even more silly than the premise of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not individually and not easily, no. He's had way too long to entrench himself and way too many successes built up for his hanging effects.<br /> <br /> One day, though. <i>ONE DAY</i>.<br /> <br /> *maniacal laughter*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:07:38-07:00","id":968457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968242#post968242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is rather disingenuous towards the Technocracy. The Technocrats are also champions of humanity and reason in what some might call a world gone mad, as well as holding the role of assholes, but that's because everyone in WoD is an asshole.<br /> <br /> Also, the Revised Convention Books show plenty of self-awareness, in Iteration X there is a <i>glorious</i> line that goes something like this: &quot;Every Iterator goes through a training camp straight out of their worst nightmares, rigorously designed to tear them apart and force them to work to their highest capabilities. We call it tech support.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, NWO and the Syndicate are pretty honest about being assholes, they are also extremely smug while doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Literally the post above you proposes an information war scenario, and we've had several cold war-esque ideas earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> But we could also have a hiding contest in case that's what you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Manus, I don't want to obtrude this flame war I had ignited - I just want to ask why the Syndicate has not already bankrupted every single Vampire through Entropic Effects, Enlightened management and hypereconomics manipulations. I have always wondered why the Syndicate, the most competitive and ruthless of the Conventions(though not necessarily <i>greedy</i>), has left their immortal (potential) financial rivals and (also potential) business competitors largely intact so long like ancient, festering tumor, especially in the Mage-centric setting. What is your thought regarding the reason? Do you have any theory or conjecture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-13-2016, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:26:53-07:00","id":968480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968457#post968457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manus, I don't want to obtrude this flame war I had ignited - I just want to ask why the Syndicate has not already bankrupted every single Vampire through Entropic Effects, Enlightened management and hypereconomics manipulations. I have always wondered why the Syndicate, the most competitive and ruthless of the Conventions(though not necessarily <i>greedy</i>), has left their immortal (potential) financial rivals and (also potential) business competitors largely intact so long like ancient, festering tumor, especially in the Mage-centric setting. What is your thought regarding the reason? Do you have any theory or conjecture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming crossover, in a post medieval world, the vampires who were too overt or too vulnerable to manipulations were bankrupted, driven out or killed by the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> 1. They don't know who to strike. Technocracy having people with Correspondence 5 does not mean they automatically know who the vampires are - much less where their wealth is located. Note that Technocrats can't ever abandon their foci, so they will always need a body sample or a lead in order to work their Magick and find those Cainites.<br /> (I assume that mystics have it easier, because they can use a &quot;Find Cainites&quot; spell...but this can have high difficulty just combing for Elders to strike...and if they fail they get Paradox'ed)<br /> <br /> 2. The Syndicate (and before this, High Guild and Invisible Exchequer) are very vulnerable to Cainites paying their employees a visit with Dominate and Presence. It's hard to pull this Entropy Effect when your personnel is hit by Mesmerize, The Forgetful Mind, or Conditioned. Or, worse of all, Possession (and if the Cainite gets good rolls, he can keep using social disciplines while Possessing)<br /> The employees can be Summoned to pay a visit to the vampire, and Blood Bound. A hit squad can be disarmed by Majesty.<br /> There is only so much resistance a Mind Shield (including those that Syndicate members can, I assume, give to their agents) can give when you factor the dice pools Cainites can have.<br /> <br /> Presence can perhaps be used to ask those present to take off those mirrorshades.<br /> <br /> If the vampire sees that you are making him bankrupt, this is pretty good evidence for him that you also know who he is. So a personal visit from a worried/angry Cainite is possible.<br /> <br /> 3. Technocracy seems to focus on battle for the Consensus and the Time Table. From such point of view, it could be argued that rich Cainites are no different than other corrupt or immoral people. (Just like parts of the Syndicate, it could be argued.) Note that Syndicate has no problem working with and within organized crime, as well. Pentex - the Fomori, at least - was deemed acceptable, too.<br /> Original Syndicate Convention Book has John Eaton Simcoe - an Arete 7 Syndic - being on good terms with Vampire Prince Siegfried. Their girlfriends hang out, too! :-) &quot;<i>The women's friendship has nurtured a similar relationship between their men, a bond that has grown into genuine affection. Although Sandra is aware of Julie's &quot;eccentricities&quot;, the vampires have kept their true nature a secret.</i>&quot; ;...;<br /> <br /> 4. Even if you find an old vampire and start trying to make him bankrupt, the spell can still fail, and you lose the funds and manpower you probably invested in this. Also, you can get hit by some Paradox. Who knows if a vampire with Intelligence 7 won't manipulate the circumstances so that your Magick will actually end up being Vulgar?<br /> The vampire can also find out who you are, either with deductions, contacts (the Traditions might even drop some information), Disciplines or torturing your agents.<br /> Also, maybe the whole thing was him testing you if you are worthy to be part of Clan Ventrue (or Clan Lasombra) ?<br /> <br /> 5. Vampires can call in boons. Also, other vampires can come in and help your target, in return for him owing them a boon. Their sire, coterie or Clan can help them. The Primogen Council of a city could be informed, as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's not far-fetched that a vampire can present herself as simply a long-lived person with a certain dietary condition. It's not like Technocracy can confirm that somebody is really a Cainite of 500+ years old. (Unless they get their hands on them or their blood, I guess) Might even be able to pass for a heavily Paradox'ed Mage or a Sorcerer living under a curse, perhaps?<br /> <br /> <br /> I just thought that the possible reason that the policy is to leave Camarilla alone is maybe because someone on the Syndicate Board thought they could win a staredown with an Elder. And maybe they could, Arete 6+ is certainly impressive...but then a Methuselah arrived.<br /> It's certainly sensible and appropriate for a Syndicate member to become a ghoul - doing so unties you from relying on those Progenitors, and what's more fitting for a Syndic than Potence? :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:36:57-07:00","id":968483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968375#post968375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, you have to actually ANSWER my questions, instead of endlessly eluding and teasing and make baseless speculations and spouting nonsenses. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually answered your questions, (or called BS on your BS), multiple times, including the whole second paragraph you just quoted above. You may not like the answer, or perhaps didn't read it.<br /> The fact of the matter is, that Mages and the Technocracy do not actually know a great deal about vampires, nor do they have a great deal of resources like nukes that the vampires do not also have, or more likely, are not actually more under the vampires control than they are the Mage's. They may think that they do, but that just means that it will be a weakness of overconfidence when it hits the fan.<br /> <br /> Your whole plan is based upon vampires being stupid. They are not. So even if the Mages get the jump on the Cainites, (which is one of the ST fiat things), all that means is that there is going to be a lot of casualties right up front, (and most likely they are going to be the younger and weaker Cainites), while the more experienced, more powerful, and luckier ones start figuring out what just happened. And they will. Unlike Mages, the Cainites don't have to actually fully understand how what's happening actually works.<br /> <br /> We have also already seen the Technocracy pull out all of the stops fighting 1 single Vampire (who was also fighting an entire pack of Werewolves, some of the strongest KotE, Wraiths, and other Mages, and in a weakened states), basically discover that their big plan almost failed. Not on it's own, but even with all of the other stuff going on at the same time. The Mages knew it was a strong vampire, but that's about it, because they don't own the Technical Manual Vampire the Masquerade Mage's Edition.<br /> <br /> So, the Technocracy's big Hail Mary plan turned out to be a bust. 100%. It failed. And that was against just one Vampire. It happened to be an Antediluvian, but they don't know that, and they would be stupid as hell, (on par with what you seem to think all Vampires are) to continue to rely on that.<br /> <br /> You also seem to think the Vampires actually need to know where the Mages are hiding. They don't, plain and simple. There are multiple higher level Disciplines that can affect targets without knowing where or who they are, and Mage's are going to have a particularly hard problem with that because Disciplines level 6+, by the Book, Mages do not have any particular defense against. Their Spheres only work to counter one for one. Vampires also have access to abilities that Mages are probably not going to know about, like the ability to become Astral, or read objects. It wouldn't take much for a survivor of a nuke to pick up a piece of metal, take a supernatural look at it, say &quot;Hmm&quot;, take a little invisible trip to the Space Station/Satellite it came from, send a message back to earth telepathically right then and there, and another vampire used mass manipulation to Dominate the president and every single Project Twilight member in the room (who autofail, even with &quot;Magick&quot;) to blast them and every satellite to dust.<br /> <br /> All in all though, this is stupid. For every &quot;But the _______ can do this&quot; there is going to be a &quot;But the _______ can counter it by, or are immune to, etc. . .&quot;<br /> <br /> Far, far too much of Mage also depends on the ST allowing it to work, which doesn't work in a Setting vs Setting battle royal, not unless there ST is partial. And if the ST is partial, than whatever side wins because the ST gave them that advantage. Nothing more.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:40:43-07:00","id":968485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968457#post968457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manus, I don't want to obtrude this flame war I had ignited - I just want to ask why the Syndicate has not already bankrupted every single Vampire through Entropic Effects, Enlightened management and hypereconomics manipulations. I have always wondered why the Syndicate, the most competitive and ruthless of the Conventions(though not necessarily <i>greedy</i>), has left their immortal (potential) financial rivals and (also potential) business competitors largely intact so long like ancient, festering tumor, especially in the Mage-centric setting. What is your thought regarding the reason? Do you have any theory or conjecture?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that depends on whether you play Mage or Vampire.<br /> <br /> In the Technocracy game that I've ran since like 2000, it almost has.<br /> <br /> Because when you play Mage, Mages get to use their Spheres like they damn well want, without the restrictions of Blood Treachery.<br /> <br /> While, if I were to suddenly stop not caring about Vampire or Werewolf, the Technocracy would not be anything more than a bunch of jumped up mortals who stole the powers of Blood/Gaia, to bend reality to their whims who'll go down to any proper vampire/werewolf.<br /> <br /> But in canon?<br /> <br /> Because vampire is more popular.<br /> <br /> No other reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:47:25-07:00","id":968488,"title":"","content":"I think they operate at different levels. The Syndicate doesn't care (much) about a huge Swiss bank account that's never accessed, or a basement full of Nazi gold. It's dead, just like the vampire that controls it. The Syndicate cares about money as an object of universal desire, and the transactions being performed with it. Every time someone exchanges something valuable for money, they cement the power that the Syndicate has. So why would you want a basement full of gold not being transacted? It's like a beautiful cathedral in which no one goes to worship. You want a respectable GDP growth rate; you want high consumer confidence; you want low inflation and a sale at Wal-Mart. You don't need to have all the money and all the businesses; you need to people to want money more than anything else, and for money to buy the stable existence they crave.<br /> <br /> Vampires want money as another way for them to exert control. The Syndicate wants money itself to be able to exert control. The two goals don't conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 09-13-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:53:33-07:00","id":968490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968483#post968483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Technocracy's big Hail Mary plan turned out to be a bust. 100%. It failed. And that was against just one Vampire. It happened to be an Antediluvian, but they don't know that, and they would be stupid as hell, (on par with what you seem to think all Vampires are) to continue to rely on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care much for this, but I'll point out that it didn't fail.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's mirrors turned him to ash in a few seconds and the only thing that stopped it were the Kuei-Jin holding the storm running.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's neutron bombs murdered everything that wasn't the Antediluvian and hurt it severely, after which the Kuei-Jin stopped the storm and the mirror turned him to ash in seconds. <br /> <br /> Here, have a link: <a href=\"http://imgur.com/gallery/M4f2Lhh\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/gallery/M4f2Lhh</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:55:29-07:00","id":968494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968488#post968488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they operate at different levels. The Syndicate doesn't care (much) about a huge Swiss bank account that's never accessed, or a basement full of Nazi gold. It's dead, just like the vampire that controls it. The Syndicate cares about money as an object of universal desire, and the transactions being performed with it. Every time someone exchanges something valuable for money, they cement the power that the Syndicate has. So why would you want a basement full of gold not being transacted? It's like a beautiful cathedral in which no one goes to worship. You want a respectable GDP growth rate; you want high consumer confidence; you want low inflation and a sale at Wal-Mart. You don't need to have all the money and all the businesses; you need to people to want money more than anything else, and for money to buy the stable existence they crave.<br /> <br /> Vampires want money as another way for them to exert control. The Syndicate wants money itself to be able to exert control. The two goals don't conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, this. The Syndicate guides the world economy, it wants to bind the world together with ties of golden currency.<br /> <br /> A vampire is just another customer, and the Syndicate never says no to customers.<br /> <br /> Except for Nephandi, they call HITMarks on those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:17:10-07:00","id":968505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968494#post968494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for Nephandi, they call HITMarks on those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the HIT Marks be called off if the Nephandi pay extra? :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:23:41-07:00","id":968506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968490#post968490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't care much for this, but I'll point out that it didn't fail.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's mirrors turned him to ash in a few seconds and the only thing that stopped it were the Kuei-Jin holding the storm running.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's neutron bombs murdered everything that wasn't the Antediluvian and hurt it severely, after which the Kuei-Jin stopped the storm and the mirror turned him to ash in seconds.<br /> <br /> Here, have a link: <a href=\"http://imgur.com/gallery/M4f2Lhh\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/gallery/M4f2Lhh</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It did fail in the sense that the Technocracy's great plan only barely succeeded, and only because there where so many other factors involved that helped out. On it's own, it's unclear. What is clear is that the Technocracy did absolutely everything they where capable of, (and where caught completely by surprise), and only barely pulled it off against one threat, (that was weakened and disorientated, and also had an alternative agenda in cursing it's own rather than focusing fully on fighting back). It also clearly survived the multiple nukes they threw at it at ground zero.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy only knows that it is a &quot;force 8 to 10&quot;, but can't seem to get any details despite having forces &quot;on the ground and in the air&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not terribly clear just what the bombs did, possibly nothing to possibly hurting is severely. But, it survived more than one of them.<br /> <br /> However, the entire point I'm making here is that we can see, as factual information, taken directly from the Technocracy's point of view, that they had no idea what they where fighting, no clue that it existed prior, and no idea how many others there could be. All of the information that they thought they had was faulty. They don't know that there are only 13 of these creatures, (if that's even true). They also don't know how many others that are slightly weaker around, which could very much be a hell of a lot more than 13. They just know that their big plan was not nearly as effective as they had believed it would be, and the had already pulled out all of the stops to make that one happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:54:08-07:00","id":968517,"title":"","content":"The funny thing is, in a Mages vs Vampires game, I'd actually say that the Mages might have the most trouble with the Gangrel over everyone else. They will be hardest to track, effectively vanishing from even magical eyes each time they Earthmeld, (and being immune to even Astral attacks). They have the supernatural toughness that they can ignore/mitigate a lot of the physical attacks (as a whole), have the ability to form a spy network through animals that Mages are much less likely to try to protect or defend against, tend to communicate in ways that the Technocracy might think is too old fashioned to consider, and unlike many other vampires, do actually communicate with each other fairly regularly, do have the potential to actually make it into outer space on their own, might easily be misidentified as a Garou, (meaning a lot of their Magik will not work, focusing incorrectly on a living target rather than an Undead one), and capable of sending Mages into a berserker state at a distance.<br /> <br /> It's a bit far fetched, but just imagine a horde of Gangrel flying through space as bats with sonar and nightvision, turning to mist or earthmelding with meteors when the sun is a little too much, tracking down satellites and space stations to unleash bestial unholy hell. I find that idea funny as heck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:17:10-07:00","id":968530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968517#post968517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit far fetched, but just imagine a horde of Gangrel flying through space as bats with sonar and nightvision, turning to mist or earthmelding with meteors when the sun is a little too much, tracking down satellites and space stations to unleash bestial unholy hell. I find that idea funny as heck.</div> </div> </div> </div>NANANANANANANANANANANA! SPAAAACE GANGREL!<br /> <br /> The thread is done now, and you have won it good sir.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:19:48-07:00","id":968532,"title":"","content":"Hey, its no less ridiculous (and actually in accordance with RAW) that most of the other stuff. Granted, there is no resistance in space, so wings do jack squat for locomotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:38:39-07:00","id":968543,"title":"","content":"But mist form allows for movement by will, so they can start moving as mist, transform into the bat form, (just for sonar and keen senses) and go from there. They have time. :P<br /> (well 10-20ish 24hour periods)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:13:28-07:00","id":968560,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11780\" data-vbnamecard=\"11780\">Posthumanity</a> <br /> <br /> I'd like to run it as a cost / benefits thing. Right now the cost for a focused campaign from the syndicate would be too negligent towards their other projects. Basically it would be a pyrrhic victory. Now if a lone wolf wants to go off the schedule and hardcore, or if a target of opportunity presents itself, they'll take it. You just run them as vamps with different powers.<br /> <br /> And remember the syndicate is one of the more lax of the conventions. From their view point they've already won the ascension war. The Short end of it is: the world is run by money, and the people tht want something have to earn it. Hell they give the tradition mages the golf clap for awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:38:51-07:00","id":968573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968532#post968532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, its no less ridiculous (and actually in accordance with RAW) that most of the other stuff. Granted, there is no resistance in space, so wings do jack squat for locomotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the blood is malleable to a degree, and Gangrel are hella prone to creating new Bloodlines, so clearly you just end up with those couple Gangrel who went buddy-buddy with the Gargoyles developing a new bloodline of Space Gangrel. They have Fortitude, Protean, and Flight as their affinity Disciplines, because Animalism isn't very useful against the horrors of the Deep Umbra, and Flight lets them move around via <i>vampire magic</i> rather than requiring physical means of generating thrust.<br /> <br /> They retain Fortitude to defend against the dangers of sunlit hard vacuum that their unliving flesh doesn't, and spend most of their time in torpor, melded with very small asteroids held in orbit with each other, until some of the squamous monstrosities of the Deep Universe happen upon them. At that point, they revive and attack in packs like wolves hunting a mammoth. Or like humans hunting a mammoth.<br /> <br /> Thus did vampires survive the near-annihilation of their race and humanity both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:15:23-07:00","id":968592,"title":"","content":"&quot;He is Space Gangrel, a <i>magical vampire that flies around in space by willing himself to move, sucking the lifeblood from aliens</i>, she is (Wo)man in Black Space Marine, a scientist that battles aliens and Elder Gods by engaging in philosophical knife fights with wizards.<br /> <br /> Together, they fight crime&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd play it, hell <i>I'd storytell it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:03:57-07:00","id":968691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968592#post968592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;He is Space Gangrel, a <i>magical vampire that flies around in space by willing himself to move, sucking the lifeblood from aliens</i>, she is (Wo)man in Black Space Marine, a scientist that battles aliens and Elder Gods by engaging in philosophical knife fights with wizards.<br /> <br /> Together, they fight crime&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd play it, hell <i>I'd storytell it.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://starreviews.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/vampire20vixens20from20venus201995.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Technocratic view point &quot;Oh and Vampirism? thats just midichlorians in your blood stream&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:25:52-07:00","id":968818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968517#post968517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit far fetched, but just imagine a horde of Gangrel flying through space as bats with sonar and nightvision, turning to mist or earthmelding with meteors when the sun is a little too much, tracking down satellites and space stations to unleash bestial unholy hell. I find that idea funny as heck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact that's not how space works. It's big. It's empty. And it's all in sunlight except for that very very very tiny smidge over there that is behind Earth. Oh, and getting into an orbit that will keep them from having sunlight come over the terminator is very very tricky especially in form of mist. And, like the rest of space, also very very empty.<br /> <br /> Gangrel in space are basically just very thin clouds of ash or, effectively, the equivalent of the critters you find under a rock, with rock being Earth, and the Void Engineers having an area to mess around with that is substantially larger (by orders of magnitude) than that rock is to the entire planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:32:47-07:00","id":968893,"title":"","content":"That part was mostly a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:42:28-07:00","id":968967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968506#post968506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It did fail in the sense that the Technocracy's great plan only barely succeeded, and only because there where so many other factors involved that helped out. On it's own, it's unclear. What is clear is that the Technocracy did absolutely everything they where capable of, (and where caught completely by surprise), and only barely pulled it off against one threat, (that was weakened and disorientated, and also had an alternative agenda in cursing it's own rather than focusing fully on fighting back). It also clearly survived the multiple nukes they threw at it at ground zero.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy only knows that it is a &quot;force 8 to 10&quot;, but can't seem to get any details despite having forces &quot;on the ground and in the air&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not terribly clear just what the bombs did, possibly nothing to possibly hurting is severely. But, it survived more than one of them.<br /> <br /> However, the entire point I'm making here is that we can see, as factual information, taken directly from the Technocracy's point of view, that they had no idea what they where fighting, no clue that it existed prior, and no idea how many others there could be. All of the information that they thought they had was faulty. They don't know that there are only 13 of these creatures, (if that's even true). They also don't know how many others that are slightly weaker around, which could very much be a hell of a lot more than 13. They just know that their big plan was not nearly as effective as they had believed it would be, and the had already pulled out all of the stops to make that one happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, it is an enigma why the Technocracy didn't teleport it into very core of the sun via quantum gateway, or bombard the whole area into oblivion through orbital weapon array, or swarm it with assortment of specialized army, instead of relying on mirrors. Simple and easy solution was at hand, and Technocracy unwisely choose the long, hard way, primarily due to plot devise, I suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-13-2016, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:12:02-07:00","id":968987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968967#post968967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Frankly, it is an enigma why the Technocracy didn't teleport it into very core of the sun via quantum gateway,</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't have that setup ready?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968967#post968967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or bombard the whole area into oblivion through orbital weapon array, or swarm it with assortment of specialized army,</div> </div> </div> </div>They did, and they did. Both failed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968967#post968967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Simple and easy solution was at hand, and Technocracy unwisely choose the long, hard way, primarily due to plot devise, I suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple and easy didn't work. I do completely agree it's plot device though. Their final solution shouldn't have worked either, given the mastery of Chimestry. But hey, Mage players got the feather in their collective cap that Mages were responsible for killing an Antediluvian.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:43:58-07:00","id":969193,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that Antediluvians+ are supposed to have powers and abilities that function similar to Awakened Magick, and themselves are intentionally beyond the rules. It's suggested that they have the ability to alter the way that the universe works, unintentionally direct the way people behave/believe/act, and alter aspects of reality simply by existing. Seemingly Caine laid down massive curses on at least 12 entire bloodlines on an angry whim, and there are plenty of cases where it is suggested that one Cainite or another made one place cursed or corrupted or another sacred, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968987#post968987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't have that setup ready?</div> </div> </div> </div>We only have, OOC, some information on what happened, and because the story kind of comes from multiple splat's points of view, we can infer some things, but it's not really &quot;factual&quot;. It seems that the Technocracy was caught completely by surprise by Ravnos waking up. This is and is not a little surprising, as Ravnos is typically seen as one of the weaker Anti's in the more physical sense. We don't know that, but generally speaking both he and his Clan have a reputation for being sneaky, deceptive, cowardly (in physical combat), and tricksters. So it makes perfect sense that he would be well hidden, but it's also a little odd that he chose to battle anyone at all, or even let himself be seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968987#post968987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple and easy didn't work. I do completely agree it's plot device though. Their final solution shouldn't have worked either, given the mastery of Chimestry. But hey, Mage players got the feather in their collective cap that Mages were responsible for killing an Antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two sides to this. Cainites of his age are generally known to have very low Path ratings, and we are clearly told that the important segments of the battle take place during the day. Even if we assume that he has a Path Rating of 10, which is highly unlikely, but technically possible, he should have been capped at an absolute max of 10 Dice, and likewise 10 Dots in anything and everything. So, even if, for instance, he had 10 Str, 10 Potence, and Blood Buffed another 10 dots in Strength, he should have been limited to only a Str of 10.<br /> <br /> It's possible that as a 3rd Gen Cainite that's been alive since nearly the dawn of humanity, he might be beyond that limit, but by the rules, he should have been limited to his Path Rating on any rolls, also constantly making rolls to stay awake, and at a penalty. There is also the problem that he should have been very low of Blood, and also suffering from a general weakness/disorientation from just recently waking up from a long Torpor. That isn't really a mechanical rule as much as a &quot;flavor&quot; restriction.<br /> <br /> Another aspect to also consider is that the Technocracy was essentially fighting blind, and there where more than one threat in the immediate area, (it quotes something like multiple factor 8-10 beings), and all of them are different, (there are Mages, Werewolves, Spirits, Wraiths, a Vampire, KotE, if not more), and while their primary target was Ravnos, that would require a lot of Mastery of a lot of Spheres to be able to pick him out and target (affect) him. Hell, probably a mastery of all, in all honesty, but the Technocracy and Mages in general as still going to run into the issue where Cainite's powers such as Disciplines and Mage's magics such as Spheres only oppose each other if they are at an equal level, failing otherwise. That is, if you have a Vampire with Dominate 6 and a Mage with Mind 5, the Mage automatically fails to counter Dominate 6, because Dominate 6 is at a higher level. If it's Dominate 5 (or lower) and Mind 5, then the &quot;defender&quot; has a chance, but it is not automatic, (and vice versa). However, when we are talking about something Level 6+ vs something capped at 5, Mages really shouldn't have had a chance at a lot of stuff. Not everything, but a lot.<br /> <br /> One last thing to keep in mind is that the entire scenario, while it was Story Fiat, it was also there to purposefully give essentially every splat a massive wake up slap across the face, that no matter how much planning they had done, (like the section where Vitel is speaking to many of the Camarilla's higher leadership when his character has secretly been hoarding the worlds nukes as a plan to survive the Antediluvians from waking up), basically sees his secret plan not work. The KotE get destroyed, the Garou don't even make it to the true battle and die almost pointlessly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 09-14-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:55:22-07:00","id":969230,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Posthumanity;n968967]<br /> Frankly, it is an enigma why the Technocracy didn't teleport it into very core of the sun via quantum gateway[QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Because Chimestry 10 is an hell of plot device (not that the other Discipline level 10 are not an hell of a plot device, but Chemistry is really versatile).<br /> He could have used it to create around him a reality were quantum physics do not work at all, or he could have used chimestry 10 to froze the sun or to create a vast region were magic does not exist at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beside that there is the big technocracy limit: they need the right focus, they can't simply create an effect on the fly, the need a focus to do it, so they would have needed to place a quantum generator somewhere, and so on.<br /> I remember that in the week of nightmare they tried to place some pretty complex high-teck to an unknown goal (I think they were some kind of targeting beacons to make the Sun-mirrors works, but I'm not sure)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , or bombard the whole area into oblivion through orbital weapon array, </div> </div> </div>They did it, they bombarded the are with 4 nuclear bombs,and he simply survived them, even while he was distracted by 3 arhat, a legion of wraiths and packs of werewolves.<br /> <br /> (He soaked something like 40 levels of agg, 40 dices of agg, 40 dices of bashing, and 64 dices of agg from the radiations)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or swarm it with assortment of specialized army, instead of relying on mirrors. </div> </div> </div>They did it too, it is stated in the first paragraph were Schiavelli appears: in the first two days of fight Technocracy deployed armed squads with plasma weapons, no one survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-14-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:08:23-07:00","id":969235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=969193#post969193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are two sides to this. Cainites of his age are generally known to have very low Path ratings, and we are clearly told that the important segments of the battle take place during the day. Even if we assume that he has a Path Rating of 10, which is highly unlikely, but technically possible, he should have been capped at an absolute max of 10 Dice, and likewise 10 Dots in anything and everything. So, even if, for instance, he had 10 Str, 10 Potence, and Blood Buffed another 10 dots in Strength, he should have been limited to only a Str of 10.<br /> <br /> It's possible that as a 3rd Gen Cainite that's been alive since nearly the dawn of humanity, he might be beyond that limit, but by the rules, he should have been limited to his Path Rating on any rolls, also constantly making rolls to stay awake, and at a penalty. There is also the problem that he should have been very low of Blood, and also suffering from a general weakness/disorientation from just recently waking up from a long Torpor. That isn't really a mechanical rule as much as a &quot;flavor&quot; restriction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>(even more by game rules Ravnos was fighting with a +2 difficulty to all attack and defense rolls while fighting against the Bodhisattvas/Arhat, and after the wraiths came in a +4 is more likely)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Multiple Opponents: A character who battles<br /> multiple opponents in close combat suffers attack and<br /> defense difficulties of +1, cumulative, for each opponent<br /> after the first (to a maximum of +4). </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-14-2016, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:20:13-07:00","id":969265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968893#post968893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That part was mostly a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue of vamps in space did come up in one of my games. It was a very odd spin-off Vampire mini-chronicle of a long-running Mage game. In the Mage game, the characters had had several brushes with a probable apocalyptic future where humanity abandoned Earth. A Nosferatu PC found out about it and the character became dedicated to figuring out how to get his Clan mates hidden in the exodus. Effectively envisioning Obfuscated Nosferatu lurking through the hidden back corridors of hollowed out asteroid habitats, crawlways on spaceships and stations and the like. (It's entirely possible that Earth was under the rule of the Antediluvians. Or the Nephandi. Or the Maeljin Incarna and their Banes. Or, Hells, bane mummies. All anyone in the future would say/knew was that Earth had been &quot;lost&quot;. I tacitly assumed it was something akin to parts of all of the above.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:01:03-07:00","id":969357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968483#post968483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually answered your questions, (or called BS on your BS), multiple times, including the whole second paragraph you just quoted above. You may not like the answer, or perhaps didn't read it.<br /> The fact of the matter is, that Mages and the Technocracy do not actually know a great deal about vampires, nor do they have a great deal of resources like nukes that the vampires do not also have, or more likely, are not actually more under the vampires control than they are the Mage's. They may think that they do, but that just means that it will be a weakness of overconfidence when it hits the fan.<br /> <br /> Your whole plan is based upon vampires being stupid. They are not. So even if the Mages get the jump on the Cainites, (which is one of the ST fiat things), all that means is that there is going to be a lot of casualties right up front, (and most likely they are going to be the younger and weaker Cainites), while the more experienced, more powerful, and luckier ones start figuring out what just happened. And they will. Unlike Mages, the Cainites don't have to actually fully understand how what's happening actually works.<br /> <br /> We have also already seen the Technocracy pull out all of the stops fighting 1 single Vampire (who was also fighting an entire pack of Werewolves, some of the strongest KotE, Wraiths, and other Mages, and in a weakened states), basically discover that their big plan almost failed. Not on it's own, but even with all of the other stuff going on at the same time. The Mages knew it was a strong vampire, but that's about it, because they don't own the Technical Manual Vampire the Masquerade Mage's Edition.<br /> <br /> So, the Technocracy's big Hail Mary plan turned out to be a bust. 100%. It failed. And that was against just one Vampire. It happened to be an Antediluvian, but they don't know that, and they would be stupid as hell, (on par with what you seem to think all Vampires are) to continue to rely on that.<br /> <br /> You also seem to think the Vampires actually need to know where the Mages are hiding. They don't, plain and simple. There are multiple higher level Disciplines that can affect targets without knowing where or who they are, and Mage's are going to have a particularly hard problem with that because Disciplines level 6+, by the Book, Mages do not have any particular defense against. Their Spheres only work to counter one for one. Vampires also have access to abilities that Mages are probably not going to know about, like the ability to become Astral, or read objects. It wouldn't take much for a survivor of a nuke to pick up a piece of metal, take a supernatural look at it, say &quot;Hmm&quot;, take a little invisible trip to the Space Station/Satellite it came from, send a message back to earth telepathically right then and there, and another vampire used mass manipulation to Dominate the president and every single Project Twilight member in the room (who autofail, even with &quot;Magick&quot;) to blast them and every satellite to dust.<br /> <br /> All in all though, this is stupid. For every &quot;But the _______ can do this&quot; there is going to be a &quot;But the _______ can counter it by, or are immune to, etc. . .&quot;<br /> <br /> Far, far too much of Mage also depends on the ST allowing it to work, which doesn't work in a Setting vs Setting battle royal, not unless there ST is partial. And if the ST is partial, than whatever side wins because the ST gave them that advantage. Nothing more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your entire argument is based on assumption that Mages are hapless like morons against 6+ Disciplines. And that is why we always substitute 6+ Disciplines with equivalent Spheres or allow the Mages counter it anyway. For instance, Eldar Vampire with Dominate 6+ has Mind 3, by the Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:15:21-07:00","id":969367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=969357#post969357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, Eldar Vampire with Dominate 6+ has Mind 3, by the Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page reference?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:24:00-07:00","id":969375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=969367#post969367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage the Ascension, First Edition, Page 279.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:29:48-07:00","id":969380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=969375#post969375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage the Ascension, First Edition, Page 279.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument against is based on the crossover rules from 2nd edition and Revised (and possibly the 20th anniversary books). While I don't agree with those rules (and don't use them) they do specifically say to compare power levels on a 1 for 1 basis. Quoting 1st edition for rules probably won't help much to for forum discussions. Especially since those rules were specifically updated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:43:34-07:00","id":969390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=969357#post969357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eldar Vampire with Dominate 6+ has Mind 3, by the Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was so only in the first edition, later it was changed, Master of Arts (1999) says it's level on level, so to counter Dominate 6 you'd need Mind 6.<br /> Storyteller's handbook (revised) (2002) confirms this in with the quick cross-over rule, otherwise the other possible system is the contested roll system introduced in the same handbook and later modified by M20.<br /> <br /> Besides, about Mage 1Ed, M20 is pretty clear:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage 1st\u2019s magick rules are broken. Please ignore them. Thanks.) </div> </div> </div><br /> V20/M20/W20 have slightly more balanced rules, with the contested rolls.<br /> But it's still much easier for vampires to win,thanks to their higher dicepools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-14-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:54:20-07:00","id":969435,"title":"","content":"Mind Shield is a level one effect<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/weirdalfoil_2322.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There is also a nice sidebar in M20 page546 that might help in cluster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:41:36-07:00","id":969763,"title":"","content":"While I am generally something of a Mage supremacist, and especially a Technocracy supremacist (One World! One Union! One Reality! Ipsa Scientia Potestas Est!). Then I'll agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a> here. The Week of Nightmares was as difficult for the Technocracy as it should be, the fact that they <i>did </i>manage to kill it without any drawbacks to themselves like say the deaths of Lasombra and Tremere is an impressive feat in itself. Generally, as an answer to &quot;why didn't the Technocracy just do X against Ravnos?&quot; I just assumed that they <i>tried and found it didn't work</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:57:12-07:00","id":971437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=968160#post968160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'll have to step in here, and in a surprising twist of events against the Union.<br /> <br /> I have no boat in this race anymore, but I am however a huge Union fan.<br /> <br /> But calling the Union, unambiguously good is doing it a disservice.<br /> <br /> The sins of the Union are the sins of the west, it is a patriarchal, explotative organization, and the entire point of many Union games are whether you can tolerate what the Union has become or whether you want to attempt to restore it to it's glory days as the Order of Reason, when nobility and Reason wasn't buried beneath layers of &quot;to break an omelet&quot; and &quot;for the good of the Union&quot; propaganda. Like, this is some of the first things that Guide to The Technocracy tells you, if you refuse that the Union is just as morally ambiguous as it's enemies, you refuse the central point of what Mage is about.<br /> <br /> The Union is not fascist however, it truly wants to elevate all of humanity to the ranks of the Enlightened, but the problem is that you have a core of Enlightened people who have reached Enlightenment 6 and can thus see that when you use a plasma cannon, all that you're really doing is that you're saying Forces 3/Primium 2 in a different way. And these people, realizing that they are the one-eyed men in a world of the blind, believe that there must be an Enlightened elite to shepherd the masses, guiding them through the terrors of the night, without realizing that they have become <i>exactly </i>like the ancient old tyrant-wizards that they rallied their fellow men to arms against during the Sorcerer's Crusade.<br /> <br /> Neither is the Technocracy un-democratic. It believes in democracy because the Union represents the sins of the patriarchial west, enforcing it's &quot;One True Way&quot; one everyone else, it's CIA infiltrating other countries and bringing them down so that USA can implement &quot;democracy&quot;, it's the USA backing terrorists to fight a greater enemy, and then being unwilling to fix the problem it created in any way other than it created it in the first place.<br /> <br /> It is not pro-rich, though the Syndicate might tell you differently depending on who you ask. The Void Engineers are Space Marines and Ghostbusters fighting a desperate battle for humanity's survival (and being space conquistadors), the Iterators are transhumanists who want to help humanity to remove it's flaws (whether you want it or not), the Progenitors are biologists and doctors, who want to free humanity from the yoke of death and disease (if you show up on a list of Reality Deviants, you count as disease btw) and the NWO support a strong state that can help it's subjects when they are in need, so they don't ever need to experience sadness or poverty or war (who cares if you have to sacrifice a little freedom to get it?).<br /> <br /> Of these, only the Syndicate is pro-rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hardly say the Union is patriarchal. Nor would I say they are democratic. Remember, the Union has a huge portion of personnel that either WERE Nazi's or were trained by people who were.<br /> <br /> What the Union is, however is aggressively Meritocratic, and very protective of their orthodoxy. Either you step up to the plate for humanity or you shut up and listen to those who do, and you have no right to your own opinion. Because remember, in mage, opinions really can cause harm if enough people hold them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:06:08-07:00","id":971665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964939-all-out-war-technocracy-against-vampire?p=971437#post971437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd hardly say the Union is patriarchal. Nor would I say they are democratic. Remember, the Union has a huge portion of personnel that either WERE Nazi's or were trained by people who were.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point me to where you get backup in the source material for this assertion. Specifically, a &quot;huge portion&quot; of current personnel and/or their mentors. Not just a passing mention of someone who belonged, the places where it says that the NWO has a large Nazi component.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:47:11-07:00","id":971683,"title":"","content":"I actually meant the Iterators. The physical book I've got for them basically has a short-story that says that the way that particular arsenal operates is so 'nazi-like' due to previous membership, that some of the sleepers working in the 'front' require frequent psych evals because it bothers them when it starts to all add up. And there's no real indication this is abnormal for that particular convention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:16:54-07:00","id":973795,"title":"","content":"Why not just use the space sun-mirrors to shine the sunlight on the cities during couple of weeks? Probably someone already had this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}